(window.COSMIC_I18N = window.COSMIC_I18N || {}).en = Object.freeze({"moon":{"aries":"the Moon in Aries","taurus":"the Moon in Taurus","gemini":"the Moon in Gemini","cancer":"the Moon in Cancer","leo":"the Moon in Leo","virgo":"the Moon in Virgo","libra":"the Moon in Libra","scorpio":"the Moon in Scorpio","sagittarius":"the Moon in Sagittarius","capricorn":"the Moon in Capricorn","aquarius":"the Moon in Aquarius","pisces":"the Moon in Pisces"},"sky":{"classic":{"fire":["{moon} inspires momentum and encourages you to choose a clear direction before acting.","{moon} brings a lively energy that works best when focused on a specific goal.","{moon} rekindles the urge to move forwards without waiting for everything to be perfect.","{moon} favours heartfelt initiatives and reminds you of the value of measured enthusiasm.","{moon} highlights what deserves your courage rather than your haste.","{moon} sets an intense pace in the sky, best met with discernment."],"earth":["{moon} invites you to return to simple routines and practical actions.","{moon} favours patience and the pleasure of making progress at your own pace.","{moon} brings your attention back to what is built through consistency.","{moon} encourages calm, stability and care over the details.","{moon} inspires practical choices without sacrificing what makes you feel good.","{moon} reminds you that quiet progress can be remarkably solid."],"air":["{moon} stimulates conversation and sets fresh ideas in motion.","{moon} opens your mind to different opinions and unexpected perspectives.","{moon} encourages curiosity while inviting you to keep a clear thread running through your day.","{moon} gives conversations a special place in the day ahead.","{moon} favours light-heartedness and discoveries sparked by a question.","{moon} invites you to organise your thoughts without stifling your imagination."],"water":["{moon} brings emotions to the surface and invites you to welcome them gently.","{moon} stirs memories that may shed light on the present.","{moon} encourages inner reflection and moments of genuine closeness.","{moon} lends greater depth to impressions and silences.","{moon} nurtures intuition when you give it a little room.","{moon} invites you to care for your connections without forgetting your own needs."]},"funny":{"fire":["{moon} gives you the energy to chase a bus, even when you're already on it.","{moon} turns every queue into an unofficial test of patience.","{moon} suggests starting five projects before the kettle has even boiled.","{moon} lights a mighty inner fire over a decision as serious as choosing a pizza.","{moon} whispers that you should press 'send' before rereading your message.","{moon} hands out courage to everyone except those waiting their turn."],"earth":["{moon} declares that a cosy blanket and a packed diary can coexist.","{moon} turns a shopping list into a document of vital strategic importance.","{moon} reminds you that ambition doesn't require leaving your favourite armchair.","{moon} elevates tidying a drawer to a major personal triumph.","{moon} advises a calm approach, especially if anyone threatens to move the sofa.","{moon} makes an afternoon snack an officially top-priority appointment."],"air":["{moon} opens twelve conversations and forgets how the first one started.","{moon} conjures three brilliant ideas between two utterly pointless notifications.","{moon} prompts you to tell a story that eventually requires a map and a diagram.","{moon} distributes opinions faster than a group chat can keep up.","{moon} turns a simple 'hello' into a debate about the meaning of life.","{moon} helps you find the words, followed by far too many more words."],"water":["{moon} adds a dramatic soundtrack to the simple act of sorting an old box.","{moon} makes you nostalgic for a childhood Sunday whose date you can't even remember.","{moon} turns a blurry photograph into a treasured exhibit in your personal museum.","{moon} makes finding a forgotten mug in the cupboard unexpectedly moving.","{moon} prompts you to ask a slightly drooping plant whether it's all right.","{moon} finds hidden emotional depths in a message that only said 'OK'."]},"piquant":{"fire":["{moon} convinces you that urgency is a personality trait, not an organisational problem.","{moon} sparks an imaginary competition with someone who merely wanted to walk past.","{moon} urges you to charge ahead before you've even learnt the address.","{moon} installs an invisible stopwatch in every peaceful conversation.","{moon} mistakes your impatience for a gift the whole world should admire.","{moon} grants you permission to declare victory before anyone else understands the rules."],"earth":["{moon} turns your comfort zone into a heavily guarded territory.","{moon} confirms that changing a cushion requires a public consultation.","{moon} places a cosmic veto on anything that disrupts your habits.","{moon} reminds you that seeking something solid can eventually lead to marrying your favourite piece of furniture.","{moon} elevates your usual routine to an unamendable constitution.","{moon} makes you treat spontaneity as an incident that must be reported."],"air":["{moon} gives you a thousand ideas and leaves someone else to finish one.","{moon} opens a debate, then another debate about whether that debate was necessary.","{moon} encourages your opinions to change faster than your phone screen.","{moon} multiplies the options until actually arriving becomes entirely optional.","{moon} gives you the final word, plus fourteen entirely unnecessary final words.","{moon} puts your thoughts in a permanent meeting without appointing anyone to lead it."],"water":["{moon} turns an ordinary silence into a four-page emotional case file.","{moon} puts a memory everyone else had filed away back on the agenda.","{moon} helps you interpret a full stop as a historical event.","{moon} adds nostalgia even to an old biscuit wrapper.","{moon} organises an emergency committee around a sigh heard from afar.","{moon} makes you sense the mood of a room before entering, then write an entire novel about it."]}},"mercury":{"classic":["Mercury retrograde invites you to reread your messages before sending them. A little clarification may prevent a misunderstanding.","An old conversation might resurface under Mercury retrograde. Take time to understand its context.","Mercury retrograde suggests checking the details instead of assuming everyone understood the same thing."],"funny":["Mercury retrograde recommends reading it again. Perhaps your message is mysterious simply because a word is missing.","An old topic resurfacing? Mercury retrograde has apparently found the drawer of unfinished conversations.","Mercury retrograde puts communication to the test. Before blaming the cosmos, check who you're sending that message to."],"piquant":["Mercury retrograde is not a cosmic licence to send an ambiguous message and promptly disappear.","The past sometimes returns with Mercury retrograde. You don't have to open every file it brings.","Mercury retrograde suggests rereading your words. The other person shouldn't have to guess the subtitles to your thoughts."]},"signs":{"aries":{"classic":{"career":["Your instinct for taking the initiative could open up an interesting opportunity at work. Take time to define your goal before involving others.","When a project is slow to get going, your energy comes into its own. Distinguish what you can do yourself from what needs a team decision.","A professional challenge sparks your drive to succeed. You can gain influence by giving other people's ideas room to be heard.","Competition awakens your determination. Use it to fuel progress rather than constantly measure your own worth.","Faced with vague instructions, your instinct is to act immediately. A few focused questions could save you unnecessary detours.","Your desire for quick results deserves a flexible framework. Break big ambitions into visible steps and appreciate each one.","If a meeting drags on, your frankness can help move things forwards. Choose the right moment to speak.","Taking the lead comes naturally to you. Remember to share your methods so the team moves with you, not behind you."],"love":["Your spontaneity brings vitality to relationships. Allow the other person the freedom to find their own pace.","When you care about someone, you show it openly. Attentive listening can give your affection just as much strength.","A hasty remark may go further than you intended. Take time to rephrase it before a disagreement becomes a contest.","Your desire to live life intensely drives your feelings. Quiet moments can also nurture a beautiful connection.","Faced with a difference of opinion, your honesty is valuable when it remains open to nuance. Seek to understand before persuading.","Your need for independence is part of your balance. Express it clearly rather than assuming the other person knows what you expect.","By always making the first move, you risk carrying all the initiative yourself. Leave room for the other person's surprises.","Knowing when to admit a mistake takes nothing away from your strength. A simple gesture can soothe more than a long argument."],"wellbeing":["Your intense energy deserves time to recover. Give yourself a proper break between bursts of activity.","When impatience rises, a walk without a particular destination can help you slow down.","A day full of challenges may tempt you to ignore ordinary tiredness. Respect your need for rest rather than treating it as an obstacle.","Your love of action follows you everywhere. Set aside a moment when nothing needs to be achieved.","When something goes wrong, breathe before charging forwards again. That brief pause may be enough to regain your calm.","Your habit of rushing can even creep into mealtimes. Give yourself a peaceful moment to savour something you enjoy.","Learning to wait does not mean giving up on progress. Try an activity that values rhythm over results.","If sleep keeps coming second to your projects, give it a place in your daily routine again."],"wisdom":["Your courage grows when it knows which battles to choose.","The strength of an impulse also lies in the direction you give it.","One considered step may take you further than a hurried dash.","Maturity means knowing when not to enter the competition.","Impatience reveals a desire; patience opens a path towards it.","Moving forwards together sometimes means slowing your first step.","Honest words gain value when they leave room for listening.","The true beginning comes before movement, in the clarity of your intention."],"roast":["Your enthusiasm sometimes races so far ahead that nobody has had time to understand your plan.","By trying to settle every disagreement immediately, you leave little room for answers that take time.","Your good ideas sometimes lose their impact when you insist on setting the pace of their execution too.","The desire to win can turn an ordinary conversation into an unnecessary competition.","Speaking frankly remains valuable when your words are carefully chosen.","What you call efficiency sometimes looks like making a decision before hearing the question.","When things resist, you double your efforts where a pause would be more useful.","You know how to launch projects with conviction; patiently guiding them onwards takes more effort."]},"funny":{"career":["Your file is already marked 'complete'. The boss has only just opened the meeting where they were supposed to explain the task.","When a colleague announces a 'quick meeting', you instinctively look for the finishing line.","A task marked 'urgent' makes you happy. At last, a document that understands your way of life.","The competition begins the moment two people head for the photocopier. The other person has no idea they're competing.","You've made a tracking spreadsheet for your twelve ideas. The 'read before starting' column is purely decorative.","This was supposed to be a team project. You've already assigned the roles, started the work and asked why nobody is keeping up.","If your boss says 'take your time', you mysteriously hear 'beat the record'.","Taking a coffee break sounds reasonable, provided you reach the machine before the rest of the department.","The meeting was meant to assign roles. You arrived with three projects already under way and an invitation to the closing ceremony.","You love pilot projects, especially when the pilot, plane and runway all bear your name on the schedule.","A colleague wrote 'idea worth exploring'. You've ordered digital shovels and booked the first presentation slot.","Your version of teamwork: you say 'let's go' while everyone else is still looking for their office shoes."],"love":["Your idea of a romantic date naturally includes an activity where someone has to finish first. Even crazy golf becomes an Olympic event.","When the other person takes ages to choose a restaurant, you've already checked three menus and mentally booked a table.","You fall in love like someone opening a present: ribbon torn off, huge grin, wrapping paper still on your head.","Affection makes you bold. You send an adorable message and check for a reply before you've even put down your phone.","Faced with 'we'll see', you immediately ask for the day, time and a written commitment, all with a smile.","This candlelit dinner seems peaceful until you turn choosing dessert into a passionate debate.","The moment someone mentions a surprise, you start looking for clues in the cupboards. Waiting is not part of your love language.","If someone teases you, you prepare a comeback. Then you remember it was meant affectionately.","Your flirting technique has three stages: instant crush, grand gesture, then learning the restaurant's name.","You planned a romantic surprise so quickly the candle never had time to leave its wrapper.","You've barely exchanged glances before proposing an adventure together. The other person thought they were choosing a pastry.","You reunite hearts with such energy that the flowers arrive before the conversation is over."],"wellbeing":["Your ideal rest looks like a race with the stopwatch removed, but not the speed.","When you try to meditate, your brain orders all your thoughts to calm down faster.","A peaceful stroll turns into an expedition the moment you spot a staircase to climb.","A nap seems suspicious to you: why lie still when so many cushions could be rearranged?","Faced with silence, you last exactly eight seconds before asking whether everyone else is bored too.","That glass of water waits on the table while you finish three 'quick' things. It never agreed to this much suspense.","Breathing calmly is an excellent idea, as long as you don't turn it into a breathing contest.","If you go out for some fresh air, warn your loved ones: 'a quick wander' might become a hike with an objective.","You installed a relaxation app. It says 'congratulations' because you finally managed a minute without changing screens.","A walk for fresh air ends with your personal league table of the neighbourhood's staircases.","Your yoga mat mostly knows you in passing. You cross it like a starting line.","You tried doing nothing all afternoon. Eight minutes later, you'd reorganised the furniture by speed of movement."],"wisdom":["Your courage is enormous; your 'wait' button is nowhere to be found.","Speed opens doors, provided you don't mistake the entrance for the exit.","Sometimes great courage means reading the sign before crossing the barrier.","Choosing a direction stops every detour turning into a trip around the world.","The universe moves at its own pace without reading your follow-up messages.","Race towards your dreams, but first check that the door is open.","A remarkable burst of energy is still a burst of energy, even if you haven't checked the map yet.","Silence is not necessarily a personal provocation.","The first door isn't always the right one. The wall beside it could confirm that.","Courage knows when to set off; judgement sometimes stays in the cloakroom just long enough to check the route.","Running towards an idea doesn't excuse you from asking where it lives.","A detour isn't a failure. Sometimes it's the only way to see the sign you rushed past."],"roast":["Your satnav didn't dare say 'recalculating' twice. It knows your temper.","You've reported an altercation with the biscuit dispenser. At the hearing, the coin slot was called as a witness.","You call it a 'constructive discussion' when everyone eventually agrees with you just so they can go home.","The doorbell rings and you're at the door before it stops. Even the postman looks surprised.","The satnav suggests a turn. You reply 'I know the way' with the conviction of an explorer standing outside their own garage.","The remote doesn't change channels at the first try. You issue it a formal warning on the corner of a napkin.","The word 'gently' makes you as suspicious as a lift stopping on every floor.","An annoying notification makes you fume, then you forgive it the moment it brings good news.","The alarm goes off. You negotiate so firmly that it rings again to summon a witness.","You accused an escalator of lacking initiative. It was doing precisely what it was built to do.","The automatic door is slow to open. You present your programme for reforming public entrances.","A jigsaw puzzle refuses to cooperate. You accuse the box of deliberately hiding the top-left corner."]},"piquant":{"career":["You launched the project without reading the brief. The team discovers the plans by watching the demolition work.","Your diary has four columns: urgent, very urgent, yesterday and 'why isn't this done?'. Monday has left the chat.","The colleague who says 'let's think' has just triggered your attack plan. Thought itself is hiding under the desk.","When an obstacle appears, you charge at it to teach it some manners. The obstacle was an open door.","You've turned handing out files into an office championship. The trainees came for paperwork, not medals.","You made a historic decision while ignoring six pages of recommendations. The final report opens with 'As stated on page one'.","The kick-off meeting hasn't started and you're already announcing the results. Out of respect for the facts, the minutes are written in the conditional.","Your natural authority extends even to the printer: you give it orders. It replies with a diplomatic paper jam.","Breaking news: you've finished a project before learning why it existed. The client wanted a poster; you inaugurated a motorway.","Office memo: all unread instructions will now be considered file decorations. You've already signed it.","Your desk resembles a command centre without maps: orders everywhere, no idea where the troops are heading.","You put 'immediate results' on the agenda. The minutes state simply: 'Reality was absent'."],"love":["Your romantic honesty arrives like an alarm with no off switch. Subtlety missed its chance to speak.","You turn choosing a film together into a duel of arguments. The credits roll before the ceasefire.","The smallest disagreement makes you argue with the passion of a historic speech. The issue was the colour of a mug.","When you're asked to let someone prepare a surprise, you're already unwrapping it. The mystery has handed in its resignation.","Your tender declaration has all the precision of a rocket launch. The other person was still looking for somewhere to put their coat.","Behind your grand declarations, a tiny voice demands an immediate answer. Even the calendar's heart can't meet that deadline.","Unanswered messages inspire four theories and three interventions. Your phone has requested a mediator.","You plan a romantic weekend like a lightning expedition. The surprise is discovering that nobody asked the other person.","Your relentless courtship has the pace of a film trailer: two exchanges, epic music, credits for an imaginary wedding.","You call it love at first sight. The calendar calls it a hostile takeover of next month.","Your reconciliation resembles fireworks set off while the other person is still finishing their explanation. Spectacular; questionable timing.","You organised a romantic treasure hunt. The only clue was 'hurry up'; the treasure gave up hiding."],"wellbeing":["Your relaxation programme includes a sprint to the nearest bench. The bench had never imagined such responsibility.","You go for a relaxing walk, then overtake every imaginary rival. The trees are calling for a referee.","The sofa welcomes you for five minutes; then you accuse it of lacking ambition. The cushions have formed a union.","When a queue moves slowly, you try to negotiate with space-time. The universe closes your case without action.","A break without a stopwatch seems suspicious. You install a finishing line next to the kettle.","Behind your explosive energy, a hammock is trying to explain the concept of calm. You interrupt it.","Quiet moments make you want to start a debate. The houseplant refuses to take sides.","You've turned tidying a drawer into a speed trial. The socks were ranked by order of arrival.","Customer review: 'The bench is comfortable but isn't making progress.' One star, signed by your impatient calf.","Your watch counted every movement during a rest session. It eventually logged a hand race across the armrests.","You turned stretching into a qualifying event. The mat won a medal for passive resistance.","Inner weather: persistent restlessness, with brief sunny spells of calm forecast only while a video loads."],"wisdom":["Charging ahead without a compass doesn't make you a pioneer. It makes you extremely punctual in the wrong place.","You don't charge in without thinking: you send reflection ahead as a scout after the battle.","The final word isn't a trophy. You've already ordered the plinth.","When someone says 'slowly', you hear 'prove you can go faster'.","Courage is like a key. You sometimes use it as a hammer on an open door.","Behind your bravery, common sense is asking for a high-visibility jacket.","Not every obstacle is provoking you. Some are simply trying to be furniture.","Waiting your turn isn't surrender. Your white flag is still in its packaging.","Bravery without direction is a postcard posted from the wrong town.","You sometimes confuse taking the lead with leaving before the story has begun.","The boldest shortcut can take you straight back to the start, with a bill for new shoes.","Knowing where to go is a virtue. Discovering it after three dramatic departures is a more personal method."],"roast":["Your toaster has received a written warning for poor responsiveness. You've granted it one final probationary slice.","You declared war on the satnav for suggesting another route. The roundabout is preparing its defence.","You appealed the verdict of a board game you were playing alone. The appeals committee, also you, is preparing a rematch.","When the coffee machine takes too long, you address it like an adversary. It protests by serving decaf.","A stubborn door offends you personally. Unfortunately, the 'pull' sign is a witness for the prosecution.","Behind your frankness, diplomacy is stranded at the tollbooth of your arguments.","You gave a red traffic light a lecture on individual initiative. It turned green halfway through your speech.","You challenged the cat to a staring contest. It yawned; you immediately disputed the rules.","The ticket machine displayed a perfectly ordinary 'please wait'. You're preparing a speech on freedom of movement for numbers.","You quarrelled with your reflection over an accidental grimace. The mirror chose not to give evidence.","Your coffee machine has been promoted to official rival. It won the debate by saying absolutely nothing.","You scolded the satnav over a road closure. A mechanical voice suggested arguing directly with the roadworks."]},"roastMy":["Aries, you're not impatient: you're an emergency that makes appointments with itself. You press the lift button seven times, then accuse the building of lacking team spirit. When the doors open, you rush inside. You only wanted to go up one floor.","You love winning, even when nobody is playing. You time yourself up the stairs, overtake a stranger and congratulate them for taking part. They were simply carrying their shopping. The Olympic committee has rejected your application.","Your honesty has all the delicacy of a drum in a library. Someone asks your opinion on a small decoration and you launch a national debate. By the end, you've convinced the vase to move. The wall wants to file a noise complaint against your arguments.","You charge ahead without thinking, then call it courage. A piece of furniture blocks your path and you start negotiating at full volume. It doesn't budge. You award it a highly disputed victory.","You can argue with anything that serves a purpose. Your satnav, alarm clock and coffee machine all feature on your list of opponents. None has accepted the challenge. Your toaster has requested an international ceasefire.","Your enthusiasm is contagious, but nobody asked you to turn the picnic into a competition. You assign teams, invent a scoring system and award points for the best-folded picnic blanket. Your friends sit down to eat. You accuse them of lacking sporting commitment.","You hate waiting almost artistically. Three people ahead of you at the counter become a major geopolitical obstacle. You mentally prepare a speech about efficiency. When it's your turn, you've forgotten what you wanted to order.","You love taking charge, especially when someone else is already doing it. A friend organises an outing; you rewrite the route and announce a 'more dynamic' version. The group arrives early at the wrong place. You claim a new speed record.","Your temper flares quickly and disappears even faster. You protest loudly over a comment, then cheerfully offer a biscuit two minutes later. The other person is still trying to work out what the argument was about. Your PR department has deleted the minutes.","You treat the slightest contradiction as an official challenge. A friend prefers another film, so you defend yours as if cinema's future depended on it. They finally agree just to get some peace. You proudly declare it a victory for dialogue.","You love being first so much that you start conversations before the other person has finished saying hello. Your diary contains projects unaware of their own existence. You call it dynamism. The office calls it a permanent preview screening.","You arrive at dinner with a brilliant idea for every minute of the evening. Everyone else had planned a quiet chat. You turn choosing the music into an opening ceremony. The waiter discreetly looks for the race judges.","Your speciality is treating any obstacle as a personal provocation. A locked door becomes a challenge, instructions become a rumour and a detour becomes an insult. Eventually you find the right route. It was on the sign all along.","You declare your affection with the energy of a speaker inaugurating a bridge. Your enthusiasm is sincere, but you're already posing for the official photo. The other person is still looking for the start of the sentence. The bridge hasn't been built yet.","Calm fascinates you like a gadget with no on switch. You tried a break, then a gentle activity, then making a schedule for future breaks. Your day of relaxation now has eight targets. The only missing one is 'relax'."]},"taurus":{"classic":{"career":["Your consistency gives projects a solid foundation. Still, be willing to reconsider a method when circumstances change.","When a suggestion disrupts your working habits, take time to assess it rather than dismissing it outright.","A long-term task suits your perseverance. Remember to communicate your progress regularly, however modest.","Your search for security shapes your decisions. It can be a strength, provided it doesn't shut out new possibilities.","Faced with a shared emergency, your calm helps everyone stay grounded. Just distinguish caution from standing still.","Your care for work well done is admirable. Sometimes delivering a finished result matters more than endlessly refining every detail.","If someone changes your routine, explain what you need to find your bearings and move forwards calmly.","You naturally favour tried-and-tested solutions. Yet a small experiment could still enrich your approach."],"love":["Your loyalty shows through everyday gestures. Leave room for the unexpected wishes of those you love.","When you grow attached, you seek to build something lasting. An open conversation can strengthen that sense of trust.","A shared habit can become a genuine language of affection. Be careful not to turn it into an obligation.","The pleasure of simple moments nourishes your relationships. Occasionally invite your companion to choose the plan.","Faced with disagreement, your firmness deserves to be balanced with listening rather than immediate defensiveness.","Your need for stability can be expressed tenderly. It doesn't require everything around you to stay the same.","You show a great deal through practical attentions. Remember to put your feelings into words too.","If a relationship enters a new phase, approach it step by step rather than clinging to what it used to be."],"wellbeing":["Your need for comfort deserves respect. Create a restful space without cutting yourself off from the outside world.","When life speeds up, a quiet moment over a meal you enjoy can help you regain your bearings.","A familiar walk can become a precious escape, especially when you take time to notice your surroundings.","The pleasure of routines supports your balance. Let a small novelty enter now and then, without pressure.","Faced with constant demands, give yourself permission to refuse anything that eats into your rest.","Your beloved sofa can provide a real break, without screens or unfinished to-do lists.","Looking after yourself can involve simple sensory pleasures: gentle music, pleasant lighting and time without urgency.","If obligations are taking over, slow down and return to an activity that brings you peace."],"wisdom":["Your perseverance becomes wisdom when it knows how to change course.","Comfort is precious as long as it remains a refuge, not a boundary.","A strong conviction doesn't need to shut the door on discussion.","Stability also grows from the ability to adapt.","Savouring the present doesn't mean holding back time.","A change you choose can respect what you already love.","Welcoming the unexpected adds richness to everyday gentleness.","Moving slowly doesn't stop you going far, provided you keep moving."],"roast":["Your attachment to routine becomes resistance when a simple alternative seems unnecessarily complicated.","Once you've made up your mind, even good arguments struggle to find a hearing.","Putting comfort first can keep you in situations that no longer truly suit you.","By demanding guarantees before every attempt, you risk never discovering what you might enjoy.","The pleasure of life's good things can take up so much room that spontaneity gets forgotten.","Beneath your apparent calm lies a determination that sometimes leaves little space for other people's opinions.","Your need to make everything predictable is reassuring, but can wear out those who enjoy improvising.","You would rather perfect a routine than admit that a new method might be simpler."]},"funny":{"career":["Your desk revolves around three priorities: efficiency, a comfortable chair and a strict ban on moving your mug.","When someone suggests new software, you ask whether the old version has done anything wrong.","A meeting at lunchtime is an attack on a fundamental pillar of your organisation.","Stability reassures you: your favourite folder has been there so long it probably deserves a plaque.","Faced with a new method, you demand a demonstration, a fortnight to think and your stapler's opinion.","This schedule will not change easily. You approved it, which is practically the same as carving it in stone.","If a task requires patience, they choose you. If it requires moving desks, recruitment starts again.","You believe in doing a job properly. You just struggle to believe anyone could do it differently from you.","The software announces an update. First you take a screenshot of the old interface to give it a dignified retirement.","You've scheduled lunch so precisely that even the canteen sets its clock by your empty chair.","Your professional objective: a stable job, a dependable team and absolutely no surprises in file names.","A colleague mentions 'rapid innovation'. You reply politely: 'Of course, once we've confirmed it's worked for fifteen years'."],"love":["Your primary love language is sharing your pudding. But beware: 'sharing' doesn't mean taking the last bite.","To win you over, there's no need to promise miracles: just remember you prefer pasta on Thursdays and a shared dessert on Saturdays.","A perfect evening begins with a good dinner and ends without anyone suggesting going out again.","Romance, to you, means remembering the exact pizza topping your loved one prefers.","Faced with a change of plan, you keep smiling. You just need time to mourn the restaurant you were expecting.","You love your little rituals together so much that you'd happily reserve them a permanent diary slot.","Your tenderness shows in the details: you know their favourite meal. One delicate question remains: how big is their portion?","If someone says 'let's improvise', you reply tenderly, 'of course, but according to which schedule?'","At dinner, you're happy to let someone else choose the music. Negotiations over the last chip are rather more formal.","You're so loyal to romantic rituals that the Friday booking knows you better than some friends.","An invitation to share a pastry turns into a crash course in the geometry of equal portions.","To show affection, you cook their favourite dish. You've also prepared a control portion, just in case."],"wellbeing":["Your sofa has an assigned seat that knows your habits better than some of your clothes do.","When you go for a walk, the route naturally includes a bakery and somewhere to sit.","A relaxation break isn't complete until the temperature, lighting and texture of the blanket have been approved.","Sunday inspires one great ambition: move as few things as possible without losing the remote.","Faced with an invitation to exercise, you offer a serious alternative: admire a beautiful view from a bench.","A cushion in the wrong position can ruin the atmosphere. You restore order with an architect's seriousness.","Fresh air sounds lovely, but first you want to know whether there'll be seats when you get back.","If anyone interrupts your nap, you open one eye with the gravity of a judge disturbed in court.","Your sofa has a perfectly calibrated landing zone. Guests cross it at their own risk.","Your favourite blanket has gone in the wash. The day is now operating under 'reduced comfort' procedures.","An unexpected nap makes you happy. An interrupted one becomes a matter discussed with administrative gravity.","In the evening you arrange a lamp, a mug and three cushions. The armchair awaits approval from the interior designer."],"wisdom":["Anything worth lasting needn't rush to arrive.","A good plan is one that includes a seat.","Perseverance is noble; refusing another restaurant for eight years is rather less so.","Happiness sometimes comes down to a blanket, especially if nobody borrows it.","Perseverance builds bridges; it's useless if you refuse to cross the one that's just been finished.","Time helps good ideas ripen. It doesn't stop you opening their window occasionally.","Faced with a cooling meal, your patience suddenly loses its crown.","Not everything comfortable is a piece of furniture you must keep for ever.","Patience can wait for the harvest; it can't plant the seeds for you.","A good idea that lasts deserves roots, not necessarily a fence around each one.","One slow step in the right direction is better than a perfect plan sitting in a drawer.","Routine is a strength. The calendar appreciates the occasional free square."],"roast":["You keep a restaurant menu out of loyalty, even after the restaurant has changed owners three times.","When an app moves its main button, you seriously consider sending a formal complaint.","Your favourite chair is so clearly claimed that guests almost ask its permission before sitting down.","The last slice of cake is a sensitive diplomatic matter. You favour a vote, while retaining your veto.","Faced with a new pillow, you conduct rigorous trials. Your old pillow awaits the results with confidence.","That comfortable outfit has survived so many Sundays it's practically part of the furniture.","Listening to you describe your morning routine is like discovering a tradition protected by a museum.","If someone proposes a shortcut, you ask why abandon a route that's always worked.","You declined three invitations to try a new method. On the fourth, you suggested reviewing it in five years.","At your internal debate, every argument voted against change. The arguments in favour hadn't been invited.","You've signed a permanent agreement with a habit. It renews automatically, with no exit clause.","Someone proved you wrong. You smiled and replied, 'An interesting perspective, but inaccurate'."]},"piquant":{"career":["The new software has three useful features. You've written a fifty-page study defending the old 'print' button.","You defend your method with the passion of a museum curator. The software has changed version; you haven't.","Moving desks strikes you as a treaty violation. Your chair has opened an embassy.","When a meeting proposes something new, you request three supporting documents and a guarantee you can return to the old system.","A procedure that works is sacred to you. Even its flaws have been granted protected-heritage status.","Behind your professional calm, an invisible sign reads 'do not touch my routines'. The interns have taken another exit.","Shortcuts make you suspicious: why save ten minutes when you can preserve a fifteen-year-old tradition?","Your desk is stable territory, right down to the biscuit you leave there. You've established a border around the tin.","The new software is installed. You've turned the old keyboard shortcut into a piece of the department's intangible heritage.","You've protected your lunch break with time barriers. An urgent call has been referred to the concept of tomorrow.","Your career advances at a carefully certified speed. Promotions have ample time to read the appendices.","The office announces a reorganisation. You submit a report praising the current desk layout, dated from when the building was erected."],"love":["Your romantic spirit can be measured by the number of dinners booked at the same restaurant. They're considering engraving your initials on the menu.","You defend your habits as a couple like listed monuments. Moving dinner by an hour requires a referendum.","Sharing is a wonderful value until the last bite arrives. Then you suddenly discover property rights.","When someone suggests somewhere new, you spend the entire journey praising your usual restaurant.","You've planned a surprise dinner for two: same table, same dishes, same dessert. The only surprise is the napkin colour.","You offer remarkably steady affection. The final mouthful, however, remains protected by a secret treaty.","Affectionate declarations delight you, but not while you're selecting the last spoonful of pudding.","You're devoted to the little rituals of a relationship. You've even registered your Friday routine as a recurring historical event.","You're happy to share your life, diary and habits. Your plate, however, has independent-nation status.","Fake survey: 98% of your romantic evenings feature the same menu. The remaining 2% are due to items being out of stock.","You've made loyalty to the favourite dinner a test of love. The other person was hoping to try something new on the menu.","Your idea of adventure together: change the order of courses without losing control over which restaurant you visit."],"wellbeing":["Your relaxation has an address, a blanket and a reserved spot. The furniture has registered your permanent residence.","You defend your nap like an international summit. Any interruption requires a written request in triplicate.","The sofa knows your habits well enough to stand in for you at meetings. Unfortunately, it refuses to leave the sitting room.","When someone suggests an impromptu walk, you first ask whether your shoes can stay where they are.","A hot drink brings great comfort, unless your usual mug is taken. No other mug is permitted across the border.","Behind your love of comfort, a military operation protects the ideal blanket temperature. The thermostat obeys cautiously.","Peaceful Sundays are your speciality, provided nobody introduces a surprise activity. The calendar remains under lock and key.","Your idea of stretching is to swap cushions. A committee is still reviewing the proposal.","Your blanket has been granted ownership rights over your evenings. Other textiles may apply, with little hope of success.","Official notice: naps are protected events. All interruptions will be reviewed after a second nap.","You've designed a relaxation route between armchair, kettle and sofa. The journey is so short it has its own imaginary Tube line.","Your spare cushion has a spare cushion. The concept of the unexpected has left the sitting room."],"wisdom":["Consistency is a virtue. Turning every past decision into a national monument is slightly less practical.","You don't change your mind: you give everyone else permission to exhaust themselves waiting.","Perseverance moves mountains. But you do have to accept that the mountain may no longer be where you left it.","When the world moves, you first check whether your armchair has brakes.","A habit isn't a law of nature. You've drafted its civil code anyway.","Behind your tranquillity, a defence committee protects the last slice of tart.","Time rewards deep effort. It never promised that conditions would remain exactly the same forever.","Moving forwards doesn't mean betraying your slippers. You insist on a notarised agreement anyway.","Perseverance is wonderful, except when it means waiting for the world to return to exactly where you left it.","You can be steadfast without becoming a statue commemorating your first decision.","What lasts deserves attention, not an unveiling ceremony on every anniversary.","Your sense of continuity is admirable. The future, however, never agreed to repeat the past exactly."],"roast":["You rejected a new idea before its author finished taking a breath. The proposal left with its first word untouched.","You resist change so consistently that a new label on a jar of honey becomes a national crisis.","The last piece of cheese isn't food: it's a strategic asset under surveillance.","Someone suggests another route to avoid roadworks. You prefer to look at the roadworks: at least it's a familiar road.","A suggestion to try something new meets your expression of a reinforced door. Even curiosity turns back.","Behind your legendary calm, a guard watches over the remote's exact position.","Your favourite phrase is 'I've always done it this way'. Innovation tried to present supporting documents and was refused entry.","You declared no argument would change your position. The chair, however, had just been moved one centimetre.","You're presented with new facts. You calmly inform them that they weren't invited to the conclusion.","Your opinion was carved in marble before the discussion ended. The sculptor had only come to take measurements.","You defended an outdated habit so passionately that the museum refused to take it: too difficult to move.","Instructions for changing your mind: step one, wait. Step two, reread step one. Step three is a state secret."]},"roastMy":["Taurus, your sofa is no longer furniture: it's a territorial administration. You have a seat, a blanket and a visitor-access procedure. Someone sits there by mistake. The cushion committee immediately orders an eviction.","Your obstinacy is like a locked door fitted with an extra lock of its own. Someone suggests a practical idea; you demand evidence, references and three seasons of testing. The idea withdraws. You announce that the current method has proved itself yet again.","You love the finer things in life, especially when nobody asks to taste the last portion. You watch the dish calmly, then discreetly move the strategically important plate. A friend suggests sharing. You suddenly discover the limits of international cooperation.","You insist you're open to new experiences. You'll even change restaurants, provided you get the same table, menu and atmosphere. A different sign outside is already a considerable adventure. Your plate requests a medal for bravery.","Your comfort has a constitution and you're its supreme guardian. Slippers wait beside the sofa, the blanket is folded to your specifications and tea arrives on time. A guest opens the window. You summon an extraordinary council of textiles.","You can defend an ordinary habit with the conviction of a top barrister. Someone wants to move the remote a few centimetres, so you explain the history of its position. Ten minutes later, they give up. The remote thanks you for your intervention.","You aren't moving slowly: you're observing the official pace of comfort. Everyone is waiting by the door for an outing while you're still looking for the right travel cushion. Someone reminds you it's only a walk. You ask whether seats have been arranged.","Your perfect Sunday tolerates no surprises unless they're delivered to your door. Someone suggests a spontaneous activity; you consult your blanket like a political adviser. The blanket says no. You present the decision as a family consensus.","You're generous until someone takes an interest in your portion. You'll happily share advice, blankets and recommendations. Then a hand approaches your biscuits. The friendship treaty is suspended until further notice.","Your love of stability would have you keep an old armchair even when it no longer suits the room. You explain that it has history, soul and a right to remain. A new chair waits outside. The old one has just been appointed Minister for the Living Room.","You treat new things like visitors who forgot to book an appointment. Updated software shows you its advantages; you proudly demonstrate the old menu. The demonstration lasts an hour. Your mouse is still working with the previous version.","You understand the value of regularity, and your habits wear long-service badges. Lunch happens in the same place, at the same time, with the same order of dishes. Once, the restaurant moved the tables. You still talk about it as a major reform.","You generously share your time and affection until a fork approaches your dessert. Suddenly you're an expert in international borders. The cake is divided into administrative zones. The enemy spoon is denied entry.","You know how to look after yourself: soft lighting, a carefully chosen book, an immaculate armchair. Moving any object requires an adjustment period. A guest helpfully rearranges the room. They discover the furniture is protected by a peace treaty.","People admire your quiet strength and ability to pursue a goal. Trouble comes when a sign suggests another direction might be better. You study it, then remain loyal to your original route. You call it consistency; the road map calls it a magnificent detour."]},"gemini":{"classic":{"career":["Your curiosity helps you connect ideas that others keep apart. Give yourself time to develop the most promising ones.","When several projects appear, your enthusiasm may become scattered. Identify a priority before taking on another.","A conversation at work can feed your creativity. Remember to turn it into clear decisions for what comes next.","Variety in your tasks stimulates your mind. A simple framework can help you finish what you start.","Faced with a complex problem, you naturally explore several angles. Then choose a solution and give it a genuine chance.","Your talent for explaining things becomes even stronger when you listen carefully to your colleagues' questions.","If new information contradicts your first opinion, flexibility is an asset. Explain what prompted the change as well.","Expanding your circle broadens your horizons. Nurture a few deeper exchanges rather than chasing every novelty."],"love":["Your need to communicate fosters closeness. Remember to welcome silences rather than rushing to fill them.","When someone intrigues you, you ask question after question. Allow the conversation to become an exchange rather than an interview.","A lively relationship inspires you when it offers room for discovery. Consistency can add richness too.","Your light-hearted humour makes connections easier. Recognise the moments when the other person seeks greater depth.","Faced with conflicting feelings, taking a step back can help distinguish passing curiosity from lasting needs.","Your taste for novelty keeps relationships fresh. Don't forget the value of the little rituals you've already built.","If you change your mind, simply explain your thinking rather than leaving someone to guess what's changed.","Speaking sincerely comes naturally. Listening without preparing your reply can create a different kind of closeness."],"wellbeing":["Your constantly active mind deserves moments of calm. Try reducing distractions during a break you've chosen.","When too many ideas collide, writing a few lines may help you regain a clear thread.","A short walk without your phone can provide pleasant space for your curiosity.","Your wide range of interests energises you. Reserve moments to enjoy just one activity as well.","After a day full of conversation, find a little quiet at your own pace.","Your need to keep discovering can wait until after a peaceful evening. Nothing obliges you to explore everything at once.","If your thoughts keep spinning late into the night, a soothing routine can make the evening gentler.","Taking a break from notifications can help separate what truly interests you from what merely distracts you."],"wisdom":["Your curiosity grows deeper when it is willing to stay.","Two opposing ideas can illuminate a choice, not replace it.","Words bring people closer when they leave room for a reply.","Exploring every path doesn't mean walking them all at once.","A free mind also knows how to finish what it chooses.","Changing your mind can be a strength when you can explain why.","Every novelty opens a door; attention helps you inhabit a room.","Listening to the end is sometimes the finest form of curiosity."],"roast":["Your curiosity sometimes stretches so far that your most important projects are still waiting for a conclusion.","When you ask a question, you've often prepared three answers before listening to the one you're given.","You change perspective with ease, sometimes leaving others unsure where you actually stand.","Your pursuit of novelty may draw you away too quickly from things that are only beginning to get interesting.","Faced with silence, you tend to add words where a glance would do.","Your need to comment on everything can tire those who appreciate a quieter presence.","If several possibilities appeal to you, putting off a choice doesn't necessarily improve them.","Starting a thousand conversations comes naturally; finishing just one sometimes demands real effort."]},"funny":{"career":["Your work browser has seventeen tabs open. You insist you know what each does, except the one playing music.","When you're asked for meeting minutes, you produce a gripping chronicle with supporting characters and plot twists.","A new app fascinates you for thirty minutes. Then you find another promising exactly the same thing.","The coffee break is mainly a chance to collect the latest office intelligence. Your mug goes cold, but your network is thriving.","Your inbox has 463 unread messages. You've sorted them into three categories: urgent, fascinating and 'I'll get back to it'.","Your report is going well until a colleague shares a new app. You open a folder labelled 'just comparing'.","You're managing five work conversations at once. The only person you've forgotten is the one waiting for you in meeting room B.","Juggling tasks amuses you. Finishing the one buried beneath the other fifteen is the real treasure hunt.","Your inbox announces 100 new messages. You say 'perfect' as though someone has delivered a box of chocolates.","You're in three video meetings simultaneously. In one, your microphone has just congratulated the wrong team.","You've created a new folder to organise your projects. It's called 'final version really final 4'.","You're working on one task, a message arrives, a colleague calls. By the end, you've made excellent progress on a fourth task's minutes."],"love":["You send a flirty message, then a second to clarify the first. The third confirms the first was meant to be romantic.","When asked where to eat, you suggest three restaurants, change your mind and meanwhile discover a pottery class.","A tender conversation with you can drift into volcanoes, neighbours and the best way to fold a sheet.","You love surprises so much that you sometimes change the plans yourself, then pretend to be amazed.","Faced with a message saying 'I miss you', you start replying and end up recounting six events from your day.","Your need to talk about everything is charming. Your partner has simply learnt to insert 'I'm off to bed' between two commas.","The moment you promise a phone-free evening, a fascinating article gives you a perfectly 'exceptional' reason to pick it up again.","You've accepted two invitations for the same evening. Your solution: suggest a walk that passes exactly halfway between the two addresses.","You've prepared four replies to 'shall we meet?'. You finally send the longest, complete with colour choices for the time slot.","Your flirting by text works brilliantly. You just need to explain why the conversation now has a contents page.","A date is barely suggested and you already know three possible cafés. Unfortunately, they're in three different neighbourhoods.","You change your mind about romantic plans like changing songs. Your companion would appreciate a pause between tracks."],"wellbeing":["Your brain opens a fresh mental window the moment you close your eyes to rest.","When you go for a walk to clear your head, you return with twelve ideas and the title of a podcast to hear.","A session of silence sounds interesting, but you'd first like to discuss its benefits with the group.","Relaxation starts when you put down your phone. It ends when you wonder what's happening elsewhere.","Faced with a pile of books, you begin four: it's your personal way of respecting every author.","You put on a podcast to relax, then increase the playback speed. The voices now sound as rushed as your thoughts.","Breathing without thinking sounds easy on paper. Your mind is already preparing a presentation to prove otherwise.","If you treat yourself to a quiet evening, try not to create a group chat to share its minute-by-minute schedule.","You tried looking at the scenery without doing anything. Moments later, you were hunting for a documentary about cloud formation.","A peaceful walk sounds lovely, especially with two podcasts and a list of things to tell people when you get back.","To avoid boredom, you decided to learn one quiet activity. You discovered six and started all six.","Your relaxation exercise involves listening to rain. You immediately compared seven recordings to select the best rain."],"wisdom":["Your mind knows a thousand routes; only one button says 'finish'.","Two opinions in the same sentence already make a panel discussion.","Silence doesn't need subtitles supplied by you.","A new idea can sometimes wait until the old one is out of its box.","Curiosity opens paths. It can also forget why it left the house.","Changing your mind is allowed; informing everyone else is still polite.","You don't have to tell everyone everything, even if you know the details.","Listening means letting a thought finish its sentence before introducing its three cousins.","A short answer can be complete, even when you know its entire family history.","A paradox makes more sense when you don't immediately give it an identical twin.","There's nothing wrong with asking a question. Occasionally it helps to hear the answer before asking eight more.","The world isn't short of topics. It just appreciates a sentence that eventually reaches a full stop."],"roast":["You know so much local gossip that the neighbourhood could commission a weekly newsletter from you.","When you say 'long story short', your friends start searching for a socket to charge their phones.","Your reading list contains articles whose headlines still fascinate you, even though you've forgotten why.","The sentence 'I've nothing to tell you' lasts less time with you than an unskippable advert.","Faced with choosing a film, you champion a comedy, then a documentary, then the idea of watching a series instead.","Your two-minute voice message needs an introduction, a digression and a conclusion announcing a second message.","The moment a party ends, you've already rewritten the best conversations to retell them to someone else.","If someone gives you the final word, you use it to launch an entirely new subject.","You heard a confidence, promised discretion and spent the evening discussing 'that story I can't tell you'.","You say 'I don't want to spread rumours', then provide a detailed map of the neighbourhood concerned.","Your version of a brief account includes the scene, context, historical background and behind-the-scenes context of the background.","You retold an adventure with two opposing endings. The audience loved it; the people involved want to check the script."]},"piquant":{"career":["Your chatter has turned the team briefing into a long-running series. The meeting now needs a recap of previous seasons.","You presented three opposing strategies in the same meeting. The 'conclusion' slide has just handed in its notice.","Your reply to an email has twelve drafts. The original message simply said 'received'.","When a colleague says 'in two words', you ask whether parentheses count. They're already closing their laptop.","A new idea thrills you until the next one arrives. Your abandoned projects have formed an administrative support group.","Your work screen resembles an international transit hub. Each tab announces a connection; none knows the final destination.","You forwarded six messages to six colleagues in six minutes. A seventh person was appointed to work out what this is all about.","Your talent for improvisation is remarkable: you change your conclusion halfway through the presentation. The slide refuses to follow.","Breaking news: your inbox holds so many drafts that a reply address has been created for messages never sent.","You assigned six tasks to six separate windows. The only one you closed was the essential file.","Your video meeting has four parallel conversations. The agenda has been sent to lost property.","Fake activity report: 27 messages, 14 follow-ups, 9 fresh ideas. Progress on the main task: a lovely title colour."],"love":["Your charm talks so quickly that silence never gets a chance to introduce itself. Even a smile receives audio commentary.","Your charm changes course halfway through a date. The table for two now has three possible restaurants and zero decisions.","Your first text was tender. The next five offered alternatives, an aside and a poll about emojis.","When someone asks what you truly think, you provide two opposite answers with the same smile. The jury demands a referee.","You chose a romantic outing, then changed your mind before putting your shoes on. The calendar keeps the first invitation as an archive exhibit.","Your declaration opens with 'there's something I want to tell you'. Eventually it reaches 'and that reminded me of Tuesday's coffee'.","Your goodnight message includes a postscript, then another. The phone has been assigned to overnight romantic duty.","Halfway through a walk together, you suddenly suggest a new destination. Your companion discovers the date has an interactive itinerary.","You created a poll to choose where to meet. Then you changed the options after the first vote; romantic democracy is reluctant to return.","Your tender message arrives with two corrections and three extra links. Affection has just acquired an after-sales department.","You proposed two outings at the same time, then claimed the invitations complemented each other. The calendar rejected the theory.","Your charm is like a five-way junction. The date was meant to be simple; it now comes with a key and directional arrows."],"wellbeing":["You've set a relaxation podcast to double speed. At that rate, the soothing voice sounds like an auctioneer.","You decide to do nothing, then search for the best ways to do nothing. Rest closes the browser.","Silence attracts you for eight seconds. Then you ask whether it has any interesting news.","When you go walking, three detours and two impromptu chats turn the neighbourhood into a travelling conference.","A break without stimulation seems suspicious. You consult the programme of available thoughts.","Behind your social energy, a blanket waits patiently. It's given up reserving a specific time.","Calm playlists never survive your curiosity. After two tracks, you're researching the history of the piano.","Your quiet evening began with a book. It continues with seven videos about how bookmarks are made.","You installed a peaceful-breathing app. It couldn't survive your desire to explore every setting.","Inner forecast: permanent restlessness, with brief calm spells during adverts you can't speed up.","You start a relaxation video, then watch it at triple speed. Serenity sprints through the room.","Silence enjoyed your company for one minute. Then you put on a podcast to assess its effectiveness."],"wisdom":["Your mind holds so many opinions that even a show of hands takes a week.","You don't change the subject: you found a new discussion without closing the old one.","Silence is sometimes an answer. You've asked it to elaborate.","When an idea crosses your mind, it meets three others travelling the other way.","You asked whether an answer could contain its opposite. You said yes, then no, then 'it depends'.","Behind every short sentence, you're preparing an appendix. The appendix has its own introduction.","Choices are easier when you stop summoning every argument. You never reach a quorum.","Knowing everyone is useful. You've also catalogued their stories into episodes.","One question can be profound. Fifteen stacked together make a staircase with no landing.","Your logic loves forks in the road. Sometimes it visits both dead ends to compare the decor.","Not all contradictions can be resolved by hosting a conference where you play every speaker.","Seeing every possibility is a gift. Deciding they're all right simultaneously is more like a philosophical circus."],"roast":["Your conversation began with 'I'll be brief'. The calendar changed month during the introduction.","You hold two contradictory opinions like two dogs on leads. The dogs want to go in opposite directions.","You've told the same rumour four different ways. The witnesses are beginning to doubt they attended the same event.","When a story is short on details, you add them. The witnesses no longer recognise their own account.","You declared 'I'm perfectly consistent', then argued the opposite to see if anyone was following. Nobody dared applaud.","Behind your curiosity, the 'next' button works much better than the 'finish' button.","Gossip travels through your mouth at express-train speed. Confidentiality is still waiting on the platform.","Your attention subscribes to every distraction available. The provider refuses to identify the main package.","Your little piece of gossip had two witnesses and a modest beginning. You added a subplot; the neighbourhood is preparing season two.","Someone shares a confidential detail. You present it to others as a totally anonymous case study, except for the address.","You changed your version of the same event three times while telling it. The original event now refuses to testify.","Your phrase 'just between us' has made four stops already. Confidentiality clearly isn't travelling on the same train."]},"roastMy":["Gemini, you don't have two opinions: you run an unstable coalition of them. Every idea demands a ministry, overthrows the previous one and announces immediate reform. You call it 'thinking aloud'. Your brain has requested standing orders.","You tell a tiny anecdote with the ambition of an international saga. There's a prologue, four supporting characters and a scene requiring a flashback. Your friends have forgotten the original question. You announce one more essential detail.","Your browser doesn't have tabs: it houses an entire city. Every window promises an exciting discovery and refuses to make room. You're looking for the page you opened this morning. Even the search engine wants a street map.","You get bored with remarkable efficiency. One activity excites you, then another, then a third, all at once. You end the day with twenty beginnings and tomorrow's idea list. Project endings have formed a defence association.","Your curiosity has no borders and no off switch. You ask someone about their weekend and three minutes later you're investigating the history of their neighbourhood. They only wanted to mention the cinema. Your interview awaits approval from the archives department.","You talk so fluently that others start nodding to get a turn. You take this as an invitation to expand. The group invents small flags for requesting the floor. You immediately suggest a debate about the flags' colours.","You can defend an idea with admirable conviction, then adopt its opposite before the coffee is finished. When someone points out the change, you explain both views are complementary. The coffee goes cold. The dictionary searches for a definition of 'agreement'.","Your flair for gossip would put a local paper to shame. You know who changed their houseplant, why a neighbour moved a chair and when two colleagues laughed. You swear you won't divulge a thing. You begin with 'I probably shouldn't say this, but...'","You want to discover the entire world in one afternoon. You start a recipe, read about a distant country and play a tutorial on fixing a drawer. Dinner approaches, the drawer is open and the trip is booked in your imagination. Your diary demands a translator.","Your mind leaps so quickly between ideas that conversations need imaginary safety helmets. A practical question becomes a philosophical debate, then a holiday memory, then a comparison of biscuits. You end with 'anyway'. Nobody dares ask for the summary.","Your mind works like a festival where every talk starts at once. You attend three sessions, speak at a fourth and take notes for a fifth. Nobody remembers the original theme. You call it an enriching evening.","You can make a simple date as complicated as a transport map. You suggest coffee, an exhibition, then a detour to try a bakery you found online. Your companion struggles to keep up. The date now needs a tour guide.","You have an extraordinary gift for recounting ordinary events. A broken doorbell becomes a serial drama with characters, motives and twists. Your friends follow the story avidly. The doorbell is still waiting to be fixed.","Your quiet moment was supposed to give you room to breathe. You selected soft music, compared five playlists and found a fascinating interview about musical instruments. Two hours later, the room is silent. Your mind is chairing a panel discussion about silence.","You hold two convincing opinions about almost everything, sometimes within the same sentence. Asked to choose, you explain that nuance matters. You add a third position for balance. The jury has just discovered you're also the jury."]},"cancer":{"classic":{"career":["Your sensitivity to the team's needs makes you attentive to subtle tensions. Try not to carry the group's entire mood on your shoulders.","When a colleague is having a difficult day, your listening can make a difference. Protect your own availability too.","A comment at work may stay with you longer than expected. Put it into context before drawing conclusions.","Your memory of past experiences guides your choices. Use it without letting an old disappointment prevent fresh initiatives.","Faced with a change of atmosphere, your intuition notices signals quickly. Check your impressions through direct conversation.","Your desire to protect others can build trust. Also let everyone experiment and make their own decisions.","If a team project matters to you, your commitment is valuable. Explain your expectations rather than hoping others will guess.","A supportive working environment helps you thrive. Learn to set limits when too many people seek your attention."],"love":["Your deep attachment finds expression in countless caring gestures. Leave room for the needs the other person actually expresses.","When a happy memory returns, share it as a gift rather than using it to measure the present.","A clumsy remark can echo for a long time. Asking for clarification is often better than withdrawing into silence.","Family and close connections hold an important place in your world. Ensure everyone can find their own place within it.","Faced with temporary distance, your imagination may fill in the blanks. A simple question can often clarify things.","Your need for comfort deserves to be expressed openly. Tenderness is easier to offer when it doesn't have to be guessed.","If you feel misunderstood, explain what affected you before withdrawing into disappointment.","Caring for someone is a beautiful way to love. Allow yourself to be cared for without organising everything."],"wellbeing":["Your sensitivity to your surroundings makes breaks in familiar places especially valuable.","When emotions accumulate, a quiet moment can help you welcome them without becoming overwhelmed.","A walk near somewhere you love can offer a comforting sense of continuity.","Nostalgia sometimes accompanies you gently. Enjoy your memories without losing sight of today's pleasures.","When loved ones make demands, give yourself permission to keep some time for yourself.","Your wish to make your home welcoming can become a soothing ritual, as long as it isn't another obligation.","If a day has required a lot from you, return to a peaceful pace and the comfort of a simple evening.","Checking on others comes naturally. Remember to ask yourself what you'd like today as well."],"wisdom":["Your gentleness grows stronger when it knows how to say no.","The past can warm your heart without directing every choice.","An emotion deserves to be heard, not necessarily to decide everything.","Protecting others doesn't mean carrying their silences.","Trust grows when expectations are expressed clearly.","A reassuring home also makes space for everyone.","Listening to intuition is valuable; testing it against reality makes it more accurate.","Caring for yourself takes nothing away from the love you give others."],"roast":["Your emotional memory can turn an old detail into a constant reference point for judging the present.","When words hurt you, your silence sometimes leaves others guessing what needs to be explained.","You care for loved ones so thoroughly that you sometimes forget to ask if they actually want your help.","Nostalgia can beautify your memories until new experiences seem less welcoming than they really are.","Faced with ordinary distance, you sometimes look for a meaning that isn't there.","Your need to protect your world can make you wary of changes that pose no threat to your connections.","If you sense tension, you may end up carrying emotional responsibility that isn't yours.","Comforting others comes naturally, but explaining what would help you can require more effort."]},"funny":{"career":["The moment a colleague sighs, you appear with a lighter schedule and an offer to proofread their report. They only wanted to change chairs.","When the boss writes 'thanks' without an exclamation mark, you spend the morning analysing the message's enthusiasm level.","An old team photograph is enough to launch a retrospective of every departure, birthday and welcome party.","The coffee machine is broken? You're more worried about team morale and set up a support group in the kitchenette.","Faced with a new intern, you arrange such a thoughtful welcome that they already know where the biscuits and tissues are.","You keep every old message from the team 'just in case'. Your inbox has become an insurance service for conversations.","If someone says 'I'm fine', you hear the hidden sigh between the words and immediately offer a proper chat.","Looking after the office atmosphere is your speciality. You even have a plant whose new leaves you celebrate with the team.","A colleague says she's having a busy day. You've already organised a rota so she won't have to carry the paperwork alone.","Your inbox contains welcome messages from everyone on the team for the past five years. You say it's 'to preserve the context'.","A trainee is looking for the meeting room. You've prepared a map, colleagues' names and a little note of encouragement.","You've distributed kind reminders to the team. The task board now resembles a very well-organised family gathering."],"love":["Your heart files memories with the precision of a national library. The ticket from your first cinema date probably has its own sleeve.","When a message arrives without an emoji, you wonder if affection has been temporarily suspended for maintenance.","Your perfect romantic evening means rewatching the film from your first outing and recounting everything the other person forgot.","Tenderness, for you, also means asking 'have you had enough to eat?' with admirable persistence.","Faced with 'see you later', you'd like an official definition of 'later' and its exact degree of emotional warmth.","That handmade present moves you so much you even keep the wrapping paper. It had a beautiful story too, after all.","The moment a familiar song starts, you recount the place, weather and feelings from the first time you heard it.","If someone forgets an important date, you say nothing. Your eyes, however, could deliver an entire lecture.","You remember the colour of the table mat on your first date. The other person mostly remembers laughing.","An old song takes you back to the start of a relationship. You recount the menu, weather and bus journey with archivist precision.","You kept the wrapping paper from a tender gift because the ribbon was lovely. The gift itself has less documentation.","You suggested recreating your first dinner exactly. The restaurant has a new chef, but you brought a copy of the original menu."],"wellbeing":["Your idea of comfort is a soft blanket, a hot drink and a film you already know by heart.","You've prepared a peaceful evening at home: dim lighting, a warm mug and a reserved armchair. The hosting arrangements are flawless.","A stroll past your old school immediately triggers an internal documentary with a melancholy soundtrack.","Relaxation is within reach, except you're wondering whether everyone else is as relaxed as you are.","Faced with a busy day, you suggest staying home. Your sofa welcomes you like a loved one returning from a long journey.","That little photo album was supposed to occupy five minutes. Two hours later, you're still moved by a photograph of a cake.","Taking a break for yourself feels odd: you instinctively look for someone to prepare a snack for.","If you watch an animated film, keep a tissue handy. Even a lost toy coming home can move you.","Your kitchen has a special recipe for busy days. You prepare it with all the solemnity of a welcome-home ritual.","A restful evening begins with choosing the blanket. This stage involves three qualifying rounds.","You've found the perfect sitting-room lighting. Since then, moving a lamp by a finger's width counts as a daring experiment.","Your definition of a peaceful outing: buy a few ingredients for a delicious dinner, then go home and enjoy the house."],"wisdom":["Your intuition sometimes hears a tragedy in a simple 'all right'.","Roots help you stand tall; they don't prevent you from growing a new branch.","Tenderness doesn't require a snack for every emotion.","A loved one's silence isn't necessarily the first episode of a tragedy.","A refuge protects you best when its door can also open from the inside.","Protecting someone close doesn't mean deciding how wide their wings should be.","Love also shows when you let someone choose their own soup.","Caring for others sometimes begins by letting them finish their sentence.","Strong roots don't decide which way the leaves must turn towards the sun.","You can cherish a relationship without managing the other person's calendar.","Looking after a garden also means letting plants invent their own shapes.","Memory illuminates the road. It shouldn't drive the car while you stare backwards."],"roast":["You've kept a birthday card so old its envelope knows more about your past than your friends.","When someone replies 'OK', your brain already drafts three possible scenarios.","You interpreted a simple 'OK' as a coded message. Three people have already received all your theories.","The theme tune from an old cartoon is enough for you to announce that the day is about to get emotional.","An advert for coloured pencils brought a tear to your eye. The main character finally found their favourite colour.","That voice message from someone dear is so precious you hesitate to delete it, even when it just says 'I'm here'.","Every family gathering ends with new photos and a personal mission: making sure everyone is happy.","If someone says 'nothing special', you're certain there's an emotion hidden behind the words and launch an investigation.","You treated a vague 'see you soon' as an official declaration of uncertainty. Your silence dressed for the occasion.","An advert shows a dog finding its toy again. You wipe away a tear while the dog has already started playing with something else.","You insist you're not offended. The tone of your 'of course' has chilled an entire group chat.","You were left off a minor group invitation. Your face stays pleasant, but your ellipses have a ceremonial air."]},"piquant":{"career":["Your sensitivity found a hidden meaning in a three-word email. The sender just wanted to confirm the time.","You saved six old versions of the meeting minutes. The server now houses a strategic reserve of semicolons.","A minor team reshuffle becomes a grand farewell ceremony. The chair that was moved receives a photo album.","When someone forgets to greet you, you mentally convene a committee on respect. They were on the phone.","A neutral remark follows you home. It's been granted a permanent place in your feelings diary.","Your support for colleagues resembles an unlimited helpdesk subscription. A simple 'thank you' is logged as official closure of the case.","You hold office traditions dear. The day the plant changes position, you consider a solemn tribute.","Your professional memory preserves anecdotes from the old building. Even the printer played a moving role.","You monitor your colleagues' morale like a forecaster of inner weather. Someone yawns: emergency support bulletin.","Your old emails are sorted into six backup folders. In case of failure, you could reconstruct the birth of every comma.","Your kindness at work has created an unofficial colleague-protection department. Even breaks come with a wellbeing form.","A new recruit says 'I'll manage'. You hand over a welcome pack so thorough it includes a map of the corridor."],"love":["Your nostalgia preserves cinema tickets like state documents. The keepsake drawer requests an extension.","You interpret an 'all right' without an emoji as an icy diplomatic declaration. The phone knows nothing about the crisis.","The slightest tender memory becomes a permanent exhibition in your head. Visitors are forbidden to touch.","When someone forgets a minor date, you declare you bear no grudge. Your silence has just sent fourteen notifications.","You kept the receipt from your first restaurant together. It now has more annotations than a historical manuscript.","Behind your caring gestures, a little monitoring unit checks whether your affection was properly noticed. The register is open.","Old conversations remain on your phone 'out of affection', you claim. Your inner archivist is preparing their decade-by-decade classification.","Your heart happily offers refuge, then takes offence when nobody admires the emotional décor in the entrance hall.","Your first date occupies an archive worthy of a guided tour. Even the paper napkin comes with explanatory notes.","You saved a blurry photo from a dinner together. You insist it captures the atmosphere; the photographer mostly sees a plate.","Your old conversations are stored under sentimental titles. The phone now thinks it's in charge of a romantic library.","You found the ticket from a memorable outing and planned a reconstruction. The other person thought they were just agreeing to coffee."],"wellbeing":["Your idea of rest is rewatching an old film and feeling exactly what you felt before. The closing credits know you by heart.","Your sitting room has been arranged to welcome every passing mood. All it lacks is a reception desk for the blankets.","The sofa understands you so well that you consult it before agreeing to go out. It always votes for the blanket.","You prepared a comforting meal with the solemnity of a ceremony. The soup received a speech before being served.","A peaceful day at home becomes a pilgrimage among photographs, boxes and sentimental mugs. The dust signs the visitors' book.","Behind your desire to nest, a fortress of cushions protects every sigh. Guests enter after an emotional security check.","Walks appeal until a bench reminds you of a conversation long ago. The bench becomes the star of a saga.","Your relaxation was meant to last an hour. You spent forty minutes looking for a blanket 'with a story'.","Your cosy evening involves four blankets, a hot drink and a check for draughts. The sitting room resembles a polar research station.","The oven releases a lovely smell and you declare the house officially reconciled with the world. The timer applauds politely.","Your favourite armchair has its own lighting, mug and standby blanket. The installation ceremony lasts longer than the film.","Customer review of your own sitting room: 'Excellent atmosphere, but the main blanket refuses to leave its residence.' Five stars."],"wisdom":["Your nostalgia requested funding to expand the museum of Sundays gone by. The present is waiting outside.","Roots nourish what grows. You've sometimes put them in charge of the entire garden.","Protecting your world doesn't require an identity check for every new experience.","When someone says 'nothing', you launch a four-chapter emotional investigation.","A tear during a cartoon doesn't require a press conference. You're preparing the dossier.","Behind your tenderness, a watchful guardian tracks who forgot to say 'thank you' at the right moment.","Your memory is a remarkable library. It would benefit from keeping the reading room open to the present.","Caring for others doesn't oblige you to knit them an emotional timetable.","You defend your roots passionately. They don't need a security guard for every new leaf.","Attachment to the past adds depth. Using it as the only map of the future makes navigation rather tricky.","Your protectiveness is precious, except when it erects a fence around people who've only come to say hello.","A strong memory is a compass. You've occasionally promoted it to permanent minister for every journey ahead."],"roast":["You sulked because someone replied 'all right' in a tone that was too neutral. The full stop is now the prime suspect.","You sulk so subtly that the entire neighbourhood has to guess why. The council refuses to investigate.","The latest cartoon reduced you to tears when an object was reunited with its owner. The object requested some privacy.","An advert about a family reunion moved you. Then you accused the toaster of failing to share the moment.","A visit to your old café becomes a historical ceremony. The waiter just wanted to take your order.","Behind your adorable attentions, an invisible checklist verifies that everyone has noticed your efforts. The stamp is missing.","A harmless joke upset you. Three hours later, you'd assigned it a file, a timeline and two witnesses.","Your sulk was supposed to go unnoticed. You merely published a detailed timetable of silences to observe.","Your 'everything's fine' comes with such carefully staged silence that it deserves opening credits.","You analysed the punctuation of a routine message like a detective in a crime novel. The culprit was a keyboard key.","An advert about a reunion moved you. You then accuse the director of springing an imaginary box of tissues on you.","A light-hearted joke doesn't land; you reply 'no worries'. The group has just received a calendar of possible apologies."]},"roastMy":["Cancer, you don't keep memories: you run a private museum of everyday feelings. A crumpled ticket, a ribbon and an old shopping list each have their own legend. You explain their importance for twenty minutes. The drawer has just opened a ticket office.","You sulk like a diplomatic service that has broken off negotiations without giving a reason. Someone asks if you're all right; you reply 'perfectly'. Your silence then issues three statements. The cushions act as peace ambassadors.","You happily cry at cartoons, especially when two characters meet again after being separated. You know the scene already and still prepare tissues. A friend asks why you're replaying the film. You say it's 'for the plot', and the credits sigh.","Your phone holds enough touching screenshots to fill a library. You keep the most ordinary messages because they arrived on an important day. Someone suggests a clear-out. The archives committee declares the proposal inadmissible.","You look after loved ones with the generosity of a 24-hour concierge service. You prepare the blanket, drink and encouraging note. Then nobody notices the perfect fold in the napkin. Your inner gratitude department files a complaint.","Your love of home goes far beyond decoration. Every cushion has a memory, every mug a story and every sofa corner sentimental value. A guest suggests moving a lamp. You ask them to respect the room's cultural heritage.","You remember everything, especially the little remarks everyone else has forgotten. A harmless joke made over lunch years ago returns complete with the date and menu. The person who said it has no idea what you mean. Your memory produces the minutes.","You adore quiet evenings with loved ones gathered round a table. Everything is cosy until someone announces they're leaving a little early. You smile, then gaze at the empty chair like a scene from a film. The chair requests an end to the dramatic music.","Your emotional intuition detects shifts in mood through punctuation. A 'thanks' without an exclamation mark triggers a search for causes. You reread three weeks of chat to understand. The person simply had a flat battery.","You love the past so much that even old biscuit tins have the right to remain. You explain that each one recalls something precious. There's no room left for new biscuits. The kitchen launches a sentimental urban development plan.","Your emotional memory could recreate a first dinner from a simple cooking smell. The dish returns, accompanied by a full account of the evening. Your loved ones listen fondly. The current dinner patiently waits its turn in the story.","At work, you protect your team with the care of a lighthouse keeper. A colleague changes desks and you immediately check everything is all right. They were just moving closer to the window. You prepare a little welcome visit anyway.","Your home is a full committee for welcoming comfort. You've selected the lighting, adjusted the cushions and found a recipe that makes the place inviting. A guest suggests going out for fresh air. The kitchen suddenly displays tomorrow's menu.","Your sensitivity can turn a tiny remark into a silent serial drama. You say you've forgotten it, then arrange the words in the order they were spoken. By the next day, all is peaceful again. Your memory has kept the subtitles.","You can laugh at an advert, then be touched by its ending with equal intensity. Minutes later, you recount it to someone, adding the sweetest details. They think they've missed a major film. It was an advert for storage boxes."]},"leo":{"classic":{"career":["Your desire to shine can become a strength when it also highlights the team's work.","You enjoy taking visible initiatives; paying sincere attention to quieter contributions will strengthen your influence.","The confidence you inspire creates space to present your ideas simply.","When your creativity is free from the need for instant approval, it gains depth.","A leading role naturally appeals to you; appreciate what is built behind the scenes too.","Behind your confidence lies a genuine sense of commitment, best expressed through your actions.","Your professional generosity can give renewed energy to a team that needs it.","The energy you devote to projects deserves a clear direction rather than constant recognition."],"love":["Your natural warmth brings a special presence to exchanges when you listen as much as you share.","You appreciate gestures of attention; offering yours without expecting a return nurtures closeness.","The need to feel appreciated in relationships benefits from curiosity about the other person.","When you let go of the need to impress, your affection appears more gently.","Generous tenderness reveals itself in simple gestures, far from grand declarations.","Behind your pride lies deep sincerity that sometimes seeks a quieter language.","Compliments touch you, but authentic conversations can bring more lasting joy.","Your way of loving finds its full value when both people have space in the relationship."],"wellbeing":["Your expansive energy deserves moments when you have nothing to prove.","You can also recharge in tranquillity, away from other people's gaze.","The pleasure of creating something just for yourself can be a lovely way to slow down.","When your diary puts you at the centre of everything, a quiet break restores balance.","A walk without a goal gives your mind space free from performance.","Behind your enthusiasm, your need for rest deserves recognition too.","Time with loved ones can nourish you without your having to entertain everyone.","Your joy in life benefits from moments of quiet, chosen simply for their own sake."],"wisdom":["Your light shines brightest when it lets others shine too.","You need no applause to have worth.","The courage to be simple reveals a more lasting greatness.","When pride listens, it becomes confidence.","A sincere presence illuminates more than a performance.","Behind every visible achievement lies devotion to small gestures.","The finest impulses don't always need a stage.","To shine is also to know how to share the space."],"roast":["Your desire to lead can take up so much room that others struggle to finish a sentence.","You enjoy being noticed; a silence around you isn't necessarily disapproval.","Your craving for compliments may sometimes obscure what genuinely makes you proud.","When every exchange becomes a chance to persuade, spontaneity fades.","An impressive entrance cannot replace an attentive presence.","Behind your generosity, consider whether the wish to do good always demands a witness.","Other people's glances cannot tell you everything about the quality of your relationships.","Your charisma loses nothing when you give up the final word."]},"funny":{"career":["Your office resembles a stage: even filing a document deserves an encore of applause.","You present an idea at a meeting as if unveiling the next great discovery. It's a new filename.","The colleague who praises you instantly becomes your favourite person in the department. Rankings are updated hourly.","When volunteers are requested, your hand shoots up before the question is finished. It then demands a microphone.","Your signature on a simple document becomes something of an official ceremony.","Behind your screen, you rehearse your speech as if the board were a television talent show jury.","Team successes delight you so much that you immediately suggest a group photo, with you in the middle.","Your business card could read 'Head of Memorable Moments'. You've already been doing the job unofficially.","Office memo: your presentations will now have end credits. The Excel document had no idea it was pursuing an artistic career.","You congratulated the whole team after the meeting. Then you handed out cards for everyone to take notes on your closing speech.","By your reckoning, meetings become 40% more interesting when you speak. Colleagues have asked how to switch off that statistic.","'Who's chairing this meeting?' 'Officially, nobody.' You've nevertheless planned a grand entrance and a final bow."],"love":["Your charm loves grand gestures; even offering a biscuit requires a presentation speech.","For a simple dinner invitation, you've planned an entrance with music. The person you love thought they were coming for pasta, not a world premiere.","The smallest date deserves a festival-style entrance, in your view. Red carpet optional.","When your partner describes their day, you listen sincerely, then discreetly check whether they noticed your outfit.","A photograph of you both works after several attempts, mainly to capture your best smile.","Behind your affectionate generosity there's sometimes a little brass band that doesn't know when to stop.","Tender words melt your heart; a simple 'nice jumper' can brighten your mood until dinner.","Your declaration fills three cards, each more romantic than the last. All that's missing is an interval for the other person to reply.","Your romantic surprise includes petals, a playlist and an itinerary. The other person merely asked where to leave their shoes.","You send such an epic declaration that your phone offers to publish it as a serial. Episode one ends on a heart.","You bring flowers to a date with a little speech. Fortunately, the bouquet doesn't need subtitles.","You've imagined a candlelit dinner with an entrance worthy of the cinema. The tiny flame nearly stole the scene."],"wellbeing":["Your relaxing morning begins with choosing an outfit worthy of a prestigious spa. You take so long the tea goes cold backstage.","You try a silent break; after two minutes, you're considering publishing a report about it.","Your skincare routine has an opening, a finale and theme music. The face-cream bottle is your most punctual co-star.","A simple walk becomes your private catwalk. You stride so confidently that pigeons step aside like imaginary photographers.","An evening with no plans feels restful, provided you get to choose its opening credits.","Behind your thirst for fresh air, sometimes all you need is a sofa and a blanket worthy of your prestige.","Quiet moments appeal to you, especially when nobody confuses calm with an absence of admiration.","You've reserved some time just for yourself. Programme: relaxing bath, majestic dressing gown and an imaginary autograph on the towel.","Your face mask turns ten minutes of quiet into ceremonial preparation. You emerge from the bathroom as though from a secret dressing room.","Fake weather forecast: spa atmosphere, light fragrant mist and a high chance of the dressing gown being worn majestically.","You chose relaxing music for your break. Two tracks in, you've composed the title of your next beauty ritual.","A quiet bath would almost be enough. The towels just need to be folded like those in a hotel with something to prove."],"wisdom":["Your modesty sometimes arrives late: it's looking for a more spectacular entrance.","You willingly share the spotlight, provided you keep control of the switch.","Light knows how to illuminate without reciting its autobiography. A technique you might borrow from the sun.","When nobody's watching, a Leo can finally finish a hot coffee.","A good idea doesn't need your portrait on the poster.","Behind every grand speech there may simply be a longing for a biscuit.","Shining isn't a contest of intensity. A candle can be useful without declaring war on a lighthouse.","Shining together means nobody has to carry all the lighting.","A lamp shines better when it accepts it isn't the only one in the room.","The courage to shine matters; so does the courage to let someone else go first.","True light isn't measured by how many people turn their heads. The streetlamp agrees.","Modesty doesn't extinguish anything. It merely turns down the dimmer when others are looking for their keys."],"roast":["Your entrance into a room deserves a trailer. Shame you only came to fetch your keys.","You don't ask the time; you give the watch an opportunity to answer you.","Your modesty is so discreet it appears in gold lettering on your wallpaper. The font size is set to 'royal'.","When someone tells a story, you have a more spectacular version, even if you weren't there.","A group photo without you in the middle looks like a framing error to you.","Behind your regal smile, there's a complaints department for insufficient compliments.","Other people's birthdays delight you: at last, a room decorated in time for your entrance.","Your generosity is sincere, but the gift occasionally comes with a programme of your own acknowledgements.","You tried taking a picture without yourself in it. The phone thought you'd pressed the wrong button.","Your mirror now bears a plaque: 'Your most devoted admirer works here.' Opening hours are extensive.","When someone says 'you're wonderful', you reply 'in which area?'. The questionnaire is three pages long.","Your ego entered a competition for discretion. It sent a press pack announcing its application."]},"piquant":{"career":["Your ambition doesn't want a job: it wants a balcony from which to salute the company. HR is considering spotlights.","You demand recognition for your contribution to the meeting. You moved a chair; the annual report will follow.","The smallest team success becomes your press conference. Everyone else is invited to find themselves in the photo.","When nobody applauds your presentation, you suspect a widespread failure of artistic judgement.","A promotion appeals mainly if the title fits on a suitably shiny plaque. The furniture is negotiating its survival.","Behind your enthusiasm as a leader, every colleague discovers they're an unwitting extra. Casting began without asking.","Anonymous tasks offend you: how can anyone perform a feat without witnesses? The printer now refuses to sign autographs.","Your leadership turns the quarterly review into a big-budget show. The figures were never consulted about being extras.","Breaking news: your team has completed a project. You've already written the victory speech, behind-the-scenes documentary and proposal for an annual ceremony.","You call it participative management. Everyone mainly participates in finding space on your launch poster.","Your contribution was so magnificent the presentation received an encore. The original subject is still waiting for a slide.","Fake staff poll: 98% know about your latest achievement. The other 2% were on leave and received a registered letter."],"love":["Your need to be admired turns a quiet dinner into an awards ceremony. The menu includes 'Outstanding Presence'.","You offer affection generously, then await the thank-you ceremony. The speech must mention your name.","You stage a romantic surprise so elaborately that your guest receives a programme. Emotion is scheduled for the opening act.","When you say 'I don't want to attract attention', you're already checking whether anyone heard the announcement.","A discreet declaration seems almost suspicious to you. You ask where the photographers and violins are hiding.","Behind your dazzling charm is a small reactions-monitoring office. Every lukewarm smile triggers an audit.","Modest romantic gestures puzzle you: where should the curtain rise? The sofa requests a performance permit.","Your heart has plenty of room, mostly for a framed portrait of you. The other person may choose the frame.","You don't plan romantic dates; you produce emotional blockbusters. The dessert has to audition.","'I have a surprise for you.' 'What is it?' 'Three minutes of speech before you can see it.' The suspense bears your signature.","Your affection arrives with a ribbon, violins and an imaginary photographer. Your companion is just looking for a chance to hold your hand.","A small affectionate card would have sufficed. You chose parchment, a seal and a public reading; the postman is now master of ceremonies."],"wellbeing":["Your rest requires an audience. Without an admirer to witness your serenity, you consider filing a complaint.","Your beauty ritual involves staging, three accessories and a majestic exit from the bathroom. The dressing gown is negotiating a fee.","The sofa was meant for a break; it now houses your ten-volume autobiography. The cushions demand royalties.","You've turned meditation into an internal awards ceremony. Calm won, but you kept the trophy.","A solitary walk becomes a parade past shop windows. The mannequins have asked you to stop competing with them.","Behind your busy days, you search for one minute without a spotlight. You find it, then name it after yourself.","You love a bath of tranquillity until you want to publish the results. A judging panel has already been summoned.","Your version of self-care resembles a touring star's dressing room. The moisturiser travels under a confidentiality agreement.","Your skincare routine has grown from a private moment into palace protocol. The cotton wool wears a badge and the towel has an official rank.","Customer review: 'Flawless relaxation break, but the dressing gown refused to leave the dressing room before its third entrance.' Overall rating: royally complicated.","You don't take a bath; you inaugurate a miniature thermal spa. The bubbles have booked the best seats.","Instructions for your calm: prepare the atmosphere, select the accessories, announce your arrival. Optional step: actually relax."],"wisdom":["Your ego doesn't need a throne: it has already booked the entire boardroom.","You call it charisma. The walls call it a conference without breaks.","Silence isn't criticism of your talent; it's a statutory pause.","When you share the spotlight, the miracles department opens specially.","An invisible crown is merely an accessory. You've requested insurance for yours.","Humility is like an open window. You've fitted theatre curtains and started charging for the view.","Sometimes lighting the way for others simply requires stepping back. You preferred to enlarge the spotlight.","Light is better shared than a crown. You put the crown on the light bulb and declared balance restored.","Shining without dazzling means making room for shade. You've installed a 'reserved area' sign.","Light belongs to nobody. Your communications team is still working on that discovery.","Greatness can be recognised by knowing when to step aside. You removed everyone from the scene except yourself.","A lighthouse is there to guide ships, not autograph them. You're preparing the signed postcards anyway."],"roast":["Your ego asks for an extra seat at dinner. The restaurant has registered it as a group booking.","You describe yourself as simple: your simplicity has a logo, a slogan and a press office.","The mirror recognises you before you arrive. It's finally asked for annual leave.","When a friend succeeds, you congratulate them and offer to host the ceremony. Uninvited.","A conversation without you at the centre triggers an emergency protocol. Reception has stopped answering.","Behind your generosity, thank-you notes come with twelve pages of house rules. Initialled by you.","Selfies have become your external memory. Your phone no longer knows what scenery looks like.","Your humility has just published a book. The dedication takes up the entire cover.","Newsflash: your selfie has been granted personal-monument status. Your phone gallery is offering guided tours.","You don't seek compliments. That would be too simple. You've opened a reception desk where compliments must book appointments.","Your ego entered a waiting room. It renamed the chairs 'royal gallery' and handed out portraits of you as tickets.","The mirror reported an anomaly: nobody has admired your favourite profile in three days. You've opened a crisis unit."]},"roastMy":["Leo, you don't enter a room: you officially open it. You check the lighting, the angle of everyone's gaze and the audience's responsiveness. Family lunch becomes your annual conference. Your relatives have requested simultaneous translation for the compulsory compliments.","You adore admiration, but 'well done' no longer suffices. You want a 'well done' with reasons, a date and two witness signatures. The compliment finally arrives and you dispute the wording. Your legal department is called 'me'.","Your generosity is enormous, especially when it comes with a poster. You buy pudding, arrange a photo and give a speech about gratitude. The cake goes cold beneath imaginary applause. The bakery has asked its next donor to keep things discreet.","You claim not to like attention. Odd, for someone who announces their arrival in the group chat before even closing the door. Once seated, you ask whether the atmosphere was different without you. The silence is recorded as a five-star review.","Your selfies don't capture moments: they document a reign. The scenery tried to appear behind you, but you cropped out the intruder. Even the sunset ended up as background to your smile. It's preparing a complaint for unfair competition.","Your ego won't fit into an ordinary meeting. You demand an agenda, a lectern and a minute's ovation at the start. The subject was choosing paper cups. The cups have left the committee.","You dream of simplicity, provided it's elegant and noticed. Your casual outfit required three fittings and an official announcement. Even your old jumper has a communications team. The dry cleaner now refuses interviews.","Your presence lights up parties, mostly because you turn up the lamps yourself. You tell a story, then reenact it with the proper dialogue. Your friends know the script by heart. One has requested a stand-in for the laughter.","You receive a compliment like a capital city receiving a state visit. Protocol, smile, a little thank-you speech and a reminder of forgotten achievements. The person only wanted to say your plant looked nice. The plant has demanded the presidency.","Your gift for leading people is undeniable; you even guide those who already know the way. You point out the exit to a shop, then check that your efficiency was acknowledged. The security guard gave you a symbolic task. You turned it into a coronation.","Leo, you agreed to join a treasure hunt with friends. At the first riddle, you took charge and renamed the team in your honour. You eventually found the treasure in your own pocket. While the others hunted for the map, you prepared the museum opening.","You wanted a simple evening without any staging. You began by assigning roles to every guest, then drew a traffic plan around your armchair. Everyone felt wonderfully welcome when they arrived. Except spontaneity, which got stuck in the cloakroom.","A day without plans was meant to help you reconnect with yourself. You created a private ceremony celebrating every tiny achievement, from choosing breakfast to putting away a book. By noon, you'd awarded seven distinctions. The day refused to introduce an eighth category.","You were chosen to announce good news to a group. Your voice became a film trailer, then you paused to build suspense. Your friends waited solemnly for the revelation. It was a new card game, now entered on your list of achievements.","Your hospitality is spectacular: you offer a chair, explain its history and describe its place in your decor. The guest finally sits, impressed by all the attention. Then you produce a booklet on the other furniture. The sofa moved out during the introduction."]},"virgo":{"classic":{"career":["Your eye for detail helps strengthen a project before it is presented.","You like clear methods; they can also make room for an unexpected idea.","The precision you bring to every step reassures those who work with you.","When your standards become too demanding, distinguishing essentials from extras makes progress easier.","A complex task often finds coherence under your methodical gaze.","Behind your need for organisation lies a sincere desire to be useful.","The small improvements you notice can make a big difference to shared work.","Your analytical ability becomes even more valuable when combined with trust in others."],"love":["Your attention to detail helps you notice needs that aren't always expressed.","You often show affection by making everyday life easier for people you care about.","Your wish to do things well can soften when you welcome the unexpected into your relationships.","When you stop searching for perfect words, your sincerity finds a more direct route.","A relationship is also built through imperfect gestures that become beautiful memories.","Behind your reserve lie attentive listening and deep loyalty.","The nuances you notice in another person sometimes deserve to be accepted without analysis.","Your tenderness shines when the wish to do everything right leaves space for spontaneity."],"wellbeing":["Your love of order can be a resource, provided rest doesn't turn into a task.","You benefit from setting aside moments with no particular goal.","The pleasure of simply walking, without an optimised route, can refresh your attention.","When everything seems to demand correction, a quiet moment helps you see things differently.","A break away from screens allows your demanding mind a little flexibility.","Behind your sense of responsibility, your need for peace deserves room too.","Simple gestures such as drinking water or breathing at your own pace support everyday balance.","Your wellbeing cannot be measured by the number of boxes you tick."],"wisdom":["Your precision serves life best when it leaves room for it.","You can care for a detail without trying to correct everything.","True balance accepts things that are still developing.","When method meets flexibility, effort becomes lighter.","A completed list does not define a day's worth.","Behind every imperfection, a fresh possibility may lie.","Simple things don't need improving to be beautiful.","Accepting the unfinished is also a form of mastery."],"roast":["Your need to check everything can make decisions heavier than they need to be.","You notice tiny discrepancies so easily that those around you get little respite.","The desire to organise perfectly sometimes postpones the moment you can enjoy the result.","When a sentence seems clumsy, correcting it may take up more space than its intention.","An overly detailed list can make you forget why you began it.","Behind your concern for efficiency, the unexpected sometimes deserves more trust.","The advice you offer so precisely isn't always requested with equal precision.","Your pursuit of flawless work benefits from recognising what's already good enough."]},"funny":{"career":["You proofread an internal memo for 'one quick check'. Three versions later, the punctuation is perfect and the meeting has been rescheduled.","You reread a colleague's email to check one detail; three commas receive a full performance review.","Someone gives you a document to proofread. You return the document, a key to the corrections and advice on naming the versions.","When someone says 'we'll improvise', your diary symbolically closes all its windows.","A fifteen-minute meeting becomes your chance to save the world from bad numbering.","Your office gets a new procedure. You immediately discover there's no procedure explaining how to read the procedure.","Your notes during a call are so precise that the person speaking wants to order a copy.","That favourite pen isn't lent lightly. It was chosen after a thorough comparison.","Official notice: any misplaced comma must be reported to your department. Sentences have started tiptoeing.","You proofread a three-line email and added a contents page. Recipients need to find their way around somehow.","'Is it ready?' 'Almost.' You're still deciding whether 'almost' needs a definition in the procedure manual.","A new procedure interests you, especially after you spot six places where it could become a better procedure."],"love":["Your declaration of affection resembles a well-run service: you've remembered the umbrella and the bus timetable.","You immediately notice that someone has changed a tiny detail in their home. They didn't realise you kept an inventory.","You prepare a dinner for two around every preference your companion has. One detail remains: how to mention that the napkin is folded incorrectly.","When someone gives you flowers, you're touched and immediately research the most suitable vase.","A surprise delights you enormously if it has the courtesy to appear in your calendar.","Behind your serious manner is someone who says 'I care about you' by fixing a cupboard door.","Your romantic message contains a lovely gesture and three useful clarifications. The last explains exactly where to find the surprise.","Your desire to care for others sometimes includes a little note on the correct way to fold napkins.","You remember their favourite drink, ideal temperature and preferred side of the table. Only their enjoyment of surprises remains unresolved.","Your tender declaration begins 'I was thinking of you' and continues with a detailed proposal for improving future dates.","You instantly notice a new habit in the person you love. They thought they'd only moved their mug.","Your partner mentions a little problem. You offer an attentive ear, then three solutions ranked by delicacy."],"wellbeing":["You tidied your relaxation space so carefully the cushion no longer dares move. Rest is waiting for permission to sit down.","You want fresh air, but compare three routes before choosing the simplest walk.","The blanket is carefully folded at precisely the moment you should be sitting beneath it.","When you take a break, you mentally note that it began two minutes late.","A cup of tea becomes an exercise in precision, with even the saucer in its assigned place.","Behind your urge to tidy everything, the sofa sends you an invitation without an attachment.","Walking does you good, especially when you accept that a leaf may be out of place.","Your notion of tranquillity includes the satisfaction of finally filing every notification.","You've reorganised the towels by size. Your bathroom now resembles a shop with just one customer: you.","Fake inner forecast: clear skies over the shelves, a little dust north of the sideboard, action scheduled before teatime.","To relax, you lined up the shoes in the hall. The laces have finally understood collective discipline.","You declared a cleaning-free evening. Then wrote an exception for crumbs, and another for fingerprints."],"wisdom":["A lovely day can tolerate one little imperfection. The sky doesn't proofread itself before opening.","You can trust life even when it forgets the contents page.","Mess isn't always an emergency; sometimes it's a displaced cushion.","When one box stays unticked, the universe doesn't automatically launch an inquiry.","A misplaced comma won't stop the coffee tasting good.","Behind perfection there's often a chair you could simply sit on.","Unexpected events never read your procedures. Very rude of them.","What matters can sometimes fit in a folder labelled 'look at later'.","One perfect detail won't always fix a shaky idea. The dot on the 'i' isn't the architect.","Accepting a small mistake is letting life write a note in the margin without reaching for the eraser.","The world sometimes moves forward with a misplaced comma. It still finds the next paragraph.","The essential things don't always wear labels. You'll need patience to recognise them."],"roast":["Your critical mind never sleeps. Even a holiday poster gets layout suggestions.","Your shopping list has a key, categories and a small box for the unexpected. The unexpected already has a label.","The slightest 'roughly' makes you want to produce a spirit level.","When someone says 'it's fine as it is', you hear the start of negotiations.","You label empty boxes to show what they might hold. The 'spontaneous ideas' box is carefully sealed.","Behind your polite smile, an assessment grid is secretly awarding everyone marks.","Your leisure spreadsheet separates 'fun', 'very fun' and 'fun, subject to approval'. Leisure awaits the verdict.","Your relaxation is so precisely scheduled that it could clock in for work.","Your weekend plan has a box labelled 'plan nothing'. It's already booked for checking the plan.","You made a list for preparing your lists. At level three, the pencil declared independence.","Fake domestic survey: 100% of objects have labels. The cat refuses to disclose its category.","You created a comparison chart for storage boxes. The boxes aren't sure they want to be put inside it."]},"piquant":{"career":["Your perfectionism has turned a simple email into a regulated building site. The opening sentence is still waiting for planning permission.","You correct colleagues' commas with the gravity of a judge. The keyboard has requested a barrister.","You proofread a colleague's presentation until you corrected the spelling of their name. The meeting opens with a debate on administrative orthography.","When a task is finished, you reopen it to check whether it deserves that status. The word 'finished' has resigned.","A simple internal memo went through your quality control. You found three inconsistencies and invented a fourth step to document them.","Behind your flawless methods, an oversight committee already oversees the oversight committee. The auditor is you again.","Deadlines only seem respectable when they include a buffer, a warning and a backup warning plan. The diary is hiding.","Your attention to detail has stalled a meeting over the title's typeface. The meeting was about an emergency that's already passed.","Breaking news: your team submitted flawless copy. You reported an inconsistency between two invisible spaces. Celebrations are postponed.","You correct procedures with the seriousness of a conductor facing a wrong note. The musicians are resigned photocopiers.","Your proofread of an internal announcement took longer than the decision it announced. The announcement has lost the will to exist.","Instructions for your ideal meeting: check the agenda, approve syntax, inspect headings. Actual subject: optional."],"love":["Your tenderness expresses itself through discreet corrections. The bouquet looked lovely before you audited its vase.","You listen to confidences like a quality-control manager. The person wanted affection; they receive an improvement plan.","A romantic message touches you, then you spot two mistakes. Cupid has been summoned for retraining.","When someone arranges a surprise, you request the time, address and degree of preparation. Mystery has cancelled its visit.","An evening together counts as a success once the cushions are symmetrical. Feelings are waiting in the cloakroom.","Behind your delicate attentions, an invisible form assesses the consistency of tender gestures. The 'spontaneity' box is greyed out.","Other people's endearing little flaws amuse you, unless you can fix them in five steps. Romance has opened a support ticket.","Your heart isn't closed: it's filed by subject, date and priority. The key is in a shared folder.","You don't observe your partner's habits; you publish a comparative study. The 'adorable little quirks' chapter has 46 appendices.","A romantic gesture arrives with storage instructions and a precise explanation of every detail. Emotion is looking for the 'free play' button.","You spotted a small inconsistency in a tender declaration. Congratulations, the feeling is now certified compliant with a previous version.","'Did you have a lovely evening?' 'Yes, but the second half could have been better structured.' The date enters the teaching archives."],"wellbeing":["You cleaned the relaxation corner with the precision of a laboratory specialising in imaginary dust. Then banned any activity that might make it dirty.","You arrange the cushions before lying down, then check their alignment. The sofa requests a mediator.","Silence soothes you until you notice a slightly crooked clock. Calm has been postponed.","When you go walking, you optimise the streets and compare pavements. Even fresh air gets a score.","A hot drink was meant to relax you; instead you started comparing mugs. It went cold during the audit.","Behind your good intentions, relaxation looks like a surprise inspection. The blanket hasn't got its papers.","Free weekends worry you: no box says where to put enjoyment. Sunday is waiting for a job description.","Your determination to switch off is exemplary. You've merely scheduled three reminders so you don't forget.","Your wardrobe is so tidy the socks have sector numbers. The odd sock now lives abroad.","Customer review: 'Spotlessly clean, impossible to find anything outside its authorised position.' You replied with a scale drawing.","You cleaned the table, then the sponge, then the spot where the sponge rested. The cycle now continues without human intervention.","Your evening ritual has four tidying steps and one relaxation break. The break has been moved so it won't interrupt the tidying."],"wisdom":["Details are useful guests, not the owners of the house. You've nevertheless given them the main bedroom.","You don't seek perfection: you pursue the flaw right into its neighbours' homes.","Chaos is sometimes just a moved sock. Your report runs to twenty pages.","When you say 'just one detail', the technical department evacuates the premises.","A comma doesn't run the world. It hasn't learnt that yet.","Behind your inner peace, an inspector checks the folds in the clouds.","Mistakes are human. You've asked to proofread the human registration form.","The unexpected failed to fill in your questionnaire. You deny it entry.","Perfection always promises one last tweak. You've taken out a lifetime subscription.","The essential doesn't disappear because a detail sticks out. You've opened a committee to measure the protrusion.","A tiny mistake can become a lesson. You've turned it into an annual conference on the millimetre.","Imperfection sometimes adds character. Your autocorrect has lodged a formal objection."],"roast":["Your priority list contains a section on how to rank priorities. The binder is preparing to enter government.","You have a list for everything, including reasons to stop making lists. It's laminated.","One crooked picture frame triggers an inquiry committee. The nail pleads not guilty.","When someone types 'should of', you mentally suspend diplomatic relations.","An improvised evening looks like logistical sabotage to you. The board game awaits authorisation.","Behind your apparent calm, an inspector checks whether the napkins have signed the register.","Other people relax; you assess the quality of their relaxation and suggest improvements.","You labelled the jars, then the spare labels. The label marked 'labels' now occupies a picture frame.","Your guest list has a 'planned sociability' column and an 'actual sociability' column. Your friends have become data.","You've made labels for the drawers that hold labels. A new category is born: 'classification crisis'.","Your spreadsheet for tracking spreadsheets has overtaken the main spreadsheet. It's now scheduling annual reviews with its own columns.","You don't make plans; you plan the plan that will approve your future plans. Chance no longer has a security pass."]},"roastMy":["Virgo, you don't tidy your home: you govern a territory. Every object has an address, a function and a penalty if it moves. Your guests leave their coats in the wrong zone. A disciplinary committee meets before pudding.","You correct mistakes the way others greet neighbours. A loving message arrives with a tiny error and you almost forget why it moved you. You send a heart, then the corrected version. The keyboard requests an administrative separation.","Your to-do list has a cover, chapters and an appendix devoted to sublists. You tick a box with the satisfaction of restoring world order. Two new tasks appear. The list has founded its own bureaucracy.","You call it 'liking things done properly'. Everyone else calls it 'having to submit paperwork to move a chair'. You offer to simplify the process with a shorter form. It has fourteen pages.","You analyse every message so closely that a simple 'that works' becomes a riddle. Why not 'perfect', why the full stop, why that exact time? The conversation was over, but you've just launched a parliamentary inquiry.","Your idea of spontaneity is switching the order of two planned activities. You experience a great thrill, then restore the schedule. Even fate receives the minutes. It didn't ask for a read receipt.","You love being helpful, especially when you can explain what should have happened beforehand. Your assistance is efficient, detailed, documented and accompanied by a diagram. Everyone thanks you sincerely. Then they hide their drawers.","You dream of a day with no obligations. So you clear your diary, prepare a list of obligation-free activities and set a reminder to enjoy them. At noon, you audit the efficiency of rest. The hammock threatens legal action.","Your kitchen is so organised that a missing spoon could trigger a national alert. You find it in its proper place, turned slightly sideways. You suspect deliberate interference. The dishwasher has requested political asylum.","You don't judge anyone, you say solemnly. You observe, classify, compare and mentally draft a constructive review. A friend merely asks whether their presentation was clear. You request an extension for the projector.","Virgo, you offered to help organise a walk with friends. You prepared a route, two alternatives and a sheet for recording deviations. The walk went smoothly, apart from a leaf falling on the path. You added 'unexpected leaves' to the next agenda.","You dreamed of giving a completely spontaneous present. You compared wrapping papers, checked dimensions and tested three ways to tie a bow. The present was delightful, perfectly wrapped. The surprise eventually arrived with its own instruction manual.","You decided to let someone else cook for once. You smiled, watched the preparation and suggested one tiny improvement that led to five more. The meal was excellent; nobody doubted that. The spatula put 'independence' on next year's wish list.","In a library, you spotted a book leaning slightly. You straightened it, then adjusted its neighbours to keep everything aligned. Ten minutes later, an entire shelf looked inspected by an invisible authority. The librarian thought the inspectors were visiting.","You decided to spend a day without evaluating anything. You resisted rating the coffee, journey and music. That evening, you congratulated yourself in a three-page review. Spontaneity received nine out of ten."]},"libra":{"classic":{"career":["Your sense of balance offers perspective when opinions clash at work.","You know how to bring different viewpoints together; choosing a clear direction completes that talent.","Your pursuit of harmony can support projects without excluding useful disagreements.","When several solutions look appealing, your essential criteria can help you move forwards.","A nuanced approach can make cooperation easier around a delicate decision.","Behind your diplomacy lies an ability to defend an idea with elegance.","Professional decisions become lighter when you accept that you needn't compare everything.","Your aesthetic sense can inspire polished presentations and an original vision."],"love":["Your desire for harmony encourages exchanges where everyone feels heard.","You love creating beautiful moments; their simplicity can matter as much as their appearance.","The need to please can ease when you express your own preferences more freely.","When a conversation calls for honesty, your gentle manner can accompany sincere words.","A balanced relationship also grows from differences you learn to welcome.","Behind your quiet charm lies a deep wish to understand the other person.","Everyday hesitations matter less than the quality of your attention.","Your sense of fairness finds a more personal expression through tenderness."],"wellbeing":["Your pursuit of balance can guide you towards a pace that respects your needs.","You appreciate pleasant places; even a simple atmosphere may be enough to soothe you.","Your concern for keeping everyone happy sometimes deserves to give way to your own peace.","When choices multiply, time away from demands can help clarify what you want.","A walk through harmonious surroundings renews your attention to small details.","Behind your willingness to help others, your personal time deserves protection.","Aesthetic pleasures, gentle music or a bright room can accompany your rest.","Your inner peace doesn't require everyone around you to agree."],"wisdom":["Your balance grows when you dare to choose without absolute certainty.","You can listen to every voice without forgetting your own.","Beauty doesn't replace truth, but it can open a door to it.","When peace demands silence, honesty deserves a space.","An imperfect decision is sometimes better than endless waiting.","Behind hesitation there is often a desire to do the right thing.","Differences don't erase harmony; they give it texture.","Choosing gently is still a genuine choice."],"roast":["Your need to compare can delay choices that really just require a preference.","You try so hard to accommodate everyone that your own opinion can become hard to hear.","Your desire for a pleasant atmosphere may lead you to avoid a necessary discussion.","When two options seem equal, you risk spending longer weighing them than enjoying either.","Being excessively polite can make people think you agree with things you don't actually want.","Behind your charm, a sincere hesitation sometimes calls for greater clarity.","Other people's opinions enrich your thinking without needing to make the decision for you.","Your sense of harmony remains precious even when a conversation becomes less comfortable."]},"funny":{"career":["Your ideal meeting ends when everybody agrees. It could therefore continue until next quarter.","Before approving a proposal, you consulted four colleagues. A fifth is tasked with checking that nobody felt left out.","A disagreement between colleagues turns you into a mediator; you've already arranged reconciliation drinks.","When two teams argue over a task, you suggest a compromise so elegant that each leaves with half a stapler.","Being asked to make a quick decision feels almost like a competitive sport.","Behind your diplomatic smile, twelve drafts of an email begin with 'perhaps'.","Your consensus meeting ends with a unanimous vote to hold another meeting. At least this one won't divide anyone.","Your talent for hearing arguments is immense; even the clock is starting to make its case.","Your favourite phrase at work is 'both your ideas have merit'. The problem is that they're completely contradictory.","Fake team survey: twelve colleagues consulted, zero conflict and a project still in consultation. You call it a peaceful start.","'Can you make a decision?' 'Of course.' You immediately suggest a meeting where everyone can explain why they'd rather not.","You defuse tense discussions with such tact that even the printer agrees to share its paper without complaining."],"love":["Your romantic side hesitates between a candlelit dinner and a walk. You mentally book both.","You hesitate between a romantic walk and an intimate concert. In search of the perfect moment, you've invented a walk with imaginary music.","Choosing a present begins with such a careful selection that it could become an exhibition.","When you're told 'you choose where we eat', you smile with the dignity of someone facing an unannounced exam.","Your sense of beauty turns a small gesture into a film scene. A simple bouquet becomes a declaration worthy of its own soundtrack.","Behind your natural charm, a silent committee debates the best way to say goodnight.","Disagreements upset you; you can present two opposing opinions with equally remarkable sweetness.","Your charm is so natural you can make ten minutes of indecision over how to say 'good evening' seem adorable.","You rehearsed a romantic invitation in three different tones. The last was so charming you couldn't choose between the other two.","An elegant shop window inspires a date idea. The next shop window inspires an even better one. Your stroll becomes a gallery of intentions.","You give flowers matched to the evening's atmosphere. Your companion mostly notices that you've finally dared give something.","Your flirting skills extend to choosing a bench with a view. Both spots appeal so much you remain standing."],"wellbeing":["Your relaxation starts with choosing an atmosphere. Three candles later, you're still unsure about the lighting.","You plan a walk, then spend ten minutes comparing two equally lovely parks.","The sofa cushion is never quite in the right place. You discuss the issue with it internally.","When a friend asks what would make you happy, you say 'whatever you like' with dangerous sincerity.","A soothing playlist becomes a compilation of difficult choices between equally beautiful tracks.","Behind your desire for peace, sometimes you need to choose without asking the vase for its opinion.","Beautiful objects relax you; yet your eyes end up mentally rearranging the entire room.","Your ideal afternoon would be free of decisions. You still need to decide how to organise it.","You rearranged three pictures to create a peaceful corner. Now the armchair doesn't know which way to relax.","Your rest ritual begins by aligning the cushions. Relaxation starts once both sides of the sofa have signed a peace treaty.","Fake inner forecast: harmonious conditions, localised risk of vase movement following a slight imbalance.","A bouquet seems ideal for softening the room. After ten attempts, you found its perfect spot: where it started."],"wisdom":["Your balance doesn't require a vote for every biscuit.","You can love two options and still choose one before the shop closes.","Good taste doesn't need twelve witnesses to exist.","Choosing one door means accepting you won't visit every other one. You can keep the brochures, but not the handles.","Having an opinion doesn't automatically trigger an international conference.","Behind every hesitation, there may simply be a sofa waiting.","Contradictions can coexist, but they needn't drive the bus.","Choosing at random is still a choice; a die could explain that better than you.","To keep your balance, sometimes you have to move forward rather than compare every available shoe.","Two choices can both be beautiful. The secret is enjoying the one you've made without writing to the other.","Hesitation helps you think; it shouldn't rent a flat inside your head.","An unmoving balance doesn't prove wisdom. Sometimes it's just waiting for someone to remove a pan."],"roast":["At a restaurant, you've narrowed the menu down to three dishes. Historic progress, but the waiter has finished their shift.","You avoid conflict so skilfully that you apologise to a door when it gets in your way.","The restaurant menu knows you well: you read it like a novel with multiple endings.","When someone asks your preference, you list the merits of both options and forget the question.","An argument nearby immediately activates your mediation service and a distribution of napkins.","You've been choosing between two paint colours for so long the wall has learnt to love temporary white.","Beautiful objects attract you so much that even a paper clip must have an elegant line.","Your tact is legendary: you could politely inform a mirror that it's reflecting badly.","You've compared the menus of three restaurants. The first closed for renovations while you were deciding.","In the paint shop, you're torn between soft beige and calm beige. The shop assistant didn't know those were two countries.","Your ideal menu offers just one option. You still wonder whether the other option was omitted by mistake.","You spent twenty minutes choosing an umbrella. The rain has stopped, but the colour is almost decided."]},"piquant":{"career":["Your indecision turns choosing a stapler into a diplomatic summit. Delegations demand a closing date.","You consult eight colleagues before sending a three-word email. The reply arrived before your question.","Your diplomacy turned a procedural disagreement into a 45-minute sharing circle. The procedure was forgotten in the cloakroom.","When management demands a decision, you deliver a comparison chart so balanced that even the columns refuse to choose.","You want every colleague to feel heard. So you organised a consultation about the order of consultations. The project is still waiting its turn.","Behind your agreeable smile, a whole department is still trying to find out what you think. The investigation was filed under 'aesthetics'.","A negotiation with you ends so peacefully nobody knows what was decided. The minutes read simply 'constructive atmosphere'.","Your diplomacy is flawless: you've secured everyone's agreement to decide nothing. The minutes are grateful.","Official notice: your team has formed a consensus committee. The committee can't agree on the meaning of 'consensus'.","You're so good at avoiding conflict that disagreements get renamed 'parallel proposals'. The meeting ends with two incompatible decisions.","You consulted twelve colleagues to approve a three-word sentence. The thirteenth didn't feel represented; back to square one.","Your gift for mediation could reconcile a stapler with a sheet of paper. Unfortunately, the required report is still unwritten."],"love":["Your charm works on everyone, including someone merely asking for directions. They leave with three hypothetical invitations.","You hesitate between two ideas for a date, then three, then five. The calendar has sought custody of the weekends.","A romantic dinner starts with 'whatever you like'. Forty suggestions later, the kitchen closes.","You flirt with such delicacy that your invitation resembles an art exhibition: beautiful, perfectly lit and impossible to interpret.","A possible argument makes you change the subject with remarkable elegance. You've just complimented a lamp.","Your romantic indecision turns two date ideas into a suspense serial. The trailer still doesn't reveal the venue.","You spread charm so effortlessly your smile resembles a product launch campaign. Romance hasn't actually seen the product yet.","Your heart wants a perfectly balanced fairy tale. The characters are still waiting for you to choose the cover.","You don't choose between two romantic ideas. You organise an imaginary final where each option must defend its charm before an absent jury.","Your art of flirting resembles a prestigious gallery: everything is gorgeous, but you must follow the marked route to reach an actual declaration.","You prepared an exquisitely elegant invitation. The wording is perfect, the paper too. The date was left blank to preserve all possibilities.","Fake romantic statistic: 100% of your declarations are beautifully delicate. Half have never left your draft notebook."],"wellbeing":["Your pursuit of serenity stops before two candle scents. The candle council refuses to take sides.","You prepare for a break by comparing cushions for forty minutes. Rest has cancelled its booking.","Choosing a bench at the park becomes a study of light, view and harmony. The pigeons occupy both candidates.","When offered a surprise walk, you ask to see the alternatives so no route feels slighted.","A cup of tea relaxes you until the mug question arises. The cupboard files a complaint for aesthetic harassment.","Behind your legendary gentleness, a small civil war rages between two relaxing playlists. Silence wins by default.","You dream of holidays without a schedule. You've drawn up a schedule for choosing the unscheduled holiday.","Your quiet moment requires the agreement of the curtains, flowers and blanket. The cat has vetoed it.","Your sitting room displays remarkable balance. A plant moved two centimetres has nevertheless triggered a decor emergency meeting.","Customer review: 'Beautiful room, peaceful atmosphere, absolutely forbidden to move a mug.' The furniture whispers its agreement.","You chose three vases to make the room more serene. They now spend all day discussing their relative positions.","The rug was supposed to add softness. You've made it responsible for morally connecting the curtains to the sofa."],"wisdom":["A balance is for weighing, not immobilising the world. You've added a third pan to examine that distinction.","Choosing means letting go of the other possibility. You tried keeping the letting-go as an optional extra.","Compromise is admirable. Asking the plants to vote on dinner is less so.","When two roads appear, you hire an architect to build a third.","A delayed decision doesn't grow more elegant. It simply acquires a new ribbon.","Balance doesn't mean standing in the middle of every road. You've installed a bench at the crossroads.","Mirrors reflect what exists. You're still asking which one is right.","Choosing isn't an attack on the remaining options. They'll recover.","An unmade choice isn't a perfect choice. You've simply preserved the decision behind glass.","Balance sometimes means leaning one way. You've invented movement without going anywhere.","Inner peace isn't a permanent negotiation between two buttons. You're drafting a neutrality treaty anyway.","Letting go of an option isn't erasing it from the world. You've erected a small memorial to it."],"roast":["Your indecision is so organised that it has an advisory committee and three deputies.","You studied the menu for so long that the chef changed it. You now have a fresh philosophical problem.","The menu is a suspense novel whose final page you refuse to reach.","When conflict erupts, you smile so hard that even the chairs feel obliged to negotiate.","A personal preference crosses your mind. You immediately put it out to public consultation.","Choosing a single colour led you to make a chart of 84 shades. White won the vote through collective exhaustion.","You distribute so many compliments that even the car park thinks it's beautiful.","Your idea of urgency is to decide quickly to postpone the decision. The minutes are ready.","Your restaurant order became a referendum. The waiter voted for their break.","You hesitated between two shades of green, then invented a third: 'green that respects the other two'.","Your inability to choose a starter created a new culinary tradition: dinner begins after dessert.","The shop offers five mug designs. You ask to compare their merits before an independent commission; the shop is closing."]},"roastMy":["Libra, you don't choose a restaurant: you organise a public consultation. Everyone offers an opinion, you build a comparison chart and add one last-minute option. The group eventually goes home. You conclude that the atmosphere stayed excellent.","Your diplomacy could reconcile two imaginary enemies, but not choose between two puddings. You weigh the price, presentation, textures and the waiter's mood. The waiter offers you both to speed things up. You ask whether there's a third option.","You love beauty so much that a misplaced cushion feels like a failed negotiation. You move it, then the other one looks unbalanced. An hour later, the sofa resembles an exhibition. Nobody is allowed to sit on it yet.","You say 'I have no preference' with a perfect smile. Everyone suggests something; you explain the merits and drawbacks of each idea. Eventually someone begs you to say no plainly. You ask whether that would be polite.","Your charm is a weapon of mass peace. You compliment the greeting, the décor and even the receipt. The shopkeeper replies kindly, and you worry you were too enthusiastic. A mediation unit assembles around a till receipt.","You avoid arguments with almost professional talent. Two friends debate and you agree with each in turn with identical conviction. Finally they ask you to decide. You propose a tea break that lasts three seasons.","You compare outfits as if a museum were preparing a permanent exhibition. Each option has its case, atmosphere and target audience. You finally choose the first, then ask whether it was really best. The wardrobe demands compensation for excessive consultation.","Your pursuit of fairness goes so far that you ask the last slice of cake whether it prefers to be eaten or shared. Nobody dares answer for it. You devise a fair rotation system. The cake demands an urgent decision.","Your need to please makes you agree with everyone, including two people saying opposite things. You then try to reword both positions into compatibility. Even the dictionary refuses to testify. You find it a bit too categorical.","You dream of a harmonious life without tension or difficult choices. Unfortunately, every morning starts with two equally pretty mugs. You stand at the cupboard weighing their merits. The kettle has applied for a transfer.","Libra, you agreed to choose the music for a trip with friends. You prepared a playlist for every possible mood, then hesitated over the order. The trip passed in remarkably peaceful silence. You arrived with a perfect return playlist that nobody dared put on.","You wanted to organise a fair exchange of presents. You compared wrapping, symbolic value and everyone's feelings, then proposed a distribution with no losers. Everyone thought your idea wonderfully thoughtful. In the end, the presents exchanged themselves to move things along.","You promised to make a spontaneous decision before going out. You opened two wardrobes, studied three outfits and pondered the impression each would make. You left wearing the first outfit you'd tried. The bravery of that decision deserved a minute's silence.","Your eye for beauty led you to rearrange the table for a game with friends. Everything needed to be accessible, attractive and fairly placed. The players admired your arrangement. Then they found the cards had been sorted alphabetically to avoid favouritism.","You were asked to settle a disagreement between two friends about a game rule. You listened to both, acknowledged their arguments and proposed wording that would satisfy everyone. The friends made up. The game was cancelled because no usable rule remained."]},"scorpio":{"classic":{"career":["Your penetrating insight helps reveal concerns others have yet to put into words.","You devote yourself intensely to projects that hold meaning for you.","Your need to understand everyone's motives can become a genuine strategic advantage.","When you place trust in others, your commitment adds depth to teamwork.","Strong intuition becomes more useful when tested against facts before guiding your choices.","Behind your reserve lies a tenacious mind, capable of handling difficulties methodically.","Complex situations stimulate your desire to look beyond appearances.","Your determination goes further when it allows others the freedom to advance in their own way."],"love":["Your emotional intensity draws you towards sincere, profound connections.","You give trust carefully; mutual confidence develops at its own pace.","Your need for honesty in conversation can go hand in hand with gentle listening.","When an emotion passes through you, finding words for it can bring you closer rather than push people away.","A solid relationship doesn't require knowing every thought the other person has.","Behind your apparent restraint lies a great capacity to be present.","Shared memories nourish your attachment without needing to define the present.","Your loyalty finds its full meaning when paired with mutual freedom."],"wellbeing":["Your intensity benefits from places where nothing requires an immediate response.","You like to understand your surroundings; a walk can also be enjoyed without interpretation.","The calm of a familiar place helps you feel grounded again.","When thoughts become persistent, some time away from conversations can give them space.","A creative activity can offer your inner depth a peaceful outlet.","Behind your vigilance, the simple pleasure of monitoring nothing deserves a place.","Frank conversations with loved ones may lighten silences that feel too heavy.","Your need for solitude works best when it remains a choice rather than a compulsory retreat."],"wisdom":["Your strength also reveals itself in what you choose to release.","You can seek the truth without demanding to know everything.","Secrecy sometimes protects; trust often brings people closer.","When intuition opens up to dialogue, it becomes understanding.","Deep feelings need not govern every decision.","Behind mistrust may lie a sincere longing for connection.","The most fruitful silences hide nothing; they offer rest.","Understanding doesn't require controlling."],"roast":["Your talent for spotting unspoken things can make you search for meaning where none exists.","You protect your inner world so carefully that your intentions sometimes become difficult to read.","A past disagreement takes up a lot of space when you keep it without discussing it.","When an answer seems vague, your curiosity risks turning into an interrogation.","A strong intuition isn't always evidence, however convincing it feels.","Behind your desire to understand, the need to control everything can wear conversations down.","Not every secret you keep needs an extra lock.","Your loyalty to first impressions improves when you give new explanations a chance."]},"funny":{"career":["At work, you notice a renamed file before anyone else. Three colleagues then discover their routine meeting has become an official investigation.","You investigate a diary change as if an international mystery had just begun.","The smallest confidential document receives the sort of attention usually reserved for a vault.","When a colleague says 'I'll explain later', you've already opened a file entitled 'why later?'.","A simple filing error sends you down a trail leading to three old meetings.","Behind your calm desk, your mind assembles clues with the patience of a detective.","Whispered conversations intrigue you so much that even the corridor plant becomes a suspect.","Your powers of observation are formidable: you know who moved your pen before they've put it down.","A colleague moved a meeting by fifteen minutes. You've already written the timeline and identified three plausible motives.","Office memo: the team's new password isn't a puzzle. You approached it like a safe to crack anyway.","You know the meeting room's habits better than its timetable. The diary has decided to keep a few secrets.","'Who changed this file?' 'Nobody knows.' You're already inspecting the version history, imaginary torch in hand."],"love":["Your intense gaze can turn 'what shall we eat?' into a scene of great suspense.","You retain the smallest conversation details with a memory that would impress an archivist.","A simple 'I'll call you back' makes your heart beat faster than expected. Your gaze grows so intense the phone seems to look for somewhere to hide.","When someone entrusts you with a secret, you mentally lock it in a safe with several keys.","You enjoy dates full of mystery. When someone plans a surprise, your smile suggests you've already considered twelve romantic scenarios.","Behind your mysterious manner, you fondly remember a compliment received at just the right time.","Very short messages make you thoughtful: 'all right' might contain an entire plot, in your view.","Your affection resembles a gripping novel with a discreet hero who already knows the chapter's ending.","Your intense gaze turns a three-second exchange into a film scene. The person opposite was only looking for the salt.","You adore profound declarations, particularly when they begin with eight bars of silence. The coffee cools while waiting for the opening line.","Jealousy drops in for a lightning visit: you spot a smile, then remember everyone is allowed to be polite.","You take someone's hand with the intensity of a romantic novel. They discreetly check whether you know how the book ends."],"wellbeing":["You choose the park's most secluded bench to enjoy the quiet. A pigeon approaches and your solitude has its first guest.","You want a quiet evening, but the neighbour moving a chair has just created a mystery.","The novel you take to relax contains ten secrets. You feel entirely at home.","A room with the curtains closed feels wonderfully restful. You've found a peace there that the ceiling light wasn't invited to comment on.","A hot cup accompanies your thoughts; it has no idea it's being silently questioned.","Behind your need for solitude, a blanket and an old television series form a trusted team.","Jigsaws soothe you, as long as nobody has deliberately hidden the final piece.","Your ideal relaxation contains no surprises. So you check under the cushion twice.","Your favourite place to unwind resembles a fairy-tale hideout. The only creature allowed in is the dimmable lamp.","To relax, you close the curtains and leave the world outside. The phone receives an official invitation to stay silent.","You've found a deserted terrace where you can recharge. Two empty chairs are enough to make you feel you own a secret castle.","Fake inner forecast: peaceful fog, perfect shady corner and a high chance of answering 'enjoying the quiet' from another room."],"wisdom":["Your intuition occasionally needs a holiday; the toaster isn't a suspect.","You can ask a question without arranging an interrogation room.","Mystery is fascinating, but not every envelope conceals a conspiracy.","Turning the page is easier when you agree not to write a fourteen-chapter preface.","A confidence doesn't necessarily need a six-digit secret code.","Behind every silence there isn't a revelation; sometimes someone's simply chewing.","Transformation sometimes means changing a story's ending. You can leave the old characters out of the new chapter.","Trust doesn't always require checking the safe's lock.","Forgiveness doesn't erase history; it just prevents you rereading it over every breakfast.","You can become a new person without holding a farewell ceremony for every old habit.","A turned page doesn't cease to exist. It simply stops acting as a bookmark for every page after it.","Renewal sometimes means opening the windows of a room you preferred to keep in the shadows."],"roast":["You still remember who moved your mug at a party last year. The mug, meanwhile, has moved on.","You keep secrets so well that even their owners forget telling you.","The slightest 'seen' without a reply becomes chapter one of a spy novel.","When someone says 'it's nothing', you immediately prepare a map of suspects.","An old grudge occupies a box labelled with an extremely precise date.","A mildly teasing remark comes back to you at every family gathering. The speaker forgot it before dessert ended.","Surprises are hard with you: you're already questioning the ribbon on the gift.","You're so discreet that the mysterious neighbour in a novel finds you rather closed off.","Your memory preserves petty slights more accurately than a calendar. The diary missed a meeting; you didn't.","You say 'no problem' with the calm of someone who has just engraved the problem on a memorial plaque.","You've forgiven a friend's lateness. You merely remind them of the achievement whenever a clock strikes.","A joke annoyed you ages ago. The group has moved on; you're preparing the closing speech."]},"piquant":{"career":["Your suspicion turns shared coffee into an intelligence operation. Sugar has been listed as a possible accomplice.","You examine a simple timetable change as though power were being transferred in secret. The diary requests a lawyer.","The colleague who writes 'let's discuss tomorrow' has just started a twelve-hour investigation. Tomorrow hasn't even begun.","When information escapes you, you open a special task force. The secret was about biscuit choices.","A closed-door meeting awakens your detective instinct. They were discussing chair maintenance.","Behind your strategic calm, an invisible file catalogues the team's sighs. The photocopier tops the list.","Your strategy is three moves ahead, with four theories and a discreet exit. The project in question only needed a folder renamed.","You studied the photocopier's movements like an intelligence network. Its only secret operation was running out of paper.","You've anticipated three management decisions before breakfast. Management was only looking for a room with enough sockets.","Your office strategy resembles an intelligence operation. The secret chamber held a supply of blue pens.","Breaking news: a file has been moved. You mobilised a crisis unit, then found it in the folder marked 'moved files'.","Fake security report: you know every office secret. Only one mystery remains unsolved: the purpose of Friday meetings."],"love":["Your intensity turns a simple 'see you later' into a sensitive case. The word 'later' is under surveillance.","You claim to trust people, then check whether their planned surprise really is a surprise. The wrapping paper requests legal counsel.","A message without a full stop intrigues you as much as one with it. Punctuation is summoned either way.","When someone says 'I had a good day', you hold their gaze as though they've revealed an ancient secret. They were just being affectionate.","An old remark remains carefully archived in your memory. It has a reference number and a review date.","Your jealousy turns a smile to the waiter into a silent opera scene. The waiter was simply collecting the plates.","Confidences touch you, but your solemn expression immediately classifies them 'top secret'. Tenderness awaits clearance.","Your heart loves depth; even a casual chat about the weather can end with the clouds under interrogation.","Your stare could lend dramatic depth to an ordinary bread order. The baker thought she was in a romantic thriller.","You call it intense affection. The other person feels they're walking through a corridor of meaningful looks just to choose a mug.","'Does this person know you?' 'Barely.' Yet your eyebrow has just published an entire novel about that reply.","Your jealousy settles in quietly, like a mysterious character in the back of a restaurant. Then it mentally occupies every table."],"wellbeing":["Your need for control turns a peaceful walk into a patrol. The pigeons are suspected of coordination.","You seek calm in an empty room, then wonder why it's empty. The chair is asked for an alibi.","You booked an hour of solitude in a dark room. The smallest ray beneath the door is treated as an uninvited guest.","You say you love silence, then choose a corner so secret even the armchair doesn't know it's hosting you. Peace keeps its anonymity.","A quiet herbal tea seems suspiciously too quiet. The teabag is subjected to thorough questioning.","Behind your silence, theories clash over the precise reason for the neighbour's last sigh. The clock refuses to testify.","Days without surprises worry you almost more than the others. The calendar hides beneath its cover.","Your way of recharging is to vanish quietly from the sitting room. Three rooms away, you declare your hideout a sovereign zone of silence.","You love solitude so much you're thinking of giving it a second bedroom. The first has been classified confidential.","Customer review: 'Lovely resting place, but the occupant communicates solely by moving the curtains.' Silence earns five stars.","You turned off every light to find peace. The beam coming under the door was expelled for excessive familiarity.","Your relaxation corner holds more mystery than an old castle. Its great secret: a cup of tea and the wish to see absolutely nobody."],"wisdom":["Forgiveness sometimes means removing a stone from the road. You started by requiring a complete plan of the new landscape.","You don't search for answers: you subject chance to an interrogation.","A mystery doesn't always conceal betrayal. Sometimes it's just a closed drawer.","Changing means stopping repainting a closed door. You've ordered colour samples for its next life.","A brilliant intuition doesn't automatically make a reliable witness. The jury awaits proof.","Rebirth isn't repeating the same scene with darker scenery. You're already preparing the new curtains.","Secrets can keep themselves. You built them a bunker anyway.","Trusting someone doesn't mean hiring a detective to monitor the trust.","Forgiving isn't endorsing the old script. You insisted on seeing the full credits before changing films.","Rebirth begins when an old version of you stops directing the next. You left it in the director's chair.","Changing your life sometimes requires opening a door. You're still studying the symbolism of the handle.","You can't become free by living forever in an old scene. You've redecorated, but kept the same set."],"roast":["Your grudges are so carefully filed that they have an archives service and a public reception desk.","You trust people the way a vault trusts a lost key.","You kept a trivial remark for three seasons. Its author has changed phones; your grudge still has the old number.","When someone says 'surprise', you immediately hunt for the information leak. The gift is still wrapped.","You forget no slight: your memory preserves them like limited editions. The reconciliation shelves are almost empty.","An ill-timed joke entered your collection of historical grievances. The person was already laughing about something else; you're on volume two.","Secrets love your company: they get a plaque, a code and visiting hours.","Your forgiveness resembles release on probation. Even the moved chair remains under surveillance.","Your grudge has a commemorations calendar. A remark about the weather now gets its own remembrance day.","You forgave a tiny slight; you've mentioned it at every meeting for three years. Forgiveness has become your official announcement.","You're not resentful, you say. That would be too simple. You're the volunteer curator of a museum of clumsy remarks.","An innocent joke aged in your memory like a historical document. The archives refused to classify it as a major event."]},"roastMy":["Scorpio, you don't listen to conversations: you build case files. A pause, a glance and a missing comma become evidence. Someone asks where the napkins are. You demand the witnesses' names.","Your memory for slights resembles the national archives, except nothing is ever closed without further action. You remember a comment about your playlist on a rainy Tuesday. The speaker has no idea proceedings exist. The forgiveness department is closed for stocktaking.","You say you love mysteries. In fact, you suspect each mystery of hiding another mystery that hides yet more. You investigate a closed door. It turns out to be a cupboard, which now refuses to receive you without a witness.","Your intense gaze makes the café waiter feel they're being formally questioned. They only wanted to know whether you'd prefer a window seat. You reply after checking the exits. The waiter has requested a transfer to the counter.","You grant trust with all the generosity of a bank vault on a public holiday. To earn a confidence, someone needs a key, a code and a reference. Once the bond is formed, you guard everything with impressive loyalty. Even the goldfish must sign a confidentiality agreement.","You love understanding everything, especially when nobody is hiding anything. Someone replies 'yes' and you analyse their tone, response time and lack of emoji. Your inquiry concludes there's a major secret. They simply meant yes.","Your calm sometimes worries inanimate objects. You stare at a spilled cup with the seriousness of an international investigator. The table is questioned, the tea towel suspected, the coffee refuses a reconstruction. The cat gets immunity for lack of evidence.","You insist you've turned the page. It's true: you turned it, added a bookmark and kept a copy. Three seasons later, a similar remark reopens the case. The court of memories sits behind closed doors.","Your need for secrecy turns a surprise afternoon snack into a classified mission. You reveal neither time nor place nor plate colour. Guests arrive separately, having received coded instructions. The cake just wants a normal invitation.","You love profound relationships, but a harmless question quickly takes on historic dimensions. Someone asks how your day went and you reply with a meaningful silence. They wait for more. Even the silence demands an accredited interpreter.","Scorpio, you took part in a team treasure trail. You knew all the discreet paths, side exits and ways round obstacles. Everyone admired your strategic instincts. Then they discovered you were looking for a puzzle that wasn't on the sheet.","You'd decided to have a light-hearted evening with friends. A small remark raised your eyebrow, but you carried on laughing as though nothing had happened. Two weeks later you repeated the exact words and intonation. The evening was over; your memory was offering a repeat broadcast.","Your need for peace is so refined that you can turn a simple journey into a territory of chosen solitude. You pick the least talkative seat, silence your phone and gaze out without a word. A friend suggests a game. You agree, provided the cards know how to keep quiet.","You love sincere conversations, especially deep ones. Someone mentions moving a lamp, and you invite them to explain what the change reveals about their aspirations. They think seriously for a minute. They only wanted to move a lamp, now promoted to a symbol of personal transformation.","You tried to draw a line under an old irritation. You wrote it on paper, folded the paper and put it in a box to mark the chapter's end. It was almost poetic. Then you labelled the box 'do not reopen unless further clarification is required'."]},"sagittarius":{"classic":{"career":["Your love of freedom brings fresh energy to projects that call for breaking with routine.","An ambitious idea sometimes needs a more precise route to reach its goal.","Your characteristic honesty becomes stronger when expressed at the right moment.","When routine weighs on your motivation, seek an opportunity to learn within your responsibilities.","Your contagious enthusiasm can help a team see broader possibilities.","Behind your urge to move quickly lies a valuable ability to connect distant ideas.","At work, your need for autonomy works best alongside clearly defined commitments.","Exploring a new method can feed creativity without scattering your efforts."],"love":["Your need for space doesn't rule out sincere presence with the people who matter.","Honest words can bring people closer when they also make room for listening.","Your natural spontaneity brings freshness to affectionate exchanges.","When the urge to go elsewhere arises, sharing that desire opens a deeper conversation.","Your natural optimism can light up a relationship without obscuring quieter feelings.","Behind your love of adventure, you also seek bonds that respect your momentum.","Within a relationship, trust gives everyone room to breathe without constant explanations.","Accepting a pace different from your own can enrich a precious connection."],"wellbeing":["Your travelling spirit finds balance in a walk without a fixed destination.","A break between projects helps your enthusiasm last without burning out.","Freedom can also take the form of an afternoon with no plans.","When your mind races towards tomorrow, pay attention to what surrounds you now.","Your love of discovery can be satisfied by somewhere nearby that you barely know.","Behind your need for movement, peaceful sleep deserves a place too.","Amid countless possibilities, sometimes choose the simplicity of a moment together.","Deliberately slowing down doesn't narrow your horizons; it lets you take in the view."],"wisdom":["Your freedom grows when it knows how to keep a promise.","A distant horizon begins by noticing the path beneath your feet.","Honesty has greater value when it leaves a door open.","Every adventure gains meaning when it makes room for coming home.","Your optimism travels further with a few bearings than with promises alone.","Exploration doesn't always mean leaving; listening can be enough.","True enthusiasm respects the pace of those accompanying you.","Nothing shrinks the world quite like believing you already understand it."],"roast":["Your thirst for freedom sometimes makes you mistake all organisation for needless restriction.","An enthusiastic promise deserves more than a hazy memory of being made.","The truth comes easily to you, but sometimes arrives without careful packaging.","When a conversation grows serious, your mind is already looking for another window to open.","Your admirable optimism occasionally forgets to check the practical details.","Behind your desire for novelty, certain projects are simply awaiting completion.","At the first tightly scheduled plan, you seem to search for an emergency exit.","Setting off towards new ideas appeals more than returning to finish yesterday's."]},"funny":{"career":["Your need for adventure turns the trip between two desks into an expedition. You've already named the corridor 'Discovery Route'.","A planning meeting inspires a brilliant idea: leave before it starts. The calendar isn't impressed.","Your honesty compels you to announce that the presentation has forty slides too many. You've only counted the first two.","When someone asks for an action plan, you produce a map of the world. The team merely wanted to move a printer.","Your enthusiasm leads you to accept five projects before lunch. By afternoon, you're considering a new career as a tour guide.","Working remotely from an unfamiliar terrace, you join the meeting with an office background. The seagulls haven't signed a confidentiality agreement.","The word 'procedure' makes you instinctively scan the exits. Even the office rules find it a bit dramatic.","Exploring possibilities fascinates you: you've turned a task tracker into a catalogue of imaginary destinations.","Office memo: your contribution to meetings must last five minutes. You spend the first four explaining why the meeting should be held elsewhere.","You're asked to summarise a workshop. You return with plans for an international conference and three enthusiastic slogans.","Your office has a world time-zone map to arrange calls. Colleagues discover you're never in the same time zone as last week.","'Can you promise a sensible deadline?' 'Of course!' You merely forgot to ask which year they meant."],"love":["Your need for freedom is so romantic that your dinner invitation includes an 'unknown destination' option.","A declaration of affection comes naturally, just before you suggest changing continents for the weekend.","You suggest an evening together, then add a clause: either of you may change the plan at any moment. Romance has put on sensible shoes.","When you say 'let's improvise', loved ones discreetly check their passports are valid.","A weekend away together with no schedule delights you. Your companion discovers 'no schedule' mainly means no return time.","Your idea of a solid relationship includes two keys, two diaries and an always-open door. You forgot to specify in which direction.","At the restaurant, you describe your ideal future: plenty of space, no routine and puddings to share.","Promising an evening without surprises seems perfectly sensible to you. You've merely booked a secret activity after dinner.","You love relationships that allow breathing space. You've even reserved a diary slot called 'spontaneity together'.","At the first suggestion of a couple's holiday, you propose two separate routes that meet for dessert. Odd organisation, but the pudding is shared.","The word 'forever' sounds lovely until it comes with a fixed meeting time.","Your romantic declaration fits on a postcard: 'I choose you'. On the back, you've drawn three hiking trails."],"wellbeing":["Your ideal relaxation resembles an improvised hike. The sofa is demanding a chance to join in.","A ten-minute stroll becomes a tour of three neighbourhoods, with a detour because 'that street looked interesting'.","A nap feels too stationary. You suggest taking one on a train, to get two things done at once.","When advised to slow down, you immediately ask in which direction.","Your morning enthusiasm makes you throw open the windows as though announcing the start of a grand adventure.","Behind your longing to escape lies a simple truth: you could just move the armchair.","At the moment you should be resting, you play a video about a distant country. Three hours later, the itinerary is ready.","Fresh air does you good. You return with six travel ideas and no idea what time it is.","Your suitcase remains half open 'just in case'. Inside are a water bottle, a jumper and an urge to walk across town.","A bench in the fresh air was meant to host your break. You preferred the path continuing over the hill.","You try a quiet day at home. By noon you've toured the neighbourhood and said hello to two railway stations.","Your ideal forecast involves wind, miles and a good excuse to change your shoes."],"wisdom":["The world's finest philosophy sometimes boils down to a simple question: have you finished what you started?","A promise is a memory best written down before you set off.","The truth lands more gracefully when it doesn't charge through the door.","Every horizon deserves a visit; the laundry is waiting its turn too.","Your optimism could move mountains, but it can't find your keys.","Exploring the world is noble; finding your charger is too.","Adventure sometimes begins by reading the time of your appointment.","Nothing forbids spontaneity, not even an open diary.","A grand idea is better when it survives the first small detail.","Wise people see far ahead. They also check their shoelaces before leaving.","Life is full of possibilities. Some are discreetly labelled 'to be completed'.","Your philosophy opens doors; sometimes check whether they lead into a room."],"roast":["You accepted dinner, a concert and a games night for the same Friday. Your diary reads like a novel missing its final chapter.","An invitation with a precise time already seems far too authoritarian.","You describe your weekend plans so confidently that friends have already written 'subject to a change of universe'.","When you promise 'five minutes', everyone understands 'perhaps this quarter'.","Every new invitation gets a yes before you check the previous three. Your calendar has switched to fiction mode.","Behind your rejection of routine hides a very regular routine: fleeing routine.","Your favourite phrase is 'I'll keep you posted'. The post went hiking and hasn't been heard from since.","You love leaving without knowing your destination. Returning without the shopping is less popular with everyone else.","You promise to drop by 'like the wind'. The wind arrived, left a message and was more punctual.","Your friends no longer confirm invitations: they wait to see which fresh adventure wins the evening's election.","A simple afternoon snack was meant to last an hour. You added a walk, an unplanned visit and an apology to the snack.","You can forget where you're supposed to meet while remembering perfectly the brilliant idea that replaced the appointment."]},"piquant":{"career":["You announce decisions in meetings like a breaking-news presenter. The minutes discover the consequences as they're being printed.","Precise instructions make you want to revolutionise the department. You were only asked to rename a file. The file has requested asylum.","Honesty is your speciality: you announce that the project is ridiculous before reading page one. The page is preparing its official response.","When you're given a file, your enthusiasm immediately sets off in search of another. The first has been reported missing in action.","Your enthusiasm promises a magnificent delivery. Then you discover the 'work required' section and suggest another launch ceremony.","You pitch nomadic remote work as the answer to everything. The team learns your time zone is now a daily surprise.","At the first request for minutes, you proclaim your desk's independence. The office supplies demand a referendum.","Exploring feels nobler than finishing. Your 'brilliant ideas' folder has opened a museum of missing conclusions.","Breaking news: you promised a 'quick and simple' project. The brief has discovered those words were fictional characters.","You work remotely from a train and call it flexibility. The connection is joining the journey without a return ticket.","'Has the plan been approved?' 'In spirit, yes.' Your spirit apparently forgot to inform the people expected to carry it out.","You enter a meeting with a brutal truth and leave with five unplanned tasks. Your honesty works like a machine for generating follow-up work."],"love":["Your freedom always comes before appointments. Even your calendar has to book an appointment to approach you.","Romantic promises slip out as easily as formal speeches. The commitments department is looking for your address.","You regard exclusivity as an optional relationship feature. Curiously, the other person would like to read the terms before clicking.","When a relationship asks for a simple meeting time, you see an international treaty. Negotiations are still stuck on the word 'Thursday'.","You book a romantic outing, then leave three exit routes 'just in case'. It's less a date than an evacuation drill.","Behind your adventurous charm lies a small-print clause: availability subject to weather and current whim.","At the word 'habit', you imagine an emergency response unit. They were talking about breakfast together.","Promising to be predictable for five minutes takes enormous effort. Your timer ran away before minute three.","Your ideal relationship: plenty of affection, few obligations and a tastefully decorated emergency exit. Even the evacuation plan is romantic.","Your grand romantic gesture is a flexible ticket. The words 'non-refundable' feel like a personal insult.","Official notice: your heart accepts closeness, provided it retains a degree of autonomy even a satellite would find excessive.","You adore 'us', provided it never replaces 'I do what I want'. That's not a relationship; it's border negotiations."],"wellbeing":["Your inability to sit still turns a break into a reconnaissance mission. The park bench demands compensation for disruption.","A day without plans seems suspicious. You design a route to confirm that you're genuinely free.","Relaxation interests you as long as it happens somewhere else. Your armchair has hired a detective to find its owner.","When someone recommends a peaceful stroll, you rush towards the most distant trail. The word 'peaceful' has handed in its badge.","Your relaxation plan starts with a walk, becomes an excursion and ends at a railway station. Rest missed its connection.","Behind your obsession with elsewhere, even an open window looks like a territorial expansion campaign.","At bedtime, you study a map 'to switch off'. Your pillow has just applied for a passport.","Slowing down is so incompatible with your reputation that you call rest 'horizontal exploration'. The sofa refuses the press release.","Your suitcase has a special compartment for spontaneous decisions. It takes up half the house.","You call a trip requiring three transport changes a 'nature break'. The garden bench has officially been downgraded.","Fake inner forecast: persistent restlessness, high chance of scenic detours. The armchair no longer appears on the map.","You buy a guide to peaceful walks. Three pages in, you're already planning to cross the country."],"wisdom":["Your philosophy always sees the glass as half full. Especially when you've forgotten whose job it was to fill it.","Thinking big doesn't exempt you from finishing small things. Your theory has a magnificent gate and no garden.","Unqualified optimism is a postcard posted from a building site that's still closed.","A philosophical certainty isn't proof. Your enthusiasm has already framed the conclusion.","Your optimism owns a world map and no return address.","Exploring without finishing is like collecting beginnings in glass cases.","Adventure isn't avoiding you: it's waiting for you to confirm the time.","Nothing ties you down as tightly as your theatrical rejection of timetables.","Your optimism finds a horizon in every wall. It might help to tell a window from a poster.","The greatness of ideas isn't measured by exclamation marks. Your philosophy has installed a siren anyway.","You search for life's meaning with the confidence of a guide whose map is still blank.","Hope is precious. Turning it into a guarantee is more the marketing department of your convictions."],"roast":["You confirm you'll attend with spectacular enthusiasm. Two hours later, a mysterious activity has 'called' you. Everyone suspects your imagination owns a phone.","A simple reservation seems an attack on fundamental rights. The restaurant has referred the case to imaginary authorities.","You promise not to forget anything this time. The phrase already appears on four abandoned invitations.","When you announce 'I'll be there', even your watch bursts out laughing. The time zone demands an investigation.","Your diary has more ellipses than actual appointments kept. The three little dots have earned permanent positions.","You have a brilliant idea for every Saturday. Last Saturday's idea is still waiting in the rain with an entire cake.","At the first form, you shout about administrative dictatorship. You only had to write your name.","You love leaving, fear staying and find returning boring. Even your doormat no longer recognises its employer.","You've just cancelled dinner for 'a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity'. It's the third one this week. The dictionary is preparing a revision.","Your 'I'll take care of it' is an oral legend. Historians are still searching for a verifiable example.","Every novelty replaces your plans. You don't have a diary; you hold permanent auditions for the role of Saturday.","You begin five adventures and promise updates on each. The group chat has become a museum of first photographs."]},"roastMy":["Sagittarius, you love freedom so much that even your alarm clock needs permission. You accept three invitations with historic enthusiasm. When the day comes, you go somewhere else 'on instinct'. The invitations have founded an association for victims of your diary.","Your suitcase is ready even though your shopping list never is. You plan an imaginary journey while someone asks you to buy bread. You return with a story about scenic detours. The bakery is preparing a missing-item notice.","Your honesty bursts into conversations like a removal lorry without an appointment. You say exactly what you think, then explain for twenty minutes why it was brave. The others only asked about a tablecloth. The tablecloth has demanded a right of reply.","Sagittarius, you make promises with the sincerity of a historic speech. Two hours later, you discover a new passion and change direction. Your commitments meet monthly to try and locate you. Attendance is now listed as optional.","Your optimism could declare 'excellent news' in front of a locked door. You'd find a window, then a path, then a way to call it an adventure. The door merely wanted you to read 'pull'. A committee has opened an inquiry into your practical sense.","You hate rules, especially those you suggested yesterday. Your plan for today says 'follow inspiration'. At noon, inspiration leaves without warning. Your task list now publishes a schedule of disappearances.","Your need for space turns the smallest commitment into a diplomatic incident. Asked to confirm dinner, you invoke the independence of your spirit. Nobody is trying to imprison you. It's a table for four.","You philosophise about life's meaning while the oven beeps. Your lecture travels through freedom, destiny and forgotten civilisations. Dinner has been waiting half an hour. It's just been granted the status of an unwilling audience member.","You adore new beginnings, unknown roads and enormous ideas. Finishing anything seems much less poetic. Your shelf holds twenty half-used notebooks and one completely worn-out pen. The pen demands a medal for services rendered.","Sagittarius, your spontaneity has an official statement: 'Nothing is planned; anything is possible.' You arrive late, suggest another venue and announce a wonderful detour. Your friends don't need a guide. They need a travel-coordination task force.","You love announcing grand adventures before you've found your shoes. At work, a short meeting becomes a manifesto for distant horizons. In love, you promise a presence free from constraints. Your one constant is the question mark beside your name on invitations.","Your enthusiasm has already booked three activities before anyone chooses the day. You suggest a romantic escape where each person is free to change countries. To relax, you hit the road without checking the distance. Your satnav now displays 'personal adventure' instead of an arrival time.","You explain life with the confidence of a philosopher on a world tour. Then you forget the anniversary of a project whose launch speech you gave. Your friends no longer worry about your changing plans. They've simply renamed you 'maybe' in their contacts.","At work, you say aloud what others haven't had time to think. In a relationship, you negotiate every Sunday's independence. Your idea of rest is discovering a new path. You're proof someone can move constantly without ever finishing a single form.","You promised a quiet outing and prepared a list of 'optional' detours. Your energy makes the journey an epic, then makes the epic an excuse to suggest something else. You have an entire philosophy about seizing the moment. Oddly, the moment you were supposed to confirm the appointment is nowhere to be found."]},"capricorn":{"classic":{"career":["Your perseverance gives complex projects a structure everyone can rely on.","An ambitious goal benefits from being divided into realistic, clearly shared steps.","Your characteristic rigour helps distinguish what matters from passing emergencies.","When results are slow to arrive, remember the value of the journey already travelled.","Your sense of responsibility can inspire confidence, provided you leave room for other people's initiatives.","Beneath your seriousness lies a deep ambition: to build something lasting.","At work, delegating some of the details can free your attention for important decisions.","Building a project patiently sometimes takes as much flexibility as discipline."],"love":["Your emotional reserve often conceals great consistency in everyday gestures.","A solid bond also grows through spontaneous moments with no goal to achieve.","Your loyalty to commitments lends depth to relationships that matter.","When words seem inadequate, a heartfelt gesture can communicate a great deal.","Your need for security can coexist with the pleasure of discovering new sides to someone.","Beneath your apparent restraint, feelings deserve a place that cannot be measured.","In moments of closeness, you don't always need to solve what the other person shares.","Sharing an unplanned moment can bring you closer to those who appreciate your presence."],"wellbeing":["Your sense of duty deserves breaks that aren't treated as rewards to be earned.","A peaceful moment can be precious even when it produces no visible result.","Discipline supports you, but doesn't demand that every minute be occupied.","When your mind anticipates the entire week, gently return to the rhythm of your breathing.","Your love of organisation can help you protect time for proper rest.","Beneath your ambition, give importance to pleasures without measurable usefulness.","Amid your commitments, a walk without a watch may offer a different relationship with time.","Slowing down doesn't erase your determination; it helps keep it steady."],"wisdom":["Your worth amounts to more than your list of achievements.","A summit keeps its meaning when you know how to admire the view.","A project's strength is also measured by its ability to evolve.","Every task deserves a place; rest does too.","Ambition can grow without filling your entire horizon.","Building the future doesn't mean missing the present.","Trust grows differently from constant monitoring.","Nothing lasting is built by forgetting those who share the journey."],"roast":["Your taste for control can turn modest surprises into problems demanding immediate solutions.","A personal goal may eventually occupy all the space reserved for enjoying life.","Your rigour serves you so well that accepting a simple approximation becomes difficult.","When someone suggests a spontaneous outing, your first instinct is to check the diary.","Your reflex for evaluating returns sometimes makes you examine leisure as another assignment.","Beneath your serious expression, it's hard to tell when you truly allow yourself a break.","At the slightest change of plan, you immediately look for whoever will update the schedule.","Organising every detail reassures you, but sometimes leaves little space for happy accidents."]},"funny":{"career":["Your career plan already includes your next role, the one after that and your acceptance speech. You're still undecided on the binder colour.","A colleague suggests a spontaneous idea. You reply with such a detailed reverse schedule that their spontaneity now has a delivery date.","The meeting starts with three goals. You've prepared a spreadsheet to track the spreadsheet's goals.","When the office runs short of pens, you launch an inquiry into quarterly consumption. The blue pen refuses to testify.","Your activity report excites you so much that you're considering having it bound for guests.","Below your screen, sticky notes are arranged by priority. Even 'urgent' has a ranking number.","The moment everyone celebrates finishing the project, you suggest a meeting on how to improve the celebration.","Planning your career soothes you: the job you're targeting in ten years is already bookmarked.","Your ambition fits into five columns and three meetings. Someone dared write 'to be decided' in the last; you've called a workshop about the phrase.","You prepare for your annual review with the efficiency of a space launch. The rocket is powered by a skills spreadsheet.","'Do you have a plan for tomorrow?' 'For the next seven years, yes.' The question felt rather short.","Your presentation ends with 'next steps'. You had to add ten slides explaining why that step isn't the last."],"love":["Your romance comes in the form of a confirmed booking, a spare umbrella and an optimised route.","A romantic surprise delights you, provided it arrives in your calendar three days early.","Tenderness makes you generous: you've already compared the warranties on possible gifts.","When asked what you feel, you first reply 'it's serious'. The rest arrives after approval.","This candlelit dinner inspires a spreadsheet of the best venues. Pudding has its own column.","Beneath your calm, you're preparing a touching declaration. The document is called 'final version 7'.","At the beginning of a romance, you're already planning the weekends. The other person was merely looking for their coat.","Sharing your sofa is a great sign of trust: you've even cleared a space on the armrest.","You express affection by thinking through future details. Your companion discovers they're already in your projected picnic schedule.","You enjoy the first meeting so much you mentally choose the crockery for future anniversaries. You've kept the warranty.","Your favourite term of endearment is 'dependable'. It took you ages to write it on a card decorated with two little flowers.","A spontaneous declaration of love moves you. Then you gently ask whether the lovely idea is intended to last."],"wellbeing":["Your rest begins at precisely 2.00 pm. At 2.03, you check whether it's progressing according to plan.","A walk without a purpose looks suspicious. You end up tracking your progress with an app.","A nap appeals, but you're still comparing fifteen and twenty minutes to maximise returns.","When you take a break, your to-do list records 'break completed' with obvious satisfaction.","Your relaxing moment requires two reminders and a ticked box. The cushion would just like you to sit down.","You've organised an evening with no obligations. At eight o'clock, you tick off 'do nothing' with the seriousness of a project manager.","In the park, you schedule three contemplation stops of equal length. The pigeons respect none of the slots.","Slowing down takes so much effort that you're considering praising yourself in the weekly review.","Your country break comes with an illustrated rest programme. Sunset has yet to sign up for the workshop.","You've devised a method for enjoying holidays more: time how long you spend not timing anything.","The relaxing walk has three stages and an optional break. You're the only walker carrying a tracking spreadsheet.","Your armchair is booked from four to twenty past four. It seems delighted to have an administrative existence at last."],"wisdom":["Your dashboard cannot measure the quality of a good belly laugh.","A Sunday without productivity can still be a perfectly successful Sunday.","What is patiently built often lasts better than something celebrated with a giant ribbon.","Every summit can wait until you've finished your snack.","Your ambition knows how to count; your armchair knows how to welcome.","Building a solid future doesn't forbid losing a sock.","Success doesn't require formal minutes at every lunch.","There's no evidence a break should have to produce receipts.","You reach a summit step by step. Nothing prevents you admiring a flower along the way.","Perseverance is a talent; it doesn't require climbing every step on the doorstep.","Patience builds bridges. Be careful not to install a tollbooth in the middle.","Even a mountain takes its time. Yet it never writes a growth report."],"roast":["You calculated the cost of a walk by the number of free steps. The result is favourable, provided you buy nothing.","An unexpected gift makes you smile. You then ask whether the warranty can be transferred.","The phrase 'we'll see how it goes' scares you more than a suspense film.","When someone says 'enjoy the moment', you ask which reporting period the assessment covers.","Your shopping budget includes the biscuit price to the last penny. The biscuit wants to negotiate.","Under your responsible-person uniform, an inner child is still waiting for approval from accounts.","At New Year's Eve, you propose an annual review of enjoyment. The guests pretend not to hear.","At your place, spontaneity only happens on the days it's scheduled.","You know the price of pens individually, in packs and by decade. The free pen has earned your eternal respect.","At the market, you compare the price of apples down to the penny. The seller has given you a calculator instead of a basket.","A three per cent discount is enough to brighten your day. You considered framing the receipt.","For you, a bargain deserves an epic account. Your friends are still waiting for the chapter about the two pounds saved."]},"piquant":{"career":["Your ambition has an organisational chart before it even has an idea. Ideas must now pass an initial interview.","A colleague mentions the weekend; you immediately ask for its productivity rate. Saturday has resigned.","You wrote your five-year plan before learning who was on the team. Your colleagues appear in the appendix 'resources to be confirmed'.","When handed a simple task, you set up a steering committee. The task requests release on bail.","Your five-year plan even includes planned improvisations. Improvisation has appealed against the damage to its reputation.","Beneath your seriousness, the coffee break is an expense to be streamlined. Coffee is drafting a voluntary redundancy plan.","At the first surprise, you demand someone accountable. Chance is waiting to be interviewed by HR.","You like organising the company so much that you've classified smiles by frequency of use. Happiness has lost its access pass.","Your five-year plan has an honours board and an emergency procedure. The present has been hired on a temporary contract.","You turn a fifteen-minute meeting into a strategic committee. The item marked 'hello' has reached consultation stage.","Fake staff survey: 100% of objectives already have a timeline. Colleagues are still looking for their names on the organisation chart.","Your ambition has scheduled its own award ceremony. The results aren't in yet, but the agenda is impeccable."],"love":["Your romantic side begins with a feasibility study. Imaginary butterflies must provide three references.","You imagine love as something built to last. A shame you treat the first date like a building-site inspection.","Tenderness, for you, resembles a carefully negotiated offer. The bouquet requests an appointment with Legal.","When someone suggests an unplanned dinner, you demand an agenda. The candles have gone on strike.","Your cautious heart doesn't open up: it launches a tendering process. Applications closed on Tuesday.","Beneath your emotional restraint, a trust agreement already has twelve clauses. Spontaneity fails the criteria.","A sweet message touches you. You file it under 'proof of seriousness', between the dinner reservation and the next five-year plan.","Sharing your future comes naturally. You've printed the forecast before even choosing pudding.","Your approach to relationships resembles building a lighthouse: solid, forward-looking and slightly excessive for choosing dinner.","You discuss the future on the third date with the gravity of a town planner. Your companion was merely suggesting the cinema.","Your romance contains a continuity-of-service clause. Even the first day's butterflies have been assigned a maintenance schedule.","'Are you thinking about us?' 'Obviously, I've already named the folder.' Tenderness might have deserved a less administrative introduction."],"wellbeing":["Your restful weekend has four compulsory stages and a satisfaction form. The cushion gave up at stage two.","An aimless walk seems inefficient. You propose optimising the route between two trees. The trees reject the merger.","Relaxation arrives with an ID badge and strict hours. It's refused admission without supporting documents.","When relaxation starts, you check your relaxation timetable. The afternoon ends up running behind its own tranquillity.","Your quiet Sunday is planned to the minute. Even the yawn must confirm attendance.","Under your blanket, you check whether you're using your free time correctly. The blanket requests a sabbatical.","At the first hint of boredom, you launch a rest-improvement project. Rest has left the group chat.","You've booked a slot to admire the scenery. By minute three, you suspect the mountain is poorly organised.","You've created a spreadsheet for the ideal holiday. Its first result reads 'error: insufficient spontaneity'.","Your rest session has an agenda and a closing time. Silence has simply declined to attend.","Your leisure forecast: clear skies, high organisational pressure. The nap is hiding behind the calendar.","You've turned a walk into three verifiable tasks. The oldest tree in the park has never seen such an audit."],"wisdom":["Your ambition climbs a mountain and asks for a promotion at the summit.","Patience builds empires. It doesn't turn every pebble into a board of directors.","Caution has opened a consultancy inside your head.","The summit must be earned, says your philosophy. It simply forgot the scenery exists on the way up.","You've confused consistency with the obligation never to loosen your shoelaces.","Building the future is noble; sending it invoices is less so.","Spontaneity does exist: you've filed it under 'unexpected incidents'.","Building for the long term is admirable. Turning every break into a foundation calls for a rather anxious architect.","A summit isn't an office with a better view. Your ambition has nevertheless installed a nameplate.","You cultivate patience like a garden, then measure every leaf with a ruler.","What lasts deserves foundations. There's no need to pour concrete around every smile.","Your philosophy of progress forgot the joy of a detour. The path is straight, but the story is short."],"roast":["Your calendar doesn't list birthdays: it treats them as contractual deadlines. The candles await an invoice.","You compare the price of two desserts while your friends have already ordered coffee. Your final calculation concludes that eating at home was better.","You've been calculating the profitability of your sofa since buying it. The sofa wants royalties for overtime.","When improvisation is mentioned, your gaze summons an emergency committee. The unexpected flees through the emergency exit.","Your discreet heart has more firewalls than a bank network. Compliments are blocked for suspicious activity.","Beneath your seriousness hides a quality manager who assesses even surprises. The surprises request a transfer.","You estimated the cost of every candle before celebrating anything. The cake was replaced by a bar chart of savings.","Organising happiness in a spreadsheet seemed sensible. The 'joy' cell has just returned a formula error.","You compare the cost of an evening out with the memories it might create. The memory seems poor value without a receipt.","Breaking news: you've found a way to save on presents. Your loved ones call it 'a very nice explanation'.","Your piggy bank has its own piggy bank for savings. A third has been appointed head of spending controls.","The word 'free' excites you more than a brass band. You still inspect the terms in tiny print."]},"roastMy":["Capricorn, you don't go on holiday: you roll out an operational plan. The journey, break and even nap all have colour codes. Your loved ones suggest looking at the sea. You ask what strategic objective that would fulfil.","Your ambition is so organised that it already knows the title of your autobiography. You've planned chapters, appendices and publication date. The section on 'times I had fun' is still missing. The editorial department awaits your availability.","You love security, numbers and solid decisions. When someone suggests an impromptu evening, you investigate the hidden costs of joy. The group leaves without you. You then request the incident report.","Capricorn, your calendar has no blank spaces: even blanks are reserved. You've set aside a slot for spontaneity between two reviews. Spontaneity hasn't confirmed its attendance. You send a final reminder.","Your relationship with money resembles a permanent negotiation with every object. A lamp appeals, but you calculate how many smiles it will provide per use. The salesperson asks you to pick a colour. You demand a five-year projection.","You manage to look serious even while watching a comedy. You analyse scene construction and time management. Everyone else laughs. You note that comic efficiency could still improve.","Your romance is reliable but built on an administrative framework. You book, compare, confirm and check the times. Your companion says it's adorable. You ask whether they'd like to sign an acknowledgement of receipt.","Capricorn, you've turned relaxation into a high-performance discipline. You define the length of the walk and the weekend's objectives. On return, you write a review. Your chair demands a holiday away from you.","Your perseverance commands respect, but you never leave a job half-done. The problem is that you also refuse to declare anything finished. Even the shopping list must go before a committee. The committee hasn't got time to shop.","You're the only person who thinks a birthday needs formal minutes. Decorations approved, schedule observed, biscuits distributed exactly. The guests sing for you. You add 'unplanned enthusiasm' to the closing report.","You've already organised your next success with a presentation and three appendices. Romantically, you plan lasting projects before finishing the starter. To relax, you make graphs about free time. Your family has nicknamed your calendar 'the fourth member of the family'.","Capricorn, your goals are so precise that future improvisations have reference numbers. You show tenderness by bringing two umbrellas and a guarantee of punctuality. During a break, you check whether the break is fulfilling its purpose. Your pillow is considering self-employment.","You build projects as others build cathedrals: slowly and with flawless technical documentation. Then you fall in love with an idea and immediately offer it a permanent contract. Your holidays end with a relaxation report. The sunset received a 'compliant' rating.","In your world, a tiny saving becomes a victory recounted in detail. At work, you turn ambition into five years of milestones. In love, loyalty touches you more than grand surprises. You're so consistent your watch checks the time against your diary.","Your relaxation programme looks like a plan to launch a new service. You chose the walk, calculated its duration and prepared a review for the return. Meanwhile, your major work project advances according to schedule. Spontaneous pleasure has been marked 'interesting avenue, to be reassessed'."]},"aquarius":{"classic":{"career":["Your originality opens fresh possibilities when habits seem to limit what can be done.","A bold idea gains reach when translated into steps others can follow.","Your distance from convention helps you question what everyone takes for granted.","When a rule seems pointless, understanding its origins may strengthen your proposal for change.","Your independent spirit finds its greatest power in collaboration where everyone contributes freely.","Behind your unique vision lies a genuine desire to help the group evolve.","At work, your ability to think differently can be precious in moving a stalled situation forwards.","Sharing your insights patiently helps your freshest ideas find their place."],"love":["Your need for independence can coexist with a tender connection freely chosen.","A relationship sometimes grows from unexpected conversations that reveal shared sensitivities.","Your curiosity about others enriches exchanges when paired with genuine attentiveness.","When your feelings remain hidden, a few simple words can make your affection easier to understand.","Your attraction to difference invites you to discover the other person beyond their habits.","Behind your apparent distance, loyalty often reveals itself in original ways.","At the heart of closeness, authenticity matters more than any ready-made model of a relationship.","Respecting different rhythms can create space where everyone feels free and recognised."],"wellbeing":["Your inventive mind also appreciates moments when no new idea is expected.","A walk through familiar surroundings may offer a fresh perspective on everyday life.","The freedom to slow down belongs to you just as much as the freedom to discover.","When thoughts multiply, a simple activity can bring your attention back to the present.","Your love of novelty can be balanced with freely chosen habits of rest.","Behind your need for intellectual stimulation, calm has its place too.","Throughout a busy day, protecting some time away from screens may do you good.","Choosing solitude or a sincere conversation depends on what genuinely restores you."],"wisdom":["Your difference becomes meaningful when it makes space for others' differences.","A rule deserves to be understood before it's replaced.","Novelty is precious only if it makes life more vibrant.","Every free spirit gains from listening without betraying itself.","Independence needn't keep others at a distance.","Thinking differently doesn't mean rejecting what works.","The future also belongs to those who care for the present.","Nothing original requires abandoning simplicity."],"roast":["Your rejection of convention may lead you to challenge habits that didn't really bother you.","A brilliant idea sometimes becomes difficult to follow when you've already invented three more.","Emotional distance protects you, but can also leave loved ones uncertain.","When everyone chooses the same solution, you immediately look for reasons it must be wrong.","Your contrarian spirit sometimes awakens before you've even heard the proposal.","Behind your love of originality, some simple ideas are still waiting for consideration.","The moment a trend becomes popular, your enthusiasm seems to lose some of its shine.","You enjoy refusing to follow the crowd so much that you sometimes refuse your own advice."]},"funny":{"career":["Your imagination suggests replacing meetings with a connected aquarium. The team just wants a coffee break.","The department wants to simplify the coffee machine. You suggest it choose drinks based on the weather. Coffee is now waiting for rain.","Management asks you to follow the protocol. You politely ask who approved the protocol.","When the office changes its chairs, you unveil a self-driving furniture concept. The chair is already going round in circles.","Your visionary mind imagines tomorrow's work. Today's is still waiting in your inbox.","Behind your silence at meetings lies a plan to reinvent the keyboard. You've already removed the 'normal' key.","At a brainstorming session, you suggest replacing chairs with moving platforms. The first volunteer rolled into the corridor.","Sharing discoveries delights you: colleagues receive a lecture on a subject they didn't know existed.","You designed a voice-controlled paperclip dispenser. The team eventually chose a bowl on the table, which talks considerably less.","In a meeting, you propose replacing forms with group drawings. The accountant is still searching for the 'total' box.","An instruction says 'use the template'. You present an entirely redesigned experimental template. The instruction was singular for a reason.","You suggest a keyboard-free day to unleash creativity. IT support is already packing boxes of pencils."],"love":["Your way of loving is unique: you send a fascinating article on jellyfish instead of an ordinary message.","A romantic evening inspires a visit to an exhibition on the future of furniture. Your companion discovers smart chairs.","Distance comes naturally: you reply enthusiastically to the group chat, then forget the personal message.","When someone asks for a spontaneous gesture, you build a machine that dispenses personalised compliments.","Your independent spirit enjoys genuine bonds, as long as the sofa has two separate remotes.","Behind your detached air, you've planned an adorable surprise. It requires assembling a small robot.","At the restaurant, choosing food turns into a debate about the future of eating. The chips wait their turn.","You enjoy watching a series together until everyone loves it. Then you suggest an obscure documentary.","You show affection by sharing a bizarre discovery. Your 'thinking of you' message links to the habits of octopuses.","Your ideal date starts with a long friendship and two independent routes. You meet afterwards to compare your walks.","A long-distance evening suits you so well that you send a drawing of dessert rather than a photo of yours.","'Shall we see each other soon?' 'Of course, in our usual space.' You meant a chatroom, not a room in the flat."],"wellbeing":["Your ideal relaxation means unplugging the screens. You begin by programming an app to remind you.","A stroll through the park becomes a study of pigeons' social behaviour. You already have three hypotheses.","Solitude restores you, but your phone has eight discussion groups devoted to the meaning of freedom.","When you decide to do nothing, you design a new method for doing nothing more efficiently.","Your inventive spirit turns a cup of tea into an experiment on the optimum drinking temperature.","Behind your researcher's curiosity, the cushion is waiting for you to test its main function.","At bedtime, you have a revolutionary idea. Your pillow suggests filing the patent tomorrow.","Slowing down sounds appealing if you can measure the effect with a smartwatch. The watch requests a break.","You bought a connected pebble to help you slow down. It now spends its days searching for Wi-Fi.","An app offers to count moments of calm. You've just spent an hour comparing the counters.","Your new relaxation experiment is listening to forest sounds recorded by a robot. The real park is at the end of the road.","You're testing a lamp that recreates dawn. It switches on at noon, perfectly in keeping with your experimental schedule."],"wisdom":["The future belongs to the bold. That doesn't mean reinventing socks every morning.","An idea for the future can start with finding the remote.","Seeing tomorrow before everyone else is useful, provided you don't forget today's appointment.","Everyone is unique; proving it at every meal is optional.","Freedom loses nothing by accepting a recipe that works.","Innovation doesn't necessarily mean replacing the spoon.","The future begins tomorrow; the washing has been waiting since yesterday.","Nothing forbids doing what everyone else does when everyone else is right.","The next great discovery can wait until you've finished your cup of tea.","Seeing things differently opens the mind; looking at them normally once can save a detour.","The future belongs to inventors. The present appreciates people who put their prototypes away.","Having an idea ahead of its time doesn't mean everyone else has forgotten to read the calendar."],"roast":["Your rejection of normality is so consistent it's beginning to resemble a family tradition.","An idea that works bores you as soon as someone else adopts it. You immediately invent an incomprehensible version.","The conversation is about the weather. You launch into your theory about floating cities.","When you announce 'nobody understands me', everyone asks you to explain your diagram again.","Your rebellious spirit chooses the most original route, even when it leads to the broom cupboard.","Behind your detached manner are forty notifications from friends you adore 'at a distance'.","At a restaurant, you order the most surprising dish. You're then surprised that it's surprising.","Rejecting labels is your speciality. You've invented a new one: 'expert in rejecting labels'.","You claimed you'd discovered music nobody knew. Now it's played everywhere and you find it 'disappointing'.","You say 'I'm not like anyone else' while choosing a mysterious drink. It's water, but in a triangular glass.","The moment your friends adopt a novelty, you explain it's already old news. Your passions have very short expiry dates.","Your favourite outfit is one that prompts a question. When nobody reacts, you explain its concept uninvited."]},"piquant":{"career":["Your need to be different makes you reinvent a tool that works. The replacement needs three training courses and an opening ceremony.","You replaced the office instructions with a twelve-page manifesto. In the final paragraph, you reinvent exactly the original instructions.","Novelty attracts you as long as nobody uses it. The moment your team adopts your idea, you declare it obsolete. The team wants a mediator.","When your manager issues a procedure, you demand the procedure authorising procedures. Legal has closed the blinds.","Your visionary mind is already working on the next decade. Friday's paperwork has reported you missing.","Behind your speeches about teamwork lies one condition: the team must agree with you first. Democracy is under maintenance.","At the first consensus, you become the official opposition. Even your own suggestion has voted against itself.","You propose a coffee machine that collects employees' ideas. It has just filed your project under 'too complicated for an espresso'.","You want to democratise the coffee machine with a voting algorithm. Since then, nobody gets an espresso without attending an assembly.","The boss authorises a simple solution. You publish a manifesto against simplicity, with appendices and a diagram of the revolution.","Your paperless office prototype replaced documents with unreadable QR codes. Filing is more modern, not more useful.","You revolutionise a procedure that already works. The result does exactly the same thing but needs three batteries recharging."],"love":["Your independence has booked two emotional bedrooms, an emergency exit and limited access to feelings. Tenderness awaits its badge.","A declaration of affection embarrasses you less than an ordinary question: 'Have you thought of me?' Your brain prepares a conference.","Emotional distance makes you seem fascinating. You merely discover that others sometimes prefer a reply to their messages.","You present friendship as the pinnacle of romance. The person opposite discovers they've received a membership card instead of a date.","For a date, you choose two different places and suggest writing to each other from afar. Physical proximity remains a paid extra.","Behind your mysterious smile is often a mundane fact: you're thinking about an invention. Romance wasn't informed.","At the first 'let's do what we usually do', you summon a domestic revolution. Dinner only needed plates.","Sharing feelings seems possible through a conceptual presentation. The heart requests a version without slides.","You reserve a special place for someone you love: somewhere between 'best friend' and 'fascinating conversation', fifty miles from daily life.","You love connections without compulsory emotional closeness. The trouble is your messages arrive like postcards from another galaxy.","Your declaration has two parts: 'You matter to me'. Then a full presentation on the benefits of living in separate homes.","You treat physical closeness as a theoretical discussion topic. The other person was simply thinking of holding your hand."],"wellbeing":["You installed a sensor to check whether you're really resting. It mainly records hours spent configuring it.","A peaceful walk seems too conventional. You follow your usual route backwards. The map demands an investigation.","Your relaxation gadget produces ten sounds, three vibrations and a calibration beep. You switched it off to get some peace.","When everyone turns off their phones, you invent a fresh reason to turn yours back on. Flight mode hands in its resignation.","Your futuristic mind wants to optimise sleep with a revolutionary idea. Your lamp merely suggests being switched off.","Behind your detachment, you monitor three groups dedicated to not following groups. Contradiction has signed up for a subscription.","As you breathe the fresh air, you propose a theoretical ventilation model for the park. The trees demand confidentiality.","You're testing a smart-napping app. It wakes you up to congratulate you on not having fallen asleep yet.","Your relaxation bracelet has an instruction manual longer than the week. After three settings, you relax by throwing it in a drawer.","Fake technical bulletin: the rest experiment failed because of the new smart headset. The headset hadn't planned to rest either.","You created a relaxation method with sensors, alerts and dashboards. It has everything except a 'stop' button.","You're testing a remotely controlled miniature fountain. It sends thirty notifications to announce that the water is flowing."],"wisdom":["You see so far into the future that the present resembles a forgotten email attachment.","An incomprehensible idea isn't automatically ahead of its time.","Rebelling against an open door is still a dramatic entrance.","Not everyone is copying you: some people just bought a chair.","Your independence rejects close ties but keeps the group chat bookmarked.","Innovating to avoid an instruction means building it a palace.","The future fascinates you; the present is still awaiting your reply.","Being ahead of your time doesn't guarantee knowing where the door is.","You're a century ahead of your era. Your era, politely, is still waiting for a demonstration.","The future doesn't have to be complicated to be new. Your compass is still trying to work that out.","A brilliant idea lights up tomorrow. Yours sometimes forgets to fit the switch.","You see tomorrow so confidently that today has filed a missing-person report."],"roast":["Your individuality matters so much that you demand an official certificate of originality. The form is identical for everyone.","An ordinary invention becomes 'a paradigm shift' with you. You've just put a label on a box.","Emotional closeness seems suspicious. You love all humanity, as long as it keeps two metres of conversational distance.","When others discover your favourite music, you immediately abandon it. Your player wants a stable identity.","Being different has become your personal brand. Whenever a trend catches up with you, you change your mind before its name is finished.","Behind your love of wild ideas lies a private war against simplicity. The spoon has taken refuge next door.","At the first unanimous agreement, you switch sides. Your former opinions have formed a parliamentary opposition.","Revolutionising the world from your sofa keeps you very busy. The sofa would first like you to find its remote.","You abandoned your favourite passion the day it gained its first admirer. That's less a taste than a chase scene.","Your personality applied for a patent on being unlike anyone else. The patent was refused for lack of novelty.","Breaking news: yesterday's trend you championed has become popular. You've already denounced it in a three-page opinion piece.","You hunt for a fashion nobody's heard of. Once you find it, you leave: it now has a witness."]},"roastMy":["Aquarius, you're not different: you've turned difference into a subscription service. You reject popular tastes, then reject your own as soon as they become popular. Your personality changes its window display every Thursday. Even originality has cancelled its contract.","Your mind invents solutions to problems nobody has. You replace a light switch with an app, then the app with an experimental prototype. The room stays dark. Nevertheless, you announce a historic technological success.","You love everyone, but at a regulated distance. A friend describes their day; you reply with a link on the evolution of societies. They wait for affection. You send them an updated link.","Aquarius, you challenge rules before reading them. You propose a free, innovative, entirely new system. Three pages later, your system contains seventeen rules and a supervisory committee. The old regulations demand rehabilitation.","Your future is already full of fabulous inventions. Your present consists of a missing charger and a stack of papers. You explain that physical objects are an outdated concept. The papers ask for an archivist.","You proclaim your independence with almost ceremonial skill. Someone offers coffee; you refuse because 'everyone does that'. You then prepare an identical drink in a strange glass. The coffee wishes to apply for normality.","Your distant gaze suggests you know a secret about the universe. In fact, you're considering installing a miniature garden on the fridge. Someone asks whether you're all right. You answer with a lecture on vertical farming.","Aquarius, you hate being categorised. Yet you've devised an entire typology of conventional people, daring people and people who don't understand you. Nobody meets your definition of genius. Oddly enough, you reserved that category for yourself.","You always believe you're five years ahead of your time. You suggest a project nobody understands, refuse to simplify it, then declare everyone else behind. Your project isn't revolutionary. It's a toaster with a navigation interface.","Your hunger for novelty turns dinner into a conference on the future. You outline eight ideas, three prototypes and a world without routine. The guests are just looking for salt. You announce that salt will be decentralised from Monday.","Aquarius, you designed a machine to simplify everyday tasks. It requires three connections and the neighbour's permission. In relationships, you prefer to begin with a friendship of cosmic depth. Both the machine and your dates are still awaiting their first use.","Your curiosity creates a wonderful future filled with inventions nobody considered. You give someone a connected gadget to wish them a nice day. The gadget spends the evening updating itself. Your affection is real enough, but it forgot to include the cable.","At work, you propose replacing a procedure with a radically new idea. After work, you test a gadget meant to improve leisure. The next day, someone adopts your favourite discovery and you instantly switch passions. You're the only person who regards success as a reason to abandon something.","You speak about the future as though you have its official programme. In love, you prefer an intellectual exchange to a traditional dinner. To relax, you test a method nobody has tried. The only truly stable element in all this is your conviction that you're ahead of everyone.","Your creativity turns the office coffee machine into a civilisation project. You need space to love and gadgets to rest. Every new fashion stops interesting you once it reaches other people. Your mind is a permanent exhibition where you remove the artwork on opening day."]},"pisces":{"classic":{"career":["Your imagination may reveal possibilities that overly rigid approaches overlook.","An intuition deserves careful exploration before becoming a shared decision.","The sensitivity you bring to conversations helps you better understand a team's expectations.","When several ideas meet, choosing one practical first step can bring your creativity to life.","Your ability to sense the atmosphere helps you approach situations delicately.","Behind your daydreaming sometimes lies an unusual talent for connecting distant elements.","At work, setting clear boundaries preserves your availability for the projects that matter.","Turning inspiration into action requires giving it a little time and structure."],"love":["Your sensitivity allows you to welcome the nuances of conversation with a great deal of heart.","A discreet gesture can say as much as a grand romantic declaration.","The tenderness you give becomes richer when paired with attention to your own needs.","When your imagination runs ahead, returning to the actual words spoken can clarify your impressions.","Your emotional generosity invites connections where everyone feels free to be themselves.","Behind your dreams of harmony, you can discover the beauty of simple, sincere relationships.","Within a close connection, trust also grows through questions asked without fear.","Welcoming another person's feelings doesn't mean having to find a solution to them."],"wellbeing":["Your sensitivity appreciates quiet places where thoughts can settle without pressure.","Gentle music or a moment of silence can help you reconnect with your own pace.","Daydreaming has a place in the day when it also leaves room to savour the present.","When demands multiply, a simple break can help you find your own space again.","Your fertile imagination can draw nourishment from a notebook, a walk or a familiar landscape.","Behind your attentiveness to others, give some time to what brings you pleasure too.","As the day unfolds, a warm conversation may provide pleasant grounding.","Respecting your need for rest takes nothing away from your generosity."],"wisdom":["Your sensitivity is a strength when it also respects your boundaries.","A dream grows deeper when it meets a practical gesture.","Gentleness doesn't mean carrying everyone's worries.","Every feeling deserves a hearing, not necessarily an entire story.","Intuition becomes clearer when it accepts a few questions.","Offering your presence doesn't mean solving every difficulty.","Imagination opens doors; reality shows you where to step.","Nothing tender requires forgetting yourself for others."],"roast":["Your imagination can turn an ordinary conversation into a scenario far more complex than the facts.","Even a small request for help sometimes makes you put your own needs aside.","Daydreams accompany you so often that practical tasks are left waiting for your return.","When an emotion passes through you, you sometimes give it all the available space.","Your desire to understand everyone can make you excuse clumsy behaviour too readily.","Behind your beautiful intuitions, a few details occasionally deserve checking.","When making a simple choice, your imagination presents a vast range of possibilities.","Following a conversation becomes difficult once your mind has set off on a story of its own."]},"funny":{"career":["Your creativity turns an office memo into the first chapter of a novel. The memo only asked everyone to close the windows.","The meeting is covering three topics. You've just returned from a fourth: the one nobody announced but your intuition finds fascinating.","Kindness makes you help three colleagues at once. Your own file sends a timid reminder.","When you gaze dreamily at your screen, perhaps you're planning a brilliant project. Or inventing the name of a kingdom.","Your intuition detects a shift in mood. It was a colleague opening a tin of biscuits.","Behind your wish to fix everything, you've agreed to reorganise someone's desk without them ever asking.","An instruction inspires a creative solution, then another, then a sketch on a napkin. The deadline for handing in the document has vanished from the picture.","You sense the best solution before the debate even begins. Your colleagues would also appreciate hearing the steps in between.","Your intuition whispers a solution during the meeting. You write it on loose paper, which instantly joins the collection of unfindable ideas.","The calendar shows a firm deadline. You see it mainly as an invitation to work in a creative atmosphere.","You prepare a presentation with beautiful drawings and thoughtful explanations. Someone asks the only terrifying question: 'What do we do first?'","A progress meeting inspires a metaphor about ocean currents. The manager writes 'fluid ideas' in the deliverables column."],"love":["Your romantic mind writes an entire film from a simple 'hello'. The person was looking for the right bus stop.","A song on the radio reminds you of a precious memory. You've already given it a complete soundtrack.","Your sensitivity notices an unusual full stop in a message. You launch an investigation into punctuation.","When someone lends you an umbrella, you're so touched that you consider writing them a poem.","Your overflowing tenderness extends even to balcony plants. You congratulate them when they seem happy.","Behind your dreamy gaze, a magnificent romantic scene is unfolding. In reality, the waiter is waiting for your order.","At your first dinner together, one tender glance is enough to launch a grand story in your mind, complete with opening credits. The other person is still reading the starters.","Sharing a walk is enough for you to invent a story about every lit-up window in the neighbourhood.","An exchanged glance at a café becomes a three-act story in your mind. Act one ends before the drinks arrive.","You've mentally chosen the music for a first date nobody has suggested yet. The conductor is waiting for invitations.","A heart printed on a wrapper inspires a romantic scene. The manufacturer was just trying to sell biscuits.","You recount your latest meeting as an epic tale. The other person mostly remembers the bus journey."],"wellbeing":["Your mind goes on holiday while you look for your slippers. The slippers remain remarkably patient.","You settle beside a stream and let the sound of water set the pace of your break. Your watch can't decide which category to put the moment in.","Your relaxation playlist begins with waves, moves on to rain and ends with a fountain. The bathroom is feeling competitive.","You listen to the same peaceful tune for an hour. By the end, you know more about the silences between notes than the song itself.","Your desire to care for others makes you offer a cushion to an armchair. The armchair looked comfortable enough.","Behind your tranquillity lies an inner epic. You've crossed three kingdoms between two sips of water.","At bedtime, you remember a touching scene from a cartoon. Your pillow anticipates a long evening.","Returning to the present sometimes requires a signpost. It's beside your keys, which you've been looking for for ten minutes.","You open the window to listen to rain. Your phone offers an app that imitates precisely what you can already hear.","Your quiet moment begins with a gentle song and ends with your feet in water. The rug accepts the decision reluctantly.","A fountain in the park is enough to give you a little escape. The duck nearby appears to have booked the same show.","You close your eyes to a peaceful melody. The world can wait until the next note."],"wisdom":["Your intuition can be brilliant. It can also mistake a mysterious sign for the arrow to the toilets.","Not every everyday sign is a message. Some signs simply point to the exit.","The cosmos may inspire you; you needn't attribute every refrigerator noise to it.","Not every mysterious glance announces an extraordinary story.","Your intuition could occasionally consult your inbox.","Offering comfort doesn't mean adopting the sad toaster.","Inspiration travels freely; your appointment still has a fixed time.","There's no proof the cloud sent you a personal message.","Intuition is a curious guide; it doesn't always replace the arrows on the path.","A sign from the heavens isn't an invitation to interrogate every signpost personally.","Your instincts sometimes guess correctly. They should also learn to read the small print.","Chance has many talents. Don't put it in charge of answering every question today."],"roast":["You lost your keys while helping three people find theirs. Your keyring is considering starting a support service.","A slightly drooping plant inspires a supportive conversation. It only needed sunlight.","Daydreaming carries you so far that your tea eventually gets its own abandonment story.","When you enter a bookshop, you become attached to the characters before even opening the books.","You offered to help someone carrying an empty bag. They went home with a recommended route and your phone number.","You went to fetch a pen and returned with water for one colleague, advice for another and no idea where the pen is.","At the slightest glance on the Tube, you invent a past, a secret and a final twist. The person was looking at the route map.","You're searching everywhere for your glasses, which are sitting on your desk. Meanwhile, you've comforted someone who wasn't upset.","You find a friend's umbrella, then lose your own while bringing it back. The objects have started playing musical chairs.","You tried to console a neighbour who was just concentrating on a crossword. They ended up giving you a clue to solve.","You leave the room to bring someone a mug. You return with three napkins, two storage ideas and no mug.","A friend says 'it'll be fine'. You're already assembling a support team, though they were talking about building a shelf."]},"piquant":{"career":["Your professional intuition has replaced the instructions with a pencil-drawn arrow. It points towards the creative workshop, not the project.","A simple remark inspires twelve interpretations. The minutes have been filed under fiction.","Kindness makes you handle the entire team's problems. Your own work has officially changed owners.","Someone needs a precise decision. You return with a poetic idea and three shades of colour. The decision has left the agenda.","Your instincts prompt you to present a good idea before checking the facts. The graph applauds, then changes its figures.","Your creative genius comes up with ten approaches to a simple task. The calendar now has an observer's seat but no voting rights.","At the office, you collect everyone's worries like abandoned objects. Lost Property has rejected your application.","Turning a dream into a schedule seems reductive. The calendar would merely like to know whether you're coming on Monday.","Your intuition just approved a project without reading the notes. The tracking sheet filed it under 'inspiration, evidence pending'.","You answer a scheduling question with an artistic diagram. The date is represented by an abstract wave.","Internal memo: your creativity has produced fourteen approaches. Not one includes the address of the folder to submit.","You arrive late with a brilliant idea about organising time. The clock has chosen not to attend your lecture."],"love":["Your romantic imagination turns a two-second glance into an eight-season saga. The main extra doesn't know filming has begun.","A short reply prompts you to write a catastrophe screenplay, then its happy sequel. The message just said 'OK'.","Tenderness makes you emotionally adopt every kind person. Even the delivery driver ends up in your inner novel.","When someone smiles politely, your imagination starts a trailer. The smile demands image rights.","A mere full stop at the end of a message becomes a sign of grand romantic destiny. The full stop thought it was just ending a sentence.","Behind your promises of simple love hides a team of scriptwriters. They've planned three twists for Tuesday.","At the slightest silence, you write an entire dialogue in your head. The other person was just making pasta.","Sharing your feelings is your speciality: you send such a nuanced message that it needs a contents page. The full stop got lost.","A glance exchanged in a lift becomes a romantic mural in your mind. The other person only wanted the fourth floor.","You turn a simple 'see you soon' into a promise worthy of a grand finale. The original exchange fitted on a bus ticket.","Your heart has already written the music, scenery and ending. The other person hasn't received an invitation to act one.","You see a romantic symbol in a badly placed mug. The coffee had simply spilled, with no narrative intention."],"wellbeing":["You play wave sounds to unwind. Three hours later, you know the soundtrack to every sea, but no longer where the pause button is.","You settle by the water for peace. You stay so long the ducks think you're part of the scenery.","Your relaxation playlist has eight watery soundscapes. By the ninth, your speaker thinks it's responsible for the tides.","When seeking calm, you begin analysing the clouds' moods. The sky blocks your notifications.","Your inner refuge features a waterfall, soft music and a secret entrance. The real sitting room is still waiting for you to return to your chair.","Behind your peaceful expression, an emotional tribunal is trying a conversation from Tuesday. Tuesday has been acquitted in absentia.","At bedtime, your mind starts the extended edition of all your touching memories. The pillow files a complaint.","You let a melody carry you away for so long that the next song has booked an appointment just to begin.","Your rain-sounds app has thirty settings. You're still searching for the precise sound of a Tuesday without obligations.","You installed a desk fountain to create a sanctuary. It now makes more noise than a residents' association meeting.","Your tranquillity forecast: a few soft clouds and an endless playlist. The stop button is hiding under a cushion.","You seek calm in the murmur of a stream. The stream simply refuses to become your private radio station."],"wisdom":["Your intuition reads novels in three-word messages.","A sign from the universe deserves a glance. A green pedestrian light isn't a personal revelation.","Compassion doesn't oblige you to defend the cushion's rights.","Not every silence hides a tragedy: sometimes someone's eating.","Your daydreaming owns a cinema; reality is waiting for its ticket.","Offering help to the whole universe leaves your diary without an owner.","Your intuition has a magnificent aerial. It also receives destiny's advertising messages.","Nothing is more epic than your interpretation of a simple 'thank you'.","Your instincts decipher secret messages everywhere. The cosmos doesn't actually run a registered-mail service.","A coincidence isn't an official declaration from infinity. Your notebook has already booked the press conference.","You treat every cloud as a personal signal. The sky also broadcasts programmes without an intended recipient.","Your intuition thinks it subscribes to the universe's newspaper. Sometimes it mistakes the weather section for the editorial."],"roast":["You offered to cheer up a perfectly content cactus. The cactus replied with an extremely clear silence.","A tear during a cartoon seems perfectly reasonable. You're now preparing an apology for the supporting character.","Compassion drives you to help everyone, even a misplaced cushion. The cushion demands independence.","Someone merely wants a tissue. You offer a consoling speech, a support plan and your last umbrella.","Your sensitivity makes you collect memories nobody can date. A restaurant napkin has just been granted historical status.","Behind your faraway gaze stands an inner film director shooting without permission. Everyday life is preparing an appeal.","At the slightest sigh, you investigate the emotions in the room. The chair confesses only to creaking.","You misplaced your diary while helping a neighbour organise theirs. Today's appointment is now filed under 'hazy memories'.","You found a neighbour's dog, then lost your own bag trying to offer it water. Your good deed forgot to plan a lost-property office.","Someone announces they can assemble their furniture alone. You arrive with encouragement, spare screws and a support ceremony.","Breaking news: you've lent your charger to someone who didn't need one. Your phone watches at one per cent.","You offer to solve the whole neighbourhood's little problems. Your own unopened post has decided to move out."]},"roastMy":["Pisces, a message without an emoji becomes the start of a drama in several acts. You reread the punctuation, invent an explanation and already choose the music for reconciliation. The other person simply had their hands full. Your screenplay has just lost its funding.","Your imagination doesn't distinguish a fact from a trailer. Someone looks at you on the bus and you invent a whole story. They ask for the time. You immediately rewrite the ending.","You want to rescue everyone, including people who never asked for help. You offer emotional support to a slightly leaning plant. It straightens when you open the window. You announce a victory for your empathy.","Pisces, you live fictional stories so intensely that your sofa knows every character in your programmes. You defend a misunderstood villain, then comfort an imaginary hero. The sofa hasn't seen the episode. You give it a forty-minute recap.","You misplace your keys, your mug and sometimes the reason you went somewhere. You search everywhere while inventing a wonderful explanation. The keys were in your pocket. You decide fate had hidden them there.","Your intuition is always ready to interpret the slightest nuance. A colleague writes 'thanks' instead of 'thanks very much'. You mentally convene a crisis team. They were simply in a hurry to catch their train.","You love memories so much that a bus ticket becomes a sentimental relic. Every object has a story, a mood and an approximate date. You refuse to throw away an old scrap of paper. The paper doesn't even remember you.","Pisces, you promise to rest, then someone mentions a tiny problem. You become adviser, mediator and organiser of solutions. They only wanted to talk about their umbrella. The umbrella now has a personal development plan.","Your mind can leave a conversation without warning and go off to build an imaginary city. You return with a poetic idea, an emotion and no answer to the original question. Others ask what you'd like to drink. You tell the story of a fountain.","You can give enormous significance to a passing cloud. You watch it, imagine its journey and wonder whether it's carrying a message. The cloud moves on without answering. Your celestial interpretation service opens an investigation anyway.","Pisces, your creativity turns a work instruction into a poetic stroll. In love, a simple smile opens an entire novel in your mind. You find peace in the sound of water, then offer to comfort a perfectly happy plant. It thanks you by continuing to be a plant.","You enter a meeting with an intuition and leave with eight ideas that fit into no category. A tender message inspires a sweeping film scene. A gentle song absorbs you for hours. Meanwhile, your diary is still looking for the person supposed to read it.","You offer support with disarming generosity, even to people who never asked for it. You interpret everyday signs with the seriousness of someone searching for stars. Then you forget your mug on the way to the sitting room. The mug had sent no distress signal whatsoever.","At work, your best idea appears just after the subject has ended. In love, you've chosen the song for a story that hasn't begun. To unwind, you listen to waves. Your daily life isn't running late: it's waiting for your soundtrack to finish.","You have a rare talent for turning a detail into a touching story. Then you offer help to three people who were merely doing their shopping. Your favourite refuge is like an inner sea where timetables aren't allowed. The shopping list, however, is still looking for its owners."]}},"events":{"newMoon":{"classic":["The new Moon invites you to set a simple intention and welcome a fresh start without demanding results already.","Under the new Moon, making room for an idea that is still fragile may open a different path.","This new Moon symbolises a blank page: choose what you would like to grow on it, at your own pace."],"funny":["New Moon, fresh start: you've already picked a brand-new notebook for an idea you've had for three years.","The new Moon hands you a blank page. You spend twenty minutes choosing the title font.","New Moon: your good intentions have returned to the office, and they've forgotten their password."],"piquant":["The new Moon suggests starting from scratch. Don't worry, your tried-and-tested method of constant improvisation is ready.","Under the new Moon, you dream of a magnificent fresh start. So far, you've moved three icons on your screen.","The new Moon opens a blank page. Your special talent is copying the same excuses onto it with a new cover."]},"firstQuarter":{"classic":["The first-quarter Moon invites you to turn intentions into action, even if early obstacles call for adjustments.","At the first quarter, taking action can reveal what needs strengthening rather than rushing.","This first-quarter Moon highlights the value of staying the course with flexibility when enthusiasm meets reality."],"funny":["First-quarter Moon: your plans call for action. Your diary suddenly claims it has never met you.","The first-quarter Moon pushes you to act. You've made such a thorough to-do list that it needs its own assistant.","First quarter: you finally take the plunge, only to discover the first step was finding your keys."],"piquant":["The first quarter calls for action. Your strategy resembles flat-pack furniture assembled without instructions: bold confidence, three screws left over.","First-quarter Moon: the sky is inviting you to act, not arrange a meeting with yourself to discuss the concept of acting.","At the first quarter, the first obstacle appears. You stare at it as though the furniture has mounted a personal attack."]},"fullMoon":{"classic":["The full Moon highlights something reaching maturity and invites you to look at your emotions with clarity.","Under the full Moon, what was once subtle may become more prominent. Welcoming that clarity can help you take stock.","The full Moon symbolises a possible culmination: acknowledging how far you've come matters as much as what comes next."],"funny":["Full Moon: your emotions are in high definition. Even a colleague's 'OK' deserves a detailed analysis.","The full Moon illuminates your little truths. You finally discover why the drawer won't shut: six mystery chargers.","Under the full Moon, everything feels more intense, including the suspense over who finished the coffee."],"piquant":["The full Moon shines a light on what you've been avoiding. Your attempt at discretion is as effective as a neon sign in a library.","Full Moon: it's time to take stock. You called it a strategy; the evidence suggests improvisation with a press pack.","The full Moon reveals everything. You hoped for a moment of grace; your decision history has booked a private screening."]},"lastQuarter":{"classic":["The last-quarter Moon invites you to sort out what still deserves your attention and let the rest go.","At the last quarter, reviewing a chapter can lighten commitments that no longer serve much purpose.","This last quarter symbolically favours perspective: simplifying your priorities makes room for what follows."],"funny":["Last quarter: the sky suggests a clear-out. Your inbox immediately requests an extension.","The last quarter encourages letting go. You start by deleting a blurry photo and wait for applause.","Last-quarter Moon: you finally tidy a drawer, then find the list of everything you were supposed to tidy."],"piquant":["The last quarter calls for some inner housekeeping. Your excuses are colour-coded, but your decisions are still under the rug.","Last quarter: time to ditch the clutter. Your collection of 'might come in handy' items already needs a warehouse.","The Moon is waning and inviting simplicity. You're still negotiating with a habit that produces nothing but complications."]},"moonInSign":{"classic":["The Moon crosses your sign and invites you to listen to your emotions without letting them make every decision.","With the Moon in your sign, your intuition may have more room. Take time to distinguish it from passing impressions.","The Moon's passage through your sign symbolically brings your feelings to the fore, giving you a chance to understand them better."],"funny":["The Moon crosses your sign. You sense the mood in a room before realising it's not the room you were looking for.","With the Moon in your sign, your emotions turn up the volume. Even choosing a mug becomes a matter of principle.","The Moon enters your sign: you know something is wrong, then realise it's just the squeaky chair."],"piquant":["The Moon crosses your sign and amplifies your impressions. Your intuition has already written a report without checking a single fact.","With the Moon in your sign, every detail becomes a message. Even the router light seems to be issuing you a secret communiqué.","The Moon visits your sign. Your inner world holds a press conference to announce a tiny inconvenience."]},"sunInSign":{"classic":["The Sun crosses your sign: this period invites you to reflect on what drives you and the momentum you want to give your projects.","Your solar season symbolically puts your journey in the spotlight. Recognising your progress can nurture quieter confidence.","With the Sun in your sign, the energy of personal renewal invites you to balance the wish to shine with your deeper needs."],"funny":["The Sun crosses your sign. You enter a room as though the opening credits should roll; it's only the microwave.","It's your solar season: you've planned a grand personal review but start by choosing a new wallpaper for your phone.","The Sun is in your sign. Your birthday is coming up or has just passed; your calendar wants an opening ceremony."],"piquant":["The Sun crosses your sign and symbolically puts you centre stage. You've already handed out the programme for your own ceremony.","Your solar season inspires a review; your ego has booked an entire hall to present its triumphant graphs.","With the Sun in your sign, you dream of shining. No need to turn every conversation into a lecture entitled 'Me: An Epic'."]},"venusInSign":{"classic":["Venus crosses your sign and invites you to enjoy simple pleasures, graceful gestures and the quality of your exchanges.","With Venus in your sign, an appreciation of beauty can inspire how you live and share your everyday life.","Venus passing through your sign emphasises gentleness and harmony, without forcing anyone closer together."],"funny":["Venus crosses your sign. You light a candle for an elegant evening; it mainly illuminates the pile of laundry waiting to be folded.","Venus is in your sign: you walk into a shop just to browse and leave with a cushion that 'changes the whole atmosphere'.","With Venus visiting, your love of beauty awakens. You spend longer arranging your afternoon snack than eating it."],"piquant":["Venus crosses your sign and flatters your tastes. You're so particular about beauty that even a plastic plant has to pass a job interview.","Venus is in your sign. You insist on perfect harmony; shame your priorities are stuck in a shared flat.","With Venus in your sign, you look for charm everywhere. Even your keyring needs a soft-focus photo shoot."]},"marsInSign":{"classic":["Mars crosses your sign: the urge to act may feel stronger. Choosing a direction helps you use that energy wisely.","As Mars moves through your sign, initiative takes on symbolic importance. Patience remains a friend to courage.","Mars in your sign invites you to assert yourself while respecting other people's pace. Momentum works best with control."],"funny":["Mars crosses your sign. You want everything sorted immediately, including the order in which notifications appear on your screen.","With Mars in your sign, you tackle your to-do list like a competition. The pen has called for a referee.","Mars enters your sign: you reply 'on my way' before you've even found out where you're going."],"piquant":["Mars crosses your sign. Your patience now fits inside an envelope, and you've already lost the envelope.","With Mars in your sign, every delay becomes a challenge to your authority. Even the red traffic light refuses to recognise your rank.","Mars in your sign gives you momentum. You charge ahead like a meeting without an agenda: fast, loud and entirely unsure why."]},"jupiterInSign":{"classic":["Jupiter crosses your sign and invites you to broaden your horizons. Confidence can grow when paired with good judgement.","Jupiter passing through your sign symbolises expansion: explore new possibilities without assuming success.","Jupiter in your sign encourages generous ambitions. A sense of proportion may give them greater reach."],"funny":["Jupiter crosses your sign. You're considering learning three languages, launching a project and tidying the cellar before Sunday.","Jupiter is in your sign: your ideas grow. The whiteboard wants a second wall.","With Jupiter in your sign, you think big. Even your shopping list has a 'strategic vision' section."],"piquant":["Jupiter crosses your sign and expands your ambitions. Your sense of proportion has bought a one-way ticket to another galaxy.","Jupiter in your sign boosts your confidence. You present a two-line draft as the master plan for an empire.","With Jupiter in your sign, anything seems possible. Even your procrastination is planning international expansion."]},"saturnInSign":{"classic":["Saturn crosses your sign and invites you to build methodically. Steady effort may provide a firmer foundation for your choices.","Saturn passing through your sign emphasises chosen responsibilities and the value of lasting commitment.","With Saturn in your sign, clarifying your boundaries may encourage calm maturity without demanding perfection."],"funny":["Saturn crosses your sign. You open a binder to organise your life; it already contains an inventory of all your other binders.","With Saturn in your sign, responsibilities settle in. Even your calendar insists on a signature under every appointment.","Saturn is in your sign. You proudly follow your rules until you discover nobody knows rule number seven."],"piquant":["Saturn crosses your sign: discipline takes the stage. Your timetable now has more authority than you do.","Saturn in your sign calls for consistency. You've written a twelve-page code of discipline to avoid starting the first task.","Saturn crosses your sign. You sometimes confuse maturity with quality control on an ordinary walk."]},"venusRx":{"classic":["Venus retrograde invites you to reconsider what moves you, how tastes change and the value you place on relationships.","Venus's apparent backward motion symbolically evokes the return of emotional memories, without confusing them with the present.","When Venus appears to move backwards, stepping back from your desires may reveal pleasures more closely aligned with your values."],"funny":["Venus retrograde: an old playlist resurfaces and suddenly every song wants written minutes of your past decisions.","Venus retrograde sends you back through your old favourites. You discover a home decoration you swore you hated.","During Venus retrograde, you reread an old message draft and thank your phone for never sending it."],"piquant":["Venus retrograde brings yesterday's tastes back. You call it nostalgia; your search history calls it evidence.","Venus retrograde invites you to revise your standards. Your list of requirements already resembles the house rules of an empty palace.","Venus retrograde puts the past back in the shop window. You rush over as though bad ideas were on special offer."]},"marsRx":{"classic":["Mars retrograde suggests rethinking how you use your energy. A thoughtful detour may serve you better than forcing action.","When Mars appears to move backwards, slowed momentum offers a chance to distinguish genuine urgency from impatience.","Mars's apparent backward motion invites you to adjust your goals and find a more measured way to act."],"funny":["Mars retrograde: you press the lift button three times. The lift still hasn't read your schedule.","Mars retrograde slows your momentum. You decide to chase after your ideas; they call for a coordination break.","Mars retrograde: even the printer seems to think carefully about every page. You're preparing it a motivational speech."],"piquant":["Mars retrograde slows the pace. Your strategy is to push harder on a door clearly marked 'PULL'.","During Mars retrograde, impatience takes the wheel. Shame your sense of direction stayed at home.","Mars retrograde invites you to rethink the plan. You insist on speeding up, like a conductor scolding the metronome for keeping time."]},"jupiterRx":{"classic":["Jupiter retrograde invites you to measure ambitions against what truly matters. Growth can happen inwardly too.","When Jupiter appears to move backwards, revisiting a project may reveal resources less obvious than immediate results.","Jupiter's apparent retrograde motion symbolically favours reflection on your beliefs and plans for expansion."],"funny":["Jupiter retrograde: your grand expansion project becomes a thorough tour of forgotten folders. There's even one marked 'sort later'.","Jupiter retrograde invites you to explore your inner world. You open a journal and find an abandoned plan to tidy the house.","During Jupiter retrograde, you reassess your goals. The 'conquer the world' project finally loses its top priority."],"piquant":["Jupiter retrograde scales down the grand spectacle. Your ambition was an airship; a closer inspection found the string holding it down.","Jupiter retrograde says think before you grow. Your ego has already ordered a neon sign for a project that doesn't exist yet.","Jupiter retrograde brings plans back down to earth. Your monumental scheme was on a napkin, and even the napkin had reservations."]},"saturnRx":{"classic":["Saturn retrograde suggests reviewing the rules you follow. Some support your path; others may need changing.","When Saturn appears to move backwards, the meaning behind your commitments may matter more than simply collecting them.","Saturn's apparent backward motion invites you to distinguish chosen responsibility from obligations maintained out of habit."],"funny":["Saturn retrograde: you reread your own rules and find a clause banning fun until absolutely everything is finished.","Saturn retrograde invites you to review commitments. You rediscover a solemn promise to clean your keyboard every Tuesday.","During Saturn retrograde, you audit your self-discipline. Your tracking spreadsheet wants a holiday of its own."],"piquant":["Saturn retrograde puts your rules under review. You've built a fortress of tiny instructions and lost the exit plan.","Saturn retrograde asks why you obey your own rules. Your rulebook requires written permission before answering.","Saturn retrograde questions your commitments. You collect responsibilities like trophies, then wonder why the shelf is so heavy."]},"eclipseSolar":{"classic":["A solar eclipse is approaching: tradition sees it as a symbol of one cycle closing and a chance to begin again.","As the solar eclipse approaches, a change of perspective may invite you to question an old habit.","The coming solar eclipse symbolically evokes a transition. Welcoming the unexpected may open a new path."],"funny":["A solar eclipse is approaching. You're preparing a major change too: moving the sofa fifteen centimetres.","The solar eclipse is coming soon: the universe is preparing a rare event, and you're still looking for the remote control.","A solar eclipse is on the horizon. You solemnly announce a new chapter; episode one involves finding your socks."],"piquant":["The solar eclipse approaches and suggests a turning point. You plan to change your life while keeping exactly the same habits: bold concept.","A solar eclipse is coming. Your renewal plan is so vague that even a draft of a draft seems overly specific.","The solar eclipse reminds us the scenery can change. You ask for a grand sign while ignoring the small obvious things for weeks."]},"eclipseLunar":{"classic":["A lunar eclipse is approaching and symbolises a chapter worth examining more clearly, without presuming its outcome.","As the lunar eclipse approaches, old emotions may call to be acknowledged and understood.","The coming lunar eclipse symbolically invites you to close a chapter gently and make room for new bearings."],"funny":["The lunar eclipse is approaching. You decide to turn the page but first spend an hour choosing the bookmark.","A lunar eclipse is on the horizon: your emotions prepare their grand unpacking. You're still searching for the box.","As the lunar eclipse approaches, you reflect on memories. The drawer of old receipts refuses to testify."],"piquant":["The lunar eclipse approaches and invites you to close a chapter. You would rather write a fifty-page appendix to get the last word.","A lunar eclipse is coming. Your unspoken thoughts have booked a hall, badges and a conference; your honesty isn't invited.","The lunar eclipse symbolically illuminates your emotions. Your talent is building them a maze, then selling the map."]},"meteors":{"classic":["The {shower} sweep across the sky, reminding you how a moment of attention can hold so much wonder.","As the {shower} pass overhead, looking up at the night sky invites you to slow down and appreciate the beauty of a moment.","The {shower} briefly light up the night. Their passage may awaken simple wishes without promising they will come true."],"funny":["The {shower} pass across the sky. You prepare a magnificent wish, then forget the important bit when it's time to make it.","To watch the {shower}, you settle in comfortably. Your neighbour picks that exact moment to test the garden lights.","The {shower} put on a night-time show. You look for a shooting star, but your weather app wants five updates."],"piquant":["The {shower} cross the night. Even the stars can gather momentum; you're still negotiating with the 'later' button.","The {shower} streak across the sky. Your wishes are so detailed they'd need a committee to review them.","During the {shower}, you wait for a spectacular sign. The sky offers meteors; you'd rather check a pointless notification."]}}});
